26-07-14\",\n  \"storyKey\": \"5-2-approve-skill-authority-expansion\",\n  \"status\": \"local-contract-not-tenant-verified\",\n  \"purpose\": \"Prove Skill authority expansion approval and denial locally: one new skill install (CSK-LOCAL-MEETING-DIGEST-001) proposes a before authority set (manual_only, no data/tool/external access) and an after authority set adding data access (outlook.calendar.read, dataverse.com_councilworkitem.read) and tool use (email.send) plus an external action, which FR25/FR13 require to be approval-gated; a human (Doug) approval receipt CR-LOCAL-SKILL-APPROVE-001 carries authority basis, rationale, before/after authority sets, and evidence refs, and activation is gated to that receipt (temporal + receipt-chain, not a flag) with the live skill row mutation deferred to Epic 2. A second new skill install (CSK-LOCAL-FABRIC-PUBLISHER-001) proposes a broader expansion (Dataverse write, two Fabric external actions, approved_automatic authority) and is denied by receipt CR-LOCAL-SKILL-DENY-001 (verb policy_denied, result rejected); the skill stays inactive (candidate) constrained to its before authority set with the denial rationale visible for future review. Before/after authority sets differ exactly by the declared delta; receipts here are local contract evidence only and every live mutation stays receipt-gated to Epic 2.\",\n  \"guards\": {\n    \"noTenantWrites\": true,\n    \"noOutboundAction\": true,\n    \"noApprovalExecution\": true,\n    \"requiresExplicitHumanApprovalForExecution\": true,\n    \"sourceRecordsRemainSeparate\": true,\n    \"meaningGraphDoesNotOwnWorkflowState\": true,\n    \"dataverseRowsNotUsedAsCouncilIdentity\": true,\n    \"receiptsAreLocalContractEvidenceOnly\": true,\n    \"receiptsAreAppendOnlyCorrectionsAreNewReceipts\": true,\n    \"authorityExpansionRequiresExplicitApprovalReceipt\": true,\n    \"activationStrictlyFollowsApprovalReceipt\": true,\n    \"denialConstrainsSkillToBeforeAuthority\": true,\n    \"denial