{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1784297639546,"sessionID":"ses_08f93ebc0ffe1KnUJW6Wj62UYD","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_ae64c11fd20f4bd0bd34f326","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# notes.md — Story 5.5 worker log\n\n## Result\n**No code change required.** Both deliverable files already exist, are committed,\nand pass the ringer-check on a clean tree. I verified them against the story spec\nand the hardening bar; nothing needed adding.\n\n## Files I own (ringer-owned)\n- `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/dataverse-readiness-slice.json` (storyKey\n  `5-5-validate-dataverse-mvp-operational-store-readiness`)\n- `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/dataverse-readiness-slice-validate.ps1`\n\nBoth were left unmodified; `git status` was clean before and after this run.\n\n## Verification (the ringer-check, run verbatim)\n```\nexport DOTNET_ROOT=$HOME/.dotnet; export PATH=$HOME/.dotnet:$HOME/.dotnet/tools:$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH; \\\n  pwsh -File _bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/dataverse-readiness-slice-validate.ps1\n```\nOutput ends with `DATAVERSE_READINESS_SLICE_VALIDATE_OK`, exit 0. Summary line:\npreflight commands 3, pending approvals 2, story-scoped write-policy entries 8,\nrollback/audit boundaries 3, referenced ids 11, deferred writes 4.\n\n## Corrupted-copy test (hardening bar)\nCopied the slice to `/tmp/opencode/corrupted-readiness.json`, flipped\n`guards.writeScriptsDisabled` to `false` and injected a fabricated UUID into\n`preflightContract.expectedCommands[pac env who].evidenceShape.environmentId`.\nRe-ran the validator with `-ReadinessSlicePath` pointing at the corrupted copy.\nResult: exit 1 with three issues (strict-bool guard, deferred-marker mismatch,\nfabricated-tenant-id tripwire). The validator FAILs on corruption as required.\n\n## Spec coverage checklist (read against the story spec)\n- Preflight CONTRACT (`pac auth who`, `pac env who`, `pac env list-settings`):\n  every evidenceShape field is the literal `VERIFY IN TENANT`,\n  `evidenceState: deferred-to-tenant`, `noLivePacCallPerformed: true`.\n  `guards.writeScriptsDisabled` strict true; `guards.noLivePacCallInThisSlice` true.\n- No fabricated tenant values: validator tripwire scans raw slice text against\n  manifest `target.environmentId/organizationId/environmentUrl/environmentUniqueName`.\n- Pending approvals: `dataverseSandboxWrites` and `publisherPrefix` are PENDING,\n  `requiredApprover: Doug`, `backingReceiptId: null`. No `com_receipt_id` field\n  anywhere in the slice. Cross-checked against `tenant-decision-packet.json`.\n- Dry-run schema manifest: `manifestRef` = committed manifest, version pinned to\n  manifest's `manifestVersion`, `fullShapeNotForcedUpfront: true`.\n- Story-scoped write policy: 8 non-empty entries (1-1, 1-3, 1-5, 2-1, 2-3, 3-1,\n  4-1, 4-4). Every table/column/relationship-table is asserted to exist in the\n  manifest; every storyKey is asserted to be a real epic story (harvested from\n  `sprint-status.yaml` + sibling slice storyKeys).\n- Rollback/audit boundaries: 3 entries, one per planned write scope\n  (`state-change-mutation`, `source-drift-supersession`, `schema-apply`).\n  Bidirectional `writeScopeKey` ↔ boundary coverage is derived, not counted.\n- Cross-slice ID harvest: validator harvests CWI/CR/CSR ids from\n  manual/outlook/proposed-work-item/zero-multi-item/source-drift +\n  work-item-shell/approval/receipt-state/memory slices + demo evidence.\n  This slice mints no new CWI/CR/CSR ids; all referenced ids must resolve and\n  idType prefix must match membership; `sourceSlice` must name the file the id\n  actually lives in (bound attribution, not prose).\n- `acceptanceMapping` covers AC1 (preflight + approvals) and AC2 (dry-run\n  manifest + boundaries), each with `localEvidence` and `tenantEvidenceRequired`.\n- Final OK token `DATAVERSE_READINESS_SLICE_VALIDATE_OK`, exit 0 on success,\n  issue list + exit 1 on any failure.\n\n## Conventions I read for guidance\n- `dataverse-mvp-schema-manifest.json` — authoritative vocabulary; the slice's\n  story-scoped policy tables/columns all resolve against it.\n- `source-drift-supersession-slice-validate.ps1` — the gold-standard pair\n  (story 1-5) I mirrored structure from: wrapped JSON loads, strict booleans,\n  TryParse-free numeric/string guards via `Test-StrictBooleanTrue` /\n  `Test-HasNonEmptyField`, ISO 8601 run id, `$PSScriptRoot`-relative defaults,\n  cross-slice id harvest distinguishing MINTED vs REFERENCED, final\n  `<NAME>_SLICE_VALIDATE_OK` token.\n- Sibling slices listed in the spec, plus the additional epic-2/3/4 slices the\n  validator pulls in for the broader id universe.\n\n## Assumptions / follow-ups\n- **Assumption:** the existing committed files are the intended baseline for\n  this worktree and I should not churn them. The validator passes and the\n  corrupted-copy test fails, so the story's hardening bar is already met. If\n  the integrator expects a fresh diff, they can re-trigger the worker; the\n  artifact set is complete and self-consistent as-is.\n- **No follow-up code change** is required for this story. Suite wiring into\n  `council-mvp-local-validate.ps1` is explicitly out of scope (the hard rules say\n  not to edit it).\n","filePath":"/home/doug/.ringer/work/bmad-hybrid/5-5-validate-dataverse-mvp-operational-store-readiness/notes.md"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/home/doug/.ringer/work/bmad-hybrid/5-5-validate-dataverse-mvp-operational-store-readiness/notes.md","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"notes.md","time":{"start":1784297639531,"end":1784297639543}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The corrupted slice fails as expected. The story's two deliverable files are complete, correct, and the validator both passes on the genuine slice and fails on a corrupted copy.\n\nThe work was already done in a prior commit. Since the task says I should \"make the code change the story requires\" and \"leave every change UNCOMMITTED\" — but the files already exist committed and are complete/correct — there is no additional code change to make. I should not modify the files unnecessarily. I'll document this state in notes.md.\n\nWait - I should double-check the spec for any missing requirement. Let me re-read the spec sections:\n\n1. \"ringer-owned: _bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/dataverse-readiness-slice.json;_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/dataverse-readiness-slice-validate.ps1\" - both exist\n2. \"ringer-expect: same\" - both exist  \n3. \"ringer-check: export DOTNET_ROOT=...; pwsh -File ...dataverse-readiness-slice-validate.ps1\" - passes with OK token\n4. Slice proves the 3 required things - all present\n5. Validator asserts all required things - all present\n6. Hardening bar - corrupted slice verified to FAIL\n7. acceptanceMapping covers AC1 and AC2 - present\n\nEverything checks out. The story was already implemented and review-hardened in commit 068ce3b / e1ba0e3. There's no further work needed. I'll write the notes.md documenting what I checked and the verification results.\n\nLet me check that no required field is missing. Looking at the slice for cross-slice uniqueness - the validator already does cross-slice id harvests. The spec mentions cross-slice collision tripwires against sibling slices (1-1..1-5) - the validator harvests from manual, outlook, proposed-work-item, zero-multi-item, source-drift, plus more. Good.\n\nOne thing to double check - story spec says \"cross-slice ID-collision tripwires against the sibling slices (1-1..1-5)\". The validator harvests from those plus later slices. The slice mints no new ids (it references existing ones), so no collision is possible. The validator correctly handles this with the \"mintedCandidates\" check.\n\nEverything is complete. Let me write notes.md and finish.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_f706ceebe001BTtOsNQBDouep3","sessionID":"ses_08f93ebc0ffe1