{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1784297673531,"sessionID":"ses_08f93ebfcffe5crM36mCTtmFiF","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_8feb687c459a4ec69c8823c3","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"export DOTNET_ROOT=$HOME/.dotnet; export PATH=$HOME/.dotnet:$HOME/.dotnet/tools:$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH\ncp _bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/skill-authority-expansion-slice.json /tmp/skill-slice-backup.json\n# Corrupt: flip the approval result to \"rejected\" so the approval-receipt result check must FAIL\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,io\np=\"_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/skill-authority-expansion-slice.json\"\nd=json.load(open(p))\nfor r in d[\"expansionRun\"][\"receipts\"]:\n    if r[\"com_receipt_id\"]==\"CR-LOCAL-SKILL-APPROVE-001\":\n        r[\"com_result\"]=\"rejected\"\njson.dump(d,open(p,\"w\"),indent=2)\nprint(\"corrupted approval result -> rejected\")\nPY\npwsh -File _bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/skill-authority-expansion-slice-validate.ps1 2>&1 | tail -15\necho \"EXIT=$?\"\n# restore\ncp /tmp/skill-slice-backup.json _bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/skill-authority-expansion-slice.json\necho \"--- restored; re-verify ---\"\npwsh -File _bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/skill-authority-expansion-slice-validate.ps1 2>&1 | tail -3\necho \"EXIT=$?\"","workdir":"/home/doug/.ringer/work/bmad-hybrid/5-2-approve-skill-authority-expansion"},"output":"corrupted approval result -> rejected\nSkill authority expansion slice validation failed:\n- Receipt CR-LOCAL-SKILL-APPROVE-001 result must be accepted for an approval receipt, found: rejected.\n- Skill CSK-LOCAL-MEETING-DIGEST-001 decisionReceipt must reference a receipt with result accepted, found: rejected.\n- Skill CSK-LOCAL-MEETING-DIGEST-001 activation.gateReceipt must be an approved/accepted receipt, found verb approved result rejected.\nEXIT=0\n--- restored; re-verify ---\nReceipt source links: 2\nDeferred skill updates: 2\nSKILL_AUTHORITY_EXPANSION_SLICE_VALIDATE_OK\nEXIT=0\n","metadata":{"output":"corrupted approval result -> rejected\nSkill authority expansion slice validation failed:\n- Receipt CR-LOCAL-SKILL-APPROVE-001 result must be accepted for an approval receipt, found: rejected.\n- Skill CSK-LOCAL-MEETING-DIGEST-001 decisionReceipt must reference a receipt with result accepted, found: rejected.\n- Skill CSK-LOCAL-MEETING-DIGEST-001 activation.gateReceipt must be an approved/accepted receipt, found verb approved result rejected.\nEXIT=0\n--- restored; re-verify ---\nReceipt source links: 2\nDeferred skill updates: 2\nSKILL_AUTHORITY_EXPANSION_SLICE_VALIDATE_OK\nEXIT=0\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"export DOTNET_ROOT=$HOME/.dotnet; export PATH=$HOME/.dotnet:$HOME/.dotnet/tools:$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH\ncp _bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/skill-authority-expansion-slice.json /tmp/skill-slice-backup.json\n# Corrupt: flip the approval result to \"rejected\" so the approval-receipt result check must FAIL\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,io\np=\"_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/skill-authority-expansion-slice.json\"\nd=json.load(open(p))\nfor r in d[\"expansionRun\"][\"receipts\"]:\n    if r[\"com_receipt_id\"]==\"CR-LOCAL-SKILL-APPROVE-001\":\n        r[\"com_result\"]=\"rejected\"\njson.dump(d,open(p,\"w\"),indent=2)\nprint(\"corrupted approval result -> rejected\")\nPY\npwsh -File _bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/skill-authority-expansion-slice-validate.ps1 2>&1 | tail -15\necho \"EXIT=$?\"\n# restore\ncp /tmp/skill-slice-backup.json _bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/skill-authority-expansion-slice.json\necho \"--- restored; re-verify ---\"\npwsh -File _bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/skill-authority-expansion-slice-validate.ps1 2>&1 | tail -3\necho \"EXIT=$?\"","time":{"start":1784297673521,"end":1784297673526}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"So HEAD (e1ba0e3) and its ancestors already contain the completed, review-hardened slice + validator for story 5-2. The validator passes with the OK token.\n\nThis is the situation: the story is ALREADY fully implemented at the base commit. The Ringer worker is being asked to implement it, but the implementation already exists and passes.\n\nThis is a known scenario in the Ringer workflow — sometimes a \"re-run\" hits a story whose work is already present (e.g., the orchestrator re-routed, or the worktree was created from a commit that already includes the prior completed work). \n\nThe task contract says: \"make the code change the story requires, then write ./notes.md\". The \"code change the story requires\" already exists in the working tree. The Ringer check exports uncommitted changes as a patch. If I make NO changes, the patch is empty.\n\nTwo interpretations:\n1. The work is done; I should verify it passes and write notes.md documenting that the files already exist and pass. But notes.md itself would be an uncommitted change — a patch with just notes.md.\n2. I should re-author the files from scratch to produce a real diff.\n\nGiven the files are already complete, correct, and pass the validator (with the OK token), re-authoring them would be wasteful and risk introducing regressions. The most sensible action: verify the validator passes (done — it does), verify a corrupted copy FAILS (the story requires this check), and write notes.md documenting the state.\n\nBut wait — the story says \"Verify a corrupted slice copy FAILS before finishing.\" This is a deliverable check I should perform. Let me do that to confirm the validator's failure path works.\n\nAlso, the ringer-owned/ringer-expect comments name exactly these two files. The Ringer check expects these files to exist (they do) and the validator to pass (it does).\n\nLet me reconsider: maybe the Ringer harness actually compares the patch against a reference. If the reference patch is \"the files should be created\", and they already exist, my empty patch wouldn't match. But I can't know the reference. \n\nThe pragmatic, correct approach given the constraints:\n1. The two required files exist and the validator passes with the OK token.\n2. Verify corruption FAILS (per story requirement).\n3. Write notes.md (this is the one new uncommitted file I produce) documenting what I did, what I read, the verify command, and assumptions/follow-ups.\n\nActually — re-reading once more: \"make the code change the story requires, then write ./notes.md\". The code change is already present at HEAD. If Ringer's check exports uncommitted changes, and I leave the two owned files as-is (already correct), plus add notes.md, the patch will contain only notes.md. That seems thin but is honest.\n\nHowever, I should consider: maybe I'm SUPPOSED to be at a base commit WITHOUT the files, and the worktree was mis-set-up. But I can't reset that. The files exist and pass. Re-creating identical content would produce no diff (git would see no change). Re-creating with different content would risk breaking the passing validator.\n\nBest path: Treat the existing files as the implementation. Verify the corruption-FAIL check. Add notes.md. Also, I could make a trivial, legitimate improvement to harden the validator or slice if I find a gap — but the validator is already very thorough and passes. Let me check the corruption-FAIL behavior and the \"review swarm's kill list\" requirements to see if there's any genuine gap.\n\nLet me run the corrupted-copy test.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_f706dae54001R0RadwWHRLIIHl","sessionID":"ses_08f93ebfcffe5crM36mCTtmFiF","messageID":"msg_f706d49c00012YXWIaN7y0Kxcv"}}
