uncommitted. But the files are already committed and correct. There's no diff for me to produce. This is the state I was handed.\n\nHowever, I should reconsider whether the existing committed files truly meet ALL the story requirements, or whether there's a subtle gap. Let me cross-check against the story's \"Slice must prove\" and \"Validator must assert\" lists:\n\nSlice must prove:\n1. Two capability evaluations, each considering >=4 Microsoft candidates from the named set, each row capturing tenant gates, permission/DLP, licensing/cost, ALM path, contract gaps, decision, review reference. ✓ (PE-LOCAL-EVAL-001 with 4 rows: Work IQ, Dataverse MCP, Fabric IQ/Graph, Fabric data agents; PE-LOCAL-EVAL-002 with 4 rows: Power Automate, Copilot Studio, Power Apps MCP agent feed, Work IQ). Each row has all 7 fields. ✓\n2. One custom-service proposal citing a specific Microsoft-native gap or tenant constraint, decision recorded (receipt) BEFORE implementation, no implementation artifacts referenced. ✓ (CSP-LOCAL-001 cites PE-LOCAL-EVAL-001-ROW-02 gap; CR-LOCAL-PE-001 decision receipt; implementationArtifactsReferenced empty).\n\nValidator must assert:\n- Candidate coverage (>=4 per evaluation, from named set) ✓\n- Row field completeness ✓\n- Custom proposal's gap citation references a recorded gap in an evaluation row ✓\n- Decision receipts complete and precede any implementation marker ✓\n- Minted-vs-referenced ids ✓\n- Cross-slice uniqueness ✓ (LIVE harvest from $PSScriptRoot)\n\nHardening bar:\n- no self-asserted booleans standing in for proof — the microsoftNativeEvaluatedBeforeCustomSubstrate guard is backed by a derived check (evalReviewTimestamps vs proposal receipt timestamp). ✓\n- no hardcoded-id binding rules — uses general rules over collections. ✓\n- LIVE cross-slice id harvests from $PSScriptRoot distinguishing MINTED vs REFERENCED ✓\n- no conditional/skippable mandatory checks — checks have no-op tripwires (e.g., \"would silently no-op\"). ✓\n- coverage derived not counted — checks candidate membership in universe, row completeness, uniqueness. ✓\n- corrupted slice copy FAILS ✓ (verified)\n\nEverything is satisfied. The deliverables are complete and correct.\n\nNow, the question: should I make any change? The files are already committed and correct. Ringer's check exports my work as a patch. If there's no diff, the export is empty. But ringer-expect just lists the files that must exist; if they exist and pass, the check should pass.\n\nActually, re-reading the worker contract: \"Edit files in place, leave every change UNCOMMITTED, and do NOT run git commit... Ringer's check exports your work as a patch.\" This strongly implies Ringer expects a diff to export. If the files are already committed, there's no diff to export, and the ringer-check would export an empty patch — which might be interpreted as \"no work done.\"\n\nBut the story is genuinely already complete and committed. The honest thing is to recognize the work is already done, and write notes.md documenting the state. Since the ringer-owned files exist and pass, and they're committed (not by me), I shouldn't fabricate edits just to create a diff.\n\nActually, wait. Let me reconsider the scenario. This is a Ringer worker invocation. The worktree is dedicated. The prior commits (068ce1b \"review-hardened validators for 5-1/5-2/5-3/5-5/5-6\") literally say 5-3 was already hardened. So this story was already completed in a prior wave. My job as a re-invoked worker is to confirm the state and write notes.\n\nBut that produces an empty patch. Hmm. The ringer-check command is the validator. If ringer expects a patch but gets empty, that may be fine if the files already exist (the check verifies existence + pass). \n\nActually, let me reconsider — maybe the files were committed by a different process and I'm supposed to re-derive them. But they're already correct and pass. Re-creating identical content would still show no diff vs HEAD.\n\nGiven the constraints, the right action is: confirm the deliverables exist, pass, and are hardened; write notes.md (which IS a new uncommitted file the contract explicitly requires) documenting the state. notes.md will be the uncommitted change Ringer exports, alongside the (already-committed) owned files which pass the check.\n\nLet me write notes.md.\n\nActually — let me double check: is notes.md tracked already? Let me check.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_f706dcdfe001QXAO4u96PVQzch","sessionID":"ses_08f93ebf7ffemEKOLZWmSXnSf7","messageID":"msg_f706d57c5001bzNAy5BY0K42rf"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1784297674575,"sessionID":"ses_08f93ebf7ffemEKOLZWmSXnSf7","part":{"id":"prt_f706dc6ea001jJihwbFrGRU7po","messageID":"msg_f706d57c5001bzNAy5BY0K42rf","sessionID":"ses_08f93ebf7ffemEKOLZWmSXnSf7","type":"text","text":"The deliverables are already complete, hardened, and committed in HEAD (commit 068ce1b \"review-hardened validators for 5-1/5-2/5-3/5-5/5-6\"). Both owned files pass validation and the corrupted-copy tripwire works. My remaining obligation is the `notes.md` output contract. Let me confirm it doesn't already exist and check the sibling-slice cross-references resolve.","time":{"start":1784297670378,"end":1784297674571}}}
