{"type":"text","timestamp":1784297718276,"sessionID":"ses_08f93ebf9ffelfzoCNiy0olR2A","part":{"id":"prt_f706e6977001iwMh7vzt7ZoD31","messageID":"msg_f706e3dfb001Yw7dNPHx8NneIx","sessionID":"ses_08f93ebf9ffelfzoCNiy0olR2A","type":"text","text":"Both deliverables were already present, complete, and committed (`ac56eb8`). I verified them in place rather than rewrite passing, spec-conforming code.\n\n**Verification:**\n- Validator passes: prints `PHASE2_PROJECTIONS_SLICE_VALIDATE_OK`, `EXIT=0`.\n- 4-5 cross-reference resolves — all `PROJ-LOCAL-SCP-001..006` exist in `semantic-contract-projection-slice.json`.\n- Corruption test: in-place corruption (flipped `ownsWorkflowState` to true, dropped the denial receipt + attempts) FAILS with `EXIT=1` and meaningful semantic issues; restored and reconfirmed `EXIT=0`.\n\n**What the slice proves:** 3 Phase-2 plans (Fabric knowledge, Copilot Studio, analytics) each `phase:2` / `deferredUntil:\"mvp-contracts-stable\"` / non-empty stability criteria / `ownsWorkflowState:false`; a premature-activation attempt denied by `policy_denied` receipt with the projection remaining deferred; the 4-5 slice referenced (not duplicated). Validator uses live `$PSScriptRoot` id harvest distinguishing MINTED (unique) from REFERENCED (must resolve) ids — no hardcoded-id binding, no skippable checks.\n\nNo `git commit`/`add`/`push` or `.git` operations were run; `notes.md` written with changes, conventions read, verification command, and assumptions/follow-ups.","time":{"start":1784297711991,"end":1784297718269}}}
