{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1784297731597,"sessionID":"ses_08f93ebfcffe5crM36mCTtmFiF","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_26940366b0cc48d9bf228930","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# notes.md — Story 5.2: Approve Skill Authority Expansion\n\n## Outcome\n\nThe two ringer-owned deliverables already exist at the worktree base (HEAD\n`e1ba0e3`, from the prior \"epic 5: review-hardened validators\" commit) and are\nbyte-identical to HEAD — I left them **unmodified** and **uncommitted**:\n\n- `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/skill-authority-expansion-slice.json`\n- `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/skill-authority-expansion-slice-validate.ps1`\n\nRationale: the slice + validator are already complete, review-hardened, and pass\nthe validator with the `SKILL_AUTHORITY_EXPANSION_SLICE_VALIDATE_OK` token.\nRe-authoring identical content produces no git diff; re-authoring with\nalterations would risk regressing a passing, review-hardened validator against\nthe story's hardening bar. The honest delivery is to confirm the deliverables\nmeet the spec and document the state.\n\n## What I changed\n\n- No changes to the two ringer-owned files (verified byte-identical to HEAD via\n  `git diff --stat` = no diff, and matching sha256sums for both files).\n- Added this `notes.md` (the only uncommitted change in the worktree).\n\n## What I read for conventions\n\n- `dataverse-mvp-schema-manifest.json` — vocabulary source: `com_receiptverb`\n  (approved, policy_denied), `com_receiptresult` (accepted, rejected),\n  `com_actortype` (human), `com_recordstatus` (candidate, active),\n  `com_authorityclass` (manual_only, ask_before_use, approved_automatic),\n  `com_councilreceiptsource.com_evidence_role` (approval, failure_evidence),\n  `com_councilskill` / `com_councilreceipt` required columns.\n- `source-drift-supersession-slice*` (story 1-5 gold standard) — mirrored\n  structure: story-keyed slice, declared guards, wrapped JSON loads, TryParse\n  numeric/confidence checks, strict booleans, ISO-8601 timestamps with explicit\n  UTC offset, `$PSScriptRoot`-relative paths, final `*_SLICE_VALIDATE_OK` token,\n  issue list + `exit 1` on any failure.\n- Sibling slices for cross-slice id collision: `manual-source-record-slice.json`,\n  `outlook-source-reference-slice.json`, `proposed-work-item-extraction-slice.json`,\n  `zero-multi-item-extraction-slice.json` — the validator LIVE-harvests ids\n  from every `*.json` in `$PSScriptRoot` (excluding the slice itself + manifest),\n  distinguishing MINTED ids (must be unique) from REFERENCED ids (must resolve).\n- Existing `state-transition-demo-evidence.json` — reserved demo receipt/work\n  item ids the slice's `CR-LOCAL-SKILL-*` ids must not collide with.\n- The slice's own `acceptanceMapping` (AC 1 approved expansion, AC 2 denied\n  expansion) — validator confirms every cited `CR-LOCAL-SKILL-*`/`CSK-LOCAL-*`/\n  `CSR-*` id resolves to a real slice entity or known cross-slice Source Record.\n\n## Verification command\n\n```\nexport DOTNET_ROOT=$HOME/.dotnet; export PATH=$HOME/.dotnet:$HOME/.dotnet/tools:$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH; pwsh -File _bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/skill-authority-expansion-slice-validate.ps1\n```\n\nResult: prints `SKILL_AUTHORITY_EXPANSION_SLICE_VALIDATE_OK`, exits 0.\n\n### Corruption-FAIL check (story requirement: \"Verify a corrupted slice copy FAILS before finishing\")\n\nBacked up the slice, mutated `CR-LOCAL-SKILL-APPROVE-001.com_result` from\n`accepted` -> `rejected`, re-ran the validator: it printed\n`Skill authority expansion slice validation failed:` with three issues\n(approval-result mismatch, decision-receipt result mismatch, gate-receipt\nverb/result mismatch) and exited non-zero. Restored the backup; re-verified\nthe OK token. The slice is byte-identical to HEAD again (`git diff` clean).\n\n## Slice proves (mapped to spec \"Slice must prove\")\n\n1. **Approved expansion** — `CSK-LOCAL-MEETING-DIGEST-001` install proposes\n   before authority (manual_only, empty) and after authority\n   (ask_before_use + `outlook.calendar.read`, `dataverse.com_councilworkitem.read`,\n   `email.send`, `send_email_on_behalf`); approval receipt\n   `CR-LOCAL-SKILL-APPROVE-001` (verb approved, human Doug, result accepted)\n   carries authority basis, rationale, before/after authority sets, evidence\n   refs; activation is gated to that receipt with a **temporal + receipt-chain**\n   check (`effectiveAt` 2026-07-14T10:30 >= receipt `com_occurred_at`\n   2026-07-14T10:15), not a self-asserted flag.\n2. **Denied expansion** — `CSK-LOCAL-FABRIC-PUBLISHER-001` install seeks\n   approved_automatic + a Dataverse write scope + two Fabric external actions;\n   denial receipt `CR-LOCAL-SKILL-DENY-001` (verb policy_denied, result rejected,\n   failure code `skill_authority_expansion_denied` declared in\n   `failureCodeVocabulary`) leaves the skill `candidate`/`manual_only` with the\n   before authority set; non-empty `denialRationale` stays visible; no\n   activation block; live mutation deferred to Epic 2.\n\n## Validator asserts (mapped to spec \"Validator must assert\")\n\n- Before/after authority sets differ exactly by `declaredDelta` (no extras, no\n  removals, no undeclared additions) via `Test-DeltaExact`.\n- Activation strictly follows an approval receipt — temporal ordering +\n  receipt-chain resolution, plus a tripwire forbidding self-asserted boolean\n  (and string-truthy) approval flags on the activation block.\n- Denied skill status stays non-active; rationale non-empty; effective authority\n  set == before authority set; `policyFlagsTraced` is a subset of the denial\n  receipt's `com_policy_flags` (cross-linked, not parallel).\n- Receipts complete (manifest-required fields + `com_before_state`,\n  `com_after_state`, `com_evidence_refs`, `com_decision_rationale`,\n  `com_policy_flags`); append-only locked strict boolean; confidence in [0,1].\n- Minted vs referenced ids: slice `CSK-LOCAL-*` / `CR-LOCAL-SKILL-*` /\n  `com_idempotency_key` are checked for intra-slice uniqueness AND cross-slice\n  uniqueness via LIVE harvest from every co-located sibling slice; referenced\n  `CSR-*` source records and `com_evidence_refs` must resolve.\n- Coverage derived not counted; no conditional/skippable mandatory checks; no\n  hardcoded-id binding rules (actor binding is `receipt.com_actor_id ==\n  run.actorId` over the collection).\n\n## Assumptions / follow-ups\n\n- **Assumption:** the worktree base already contains the completed, review-\n  hardened deliverables for story 5-2 (committed in `068ce1b` / `ac56eb8`).\n  I treated this as the intended end state and did not re-author the files,\n  since re-authoring identical content yields no diff and altering a passing\n  review-hardened validator risks regressions. If the Ringer harness expected a\n  fresh authoring diff, follow-up: re-create the worktree from a base commit\n  that does NOT contain these two files, then re-run this worker.\n- **Follow-up (integrator, not this story):** wire\n  `skill-authority-expansion-slice-validate.ps1` into\n  `council-mvp-local-validate.ps1` — slice-suite wiring is explicitly the\n  integrator's job per the hard rules (\"Do NOT edit council-mvp-local-validate.ps1\").\n- **Deferred to Epic 2 (per slice):** the live Skill row mutation\n  (candidate -> active, manual_only -> ask_before_use, applying granted\n  authority) and the tenant receipt writes are receipt-gated deferred updates;\n  no live tenant write occurred in this slice.\n","filePath":"/home/doug/.ringer/work/bmad-hybrid/5-2-approve-skill-authority-expansion/notes.md"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/home/doug/.ringer/work/bmad-hybrid/5-2-approve-skill-authority-expansion/notes.md","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"notes.md","time":{"start":1784297731581,"end":1784297731593}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Both owned files are byte-identical to HEAD — I left them unchanged and the working tree is clean for the owned files. The implementation already exists and passes.\n\nNow, the story spec requires me to actually implement the story. The implementation is already present at the base commit. The Ringer contract expects a patch. If I produce zero changes to the owned files (they're already correct), the only uncommitted change will be notes.md.\n\nBut wait — is it acceptable to deliver only notes.md as the patch? The ringer-expect says the two files must exist (they do). The ringer-owned says I own them (I do). The check runs the validator (passes). If the Ringer harness's \"export patch\" is just for inspection, then having the owned files already correct + passing validator + notes.md is a legitimate complete delivery.\n\nHowever, I'm uneasy. Let me reconsider whether the harness actually started me at a base WITHOUT the files and something restored them. No — git ls-files shows them tracked at HEAD, and HEAD is the base. They were committed in prior epic-5 work. This worktree's HEAD already includes the completed story 5-2.\n\nActually, I realize there might be a subtlety: this is a *dedicated worktree* for story 5-2. The orchestrator may have created the worktree from the main branch tip (e1ba0e3) which already contains the merged epic-5 work. So the story is already done on main. The Ringer worker is being asked to redo it — but it's already done.\n\nGiven the constraints and that the deliverables are correct + pass, the honest and correct action is:\n1. Confirm the two owned files are present and the validator passes with the OK token (done).\n2. Confirm corruption FAILS (done).\n3. Write notes.md documenting this exact state, what I read for conventions, the verify command, and the assumption/follow-up that the implementation was already present at the worktree base.\n\nThis is legitimate. Re-authoring identical files would produce no diff (git sees no change). Re-authoring with alterations risks regressing a passing, review-hardened validator. So I'll deliver notes.md as the patch payload, with the owned files left untouched (already correct).\n\nLet me verify the sibling-slice uniqueness requirement is genuinely satisfied by the LIVE harvest (the validator does this, and it passes, so CSK-LOCAL-* and CR-LOCAL-SKILL-* are unique across all co-located slices). Good.\n\nNow write notes.md.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_f706e31fa001G0YQ95SPMLUfxp","sessionID":"ses_08f93ebfcffe5crM36mCTtmFiF","messageID":"msg_f706df764001ainOec82Ifbibd"}}
