eed-v0.2.0)\n068ce1b epic 5: review-hardened validators for 5-1/5-2/5-3/5-5/5-6 (5-4 re-fix pending — orchestrator probe disproved its fabrication scan)\nac56eb8 epic 5 stories 5-1..5-6: slices + validators via Reflex v2 (pre-review)\nf41ff5d Merge reflex/epic-4 into main: epic 4 complete via Reflex v2\n136b369 epic 4: review-hardened validators — epic complete via Reflex v2\n80ad597 epic 4 stories 4-1..4-5: slices + validators via Reflex v2 (pre-review)\nf785110 Merge reflex/epic-3 into main: epic 3 complete via Reflex v2\nbd52a66 epic 3: review-hardened validators — epic complete via Reflex v2\n95066d7 epic 3 stories 3-1..3-3: slices + validators via Reflex v2 (pre-review)\n=== git diff --stat HEAD ===\n notes.md | 150 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n 1 file changed, 150 insertions(+)\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"echo \"=== git status ===\" && git status && echo \"=== git log --oneline -10 ===\" && git log --oneline -10 && echo \"=== git diff --stat HEAD ===\" && git diff --stat HEAD","time":{"start":1784297768368,"end":1784297768375}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Let me analyze this situation. The previous attempt failed because the worker found that the ringer-owned files (`platform-evaluation-slice.json` and `platform-evaluation-slice-validate.ps1`) were already committed in HEAD, so it only wrote `notes.md` and considered the job done. But the check exports work as a patch, and since the owned files were already committed, there's no diff for them — producing an \"empty patch.\"\n\nWait, but the worker wrote notes.md, which should be uncommitted. Let me re-read the failure message.\n\nThe failure says: \"FAIL: worker produced an empty patch for 5-3-record-microsoft-platform-evaluation-evidence (no code changes detected). Fix it.\"\n\nSo the patch is empty. That means notes.md wasn't detected as a change either. Hmm. Or maybe notes.md was already there too? Or maybe the patch only looks at certain files?\n\nActually, looking more carefully — the story says \"You own ONLY the two files named in ringer-owned.\" The ringer-owned files are:\n- `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/platform-evaluation-slice.json`\n- `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/platform-evaluation-slice-validate.ps1`\n\nThe previous worker found these already committed in HEAD and made no changes. It wrote notes.md. But the check says \"empty patch (no code changes detected).\"\n\nSo the issue is: the patch check is looking for changes to the owned files (or any tracked code files), and notes.md alone isn't enough — or notes.md also already exists. Either way, I need to actually produce a change to the owned files.\n\nWait, but if the owned files are already committed and correct... the worker's assumption was that they're already done. But the check wants a non-empty patch. So I need to actually make changes to these files.\n\nLet me think about this differently. The task is to implement the story. The story requires the two deliverable files to exist and be correct. If they're already committed and correct, then there's no work to do — but the check framework expects a patch.\n\nThe instructions say: \"Edit files in place, leave every change UNCOMMITTED.\" So the expectation is that I'm editing files that will show up as uncommitted changes in the worktree. The patch is taken from `git diff` of the worktree (uncommitted changes).\n\nIf the files are already committed in HEAD and I make no edits, the patch is empty. The check fails.\n\nSo I need to actually make edits to the owned files. But if they're already correct and hardened... what do I do?\n\nPossibilities:\n1. The files aren't actually committed — the previous worker was wrong. Let me verify.\n2. The files are committed but need improvements/fixes that the previous worker missed.\n3. The files need some legitimate change.\n\nLet me start by investigating the actual state of the worktree. Let me check:\n- git status\n- git log\n- whether the owned files exist\n- whether they're tracked/committed\n\nActually, the most important thing: the previous worker claimed the files were committed in HEAD and correct, validator passed. But the check failed with \"empty patch.\" \n\nThe key insight: even if the files are committed and pass, the Ringer check needs a PATCH (uncommitted diff). So I must make some edit that produces a diff. But I should make a MEANINGFUL edit, not a spurious one.\n\nHmm, but the story says the files are the deliverable. If they're already committed and correct, maybe the right move is to... not rely on that assumption. Maybe the files are NOT actually committed, or maybe they have issues.\n\nLet me investigate the actual state first before deciding. I should not trust the previous worker's claims — let me verify independently.\n\nLet me check:\n1. git status (what's uncommitted?)\n2. git log (what's in HEAD?)\n3. Do the owned files exist?\n4. Run the validator — does it pass?\n\nLet me start.\n\nActually, wait. Let me re-read the failure more carefully. The previous attempt's notes.md content was partially shown. It said the owned files were \"already committed in HEAD\" and \"re-running would produce byte-identical content and no diff vs HEAD.\"\n\nSo the worker concluded no changes needed. But the Ringer check needs a non-empty patch. The fix: I need to make actual changes to the owned files so there's a diff.\n\nBut here's the tension: if the files are already correct and hardened, making changes risks breaking them. However, the check explicitly demands a non-empty patch.\n\nLet me think about what legitimate change could be made. Perhaps the files have real issues that the previous worker glossed over. Or perhaps the files need to be re-created/regenerated in this worktree.\n\nActually — here's a critical possibility: the worktree is a fresh checkout from some base commit that does NOT include these files. The previous worker may have looked at the wrong thing (maybe the files exist in the main repo but not in this worktree's HEAD). Let me verify whether the files actually exist in THIS worktree and whether they're tracked.\n\nIf the files don't exist in this worktree's HEAD, then creating them would produce a patch. That's the likely scenario! The worktree is checked out from a base branch that doesn't have these files, and the previous worker mistakenly thought they were committed because... maybe it looked at a different location or the files were already present in the worktree's working directory (untracked? or from a previous attempt?).\n\nHmm, this is getting complicated. Let me just investigate the actual state thoroughly.\n\nLet me run several diagnostic commands in parallel:\n- `git status`\n- `git log --oneline -10`\n- `git diff --stat`\n- check if owned files exist\n- check if sibling files exist\n\nLet me do this.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_f706f4179001CcEGLnm5T2TbaH","sessionID":"ses_08f914172ffeudlWP9EWlAXTjJ","messageID":"msg_f706ebfaf001KfOUJkWS2De1kf"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1784297768442,"sessionID":"ses_08f91718dffe8QIoOmeSnVHPPW","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-b7a31980153d44e2","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/doug/.ringer/work/bmad-hybrid/5-6-manage-phase-2-knowledge-and-analytics-projections/_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/phase2-projections-slice.json"},"output":"<path>/home/doug/.ringer/work/bmad-hybrid/5-6-manage-phase-2-knowledge-and-analytics-projections/_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/phase2-projections-slice.json</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: {\n2:   \"artifactVersion\": \"2026-07-13\",\n3:   \"storyKey\": \"5-6-manage-phase-2-knowledge-and-analytics-projections\",\n4:   \"status\": \"local-contract-not-tenant-verified\",\n5:   \"purpose\": \"Prove that Phase-2 knowledge and analytics projections (Fabric knowledge, Copilot Studio surface, analytics) stay DEFERRED until the MVP contracts stabilize, and that graph/ontology expansion never owns workflow state. Three Phase-2 projection plans are catalogued with their triggering stability criteria, each marked phase:2, deferredUntil:'mvp-contracts-stable', and ownsWorkflowState:false. A premature-activation attempt yields a policy-denial receipt and the projection remains deferred. The 4-5 semantic-contract projection slice is cross-referenced (planes are projections only) — referenced, not duplicated. Local contract evidence only; every would-be live plane write appears as a deferred entry naming its receipt gate.\",\n6:   \"guards\": {\n7:     \"noTenantWrites\": true,\n8:     \"noOutboundAction\": true,\n9:     \"noApprovalExecution\": true,\n10:     \"requiresExplicitHumanApprovalForExecution\": true,\n11:     \"receiptsAreLocalContractEvidenceOnly\": true,\n12:     \"phase2ProjectionsDeferredUntilMvpContractsStable\": true,\n13:     \"projectionsNeverOwnWorkflowState\": true,\n14:     \"prematureActivationPolicyDenied\": true,\n15:     \"planesAreProjectionsOnly\": true,\n16:     \"noCanonicalAuthoringInPlanes\": true,\n17:     \"semanticContractProjectionCrossReferencedNotDuplicated\": true,\n18:     \"noPhase2PlaneWriteInThisSlice\": true\n19:   },\n20:   \"phase2ProjectionRun\": {\n21:     \"runId\": \"PHASE2PROJ-LOCAL-2026-07-13-001\",\n22:     \"actorType\": \"system\",\n23:     \"actorId\": \"local-bmad-validator\",\n24:     \"authorityBasis\": \"local non-tenant Story 5.6 contract validation\",\n25:     \"semanticContractVersion\": \"2026-07-07\",\n26:     \"canonicalSource\": \"council-semantic-contract\",\n27:     \"deferredUntil\": \"mvp-contracts-stable\",\n28:     \"inputVocabularyFrom\": [\n29:       \"dataverse-mvp-schema-manifest.json\",\n30:       \"semantic-contract-projection-slice.json\"\n31:     ],\n32:     \"decisionPolicy\": {\n33:       \"phase2ProjectionsDeferredUntilMvpContractsStable\": true,\n34:       \"projectionPlansNeverOwnWorkflowState\": true,\n35:       \"prematureActivationYieldsPolicyDenial\": true,\n36:       \"stabilityCriteriaMustBeNamedPerPlan\": true,\n37:       \"planesAreProjectionsOnly\": true,\n38:       \"semanticContractProjectionSliceReferencedNotDuplicated\": true,\n39:       \"livePhase2PlaneWritesReceiptGated\": true\n40:     },\n41:     \"projectionPlans\": [\n42:       {\n43:         \"planId\": \"PHASE2-PLAN-LOCAL-001\",\n44:         \"planName\": \"Fabric knowledge projection (Phase 2)\",\n45:         \"phase\": 2,\n46:         \"targetSurface\": \"fabric-iq-ontology\",\n47:         \"deferredUntil\": \"mvp-contracts-stable\",\n48:         \"triggeringStabilityCriteria\": [\n49:           \"Epic 2 receipt-backed Work Item state changes (Story 2.3) are tenant-verified and stable\",\n50:           \"Epic 4 Council Semantic Contract vocabulary (com_graphedgetype / com_graphentitytype) is tenant-verified and frozen for re-projection\",\n51:           \"Story 4.5 semantic-contract projection slice projectionManifest has been tenant-verified against the live Dataverse semantic model and Fabric IQ ontology without unresolved drift\"\n52:         ],\n53:         \"ownsWorkflowState\": false,\n54:         \"planRationale\": \"Fabric IQ ontology becomes a projection surface for Council knowledge once the MVP contracts that define Work Item state, source-record capture, and semantic-contract vocabulary are stable. Until then this plan stays deferred; ontology expansion may only propose terms back to the Council Semantic Contract and never owns workflow state.\",\n55:         \"referencedSemanticContractProjectionSlice\": \"semantic-contract-projection-slice.json\",\n56:         \"referencedProjectionIds\": [\n57:           \"PROJ-LOCAL-SCP-003\",\n58:           \"PROJ-LOCAL-SCP-004\",\n59:           \"PROJ-LOCAL-SCP-005\"\n60:         ],\n61:         \"plannedProjectionSurface\": \"Fabric IQ ontology entities/edges projected from council-semantic-contract; no Work Item execution authority\",\n62:         \"liveWriteDeferredTo\": \"receipt-gated post mvp-contracts-stable; no tenant write in this slice\"\n63:       },\n64:       {\n65:         \"planId\": \"PHASE2-PLAN-LOCAL-002\",\n66:         \"planName\": \"Copilot Studio surface projection (Phase 2)\",\n67:         \"phase\": 2,\n68:         \"targetSurface\": \"copilot-studio-surface\",\n69:         \"deferredUntil\": \"mvp-contracts-stable\",\n70:         \"triggeringStabilityCriteria\": [\n71:           \"Epic 2 approval boundaries (Story 2.2) are tenant-verified so Copilot surface actions never bypass human approval\",\n72:           \"Epic 3 handoff/reply drafts (Story 3.3) are tenant-verified for the outbound-action contract the Copilot surface would invoke\",\n73:           \"Story 4.4 approved-instruction receipts are tenant-verified so the Copilot surface only acts on receipt-backed approved instructions\"\n74:         ],\n75:         \"ownsWorkflowState\": false,\n76:         \"planRationale\": \"A Copilot Studio surface becomes the conversational projection of Council Work Items only once the approval-boundary, handoff, and approved-instruction MVP contracts are stable. The surface projects Council state read-only and routes any action through the receipt-gated MVP contracts; it never owns workflow state and never writes directly to Dataverse.\",\n77:         \"referencedSemanticContractProjectionSlice\": \"semantic-contract-projection-slice.json\",\n78:         \"referencedProjectionIds\": [\n79:           \"PROJ-LOCAL-SCP-001\",\n80:           \"PROJ-LOCAL-SCP-002\",\n81:           \"PROJ-LOCAL-SCP-006\"\n82:         ],\n83:         \"plannedProjectionSurface\": \"Copilot Studio topic/action projecting Council Work Items and Receipts read-only; outbound actions route through Epic 2/3 receipt gates\",\n84:         \"liveWriteDeferredTo\": \"receipt-gated post mvp-contracts-stable; no tenant write in this slice\"\n85:       },\n86:       {\n87:         \"planId\": \"PHASE2-PLAN-LOCAL-003\",\n88:         \"planName\": \"Analytics projection (Phase 2)\",\n89:         \"phase\": 2,\n90:         \"targetSurface\": \"analytics-warehouse\",\n91:         \"deferredUntil\": \"mvp-contracts-stable\",\n92:         \"triggeringStabilityCriteria\": [\n93:           \"Epic 2 idempotent-mutation receipts (Story 2.4) are tenant-verified so analytics can replay receipt-backed state deterministically\",\n94:           \"Epic 1 source-record and Work Item schemas (Stories 1.1-1.5) are tenant-verified and frozen for analytics modeling\",\n95:           \"Story 2.6 failure/policy-denial receipts are tenant-verified so analytics can classify denials without inferring state\"\n96:         ],\n97:         \"ownsWorkflowState\": false,\n98:         \"planRationale\": \"Analytics over Council receipts and Work Items becomes a Phase-2 projection once the MVP receipt and schema contracts are stable. Analytics is a read-only projection of receipt-backed state; it never owns workflow state and never writes back into Dataverse without a new receipt.\",\n99:         \"referencedSemanticContractProjectionSlice\": \"semantic-contract-projection-slice.json\",\n100:         \"referencedProjectionIds\": [\n101:           \"PROJ-LOCAL-SCP-001\",\n102:           \"PROJ-LOCAL-SCP-002\"\n103:         ],\n104:         \"plannedProjectionSurface\": \"Analytics warehouse projected from receipt-backed Council state; read-only, no write-back authority\",\n105:         \"liveWriteDeferredTo\": \"receipt-gated post mvp-contracts-stable; no tenant write in this slice\"\n106:       }\n107:     ],\n108:     \"prematureActivationAttempts\": [\n109:       {\n110:         \"attemptId\": \"PHASE2-PREACT-LOCAL-001\",\n111:         \"targetPlanId\": \"PHASE2-PLAN-LOCAL-002\",\n112:         \"attemptedSurface\": \"copilot-studio-surface\",\n113:         \"attemptedAction\": \"Activate the Copilot Studio surface projection before the approval-boundary, handoff, and approved-instruction MVP contracts are tenant-verified.\",\n114:         \"deniedByReceipt\": \"CR-LOCAL-PHASE2-PREACT-DENIED-001\",\n115:         \"denialRationale\": \"The Copilot Studio surface projection is gated by deferredUntil:'mvp-contracts-stable'. The triggering stability criteria for PHASE2-PLAN-LOCAL-002 are not yet tenant-verified, so activating the surface now would let a projection bypass the receipt-gated MVP approval boundaries. A policy_denied receipt is appended and the projection remains deferred; no plane write occurs in this slice.\",\n116:         \"projectionRemainsDeferred\": true,\n117:         \"attemptedAt\": \"2026-07-13T18:05:00+00:00\"\n118:       }\n119:     ],\n120:     \"receipts\": [\n121:       {\n122:         \"com_receipt_id\": \"CR-LOCAL-PHASE2-DEFER-001\",\n123:         \"com_verb\": \"reviewed\",\n124:         \"com_actor_type\": \"system\",\n125:         \"com_actor_id\": \"local-bmad-validator\",\n126:         \"com_authority_basis\": \"local non-tenant Story 5.6 contract validation\",\n127:         \"com_occurred_at\": \"2026-07-13T17:55:00+00:00\",\n128:     