{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1784297770271,"sessionID":"ses_08f91718dffe8QIoOmeSnVHPPW","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-94449c3f2ed02349","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/doug/.ringer/work/bmad-hybrid/5-6-manage-phase-2-knowledge-and-analytics-projections/notes.md"},"output":"<path>/home/doug/.ringer/work/bmad-hybrid/5-6-manage-phase-2-knowledge-and-analytics-projections/notes.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Notes — Story 5.6: Manage Phase 2 Knowledge and Analytics Projections\n2: \n3: ## Outcome\n4: \n5: Both ringer-owned deliverables already exist in the worktree, committed at\n6: `ac56eb8` (\"epic 5 stories 5-1..5-6: slices + validators via Reflex v2\n7: (pre-review)\"), and are **complete and correct per the story spec**. No edits\n8: were required; I verified them in place and left them unmodified.\n9: \n10: ## Files owned / verified\n11: \n12: - `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/phase2-projections-slice.json`\n13:   (storyKey `5-6-manage-phase-2-knowledge-and-analytics-projections`)\n14: - `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/phase2-projections-slice-validate.ps1`\n15:   (prints `PHASE2_PROJECTIONS_SLICE_VALIDATE_OK`, exits 0 on success)\n16: \n17: No `git commit` / `git add` / `git push` was run; `.git` was not touched.\n18: \n19: ## What the slice proves (matches \"Slice must prove\")\n20: \n21: 1. Three Phase-2 projection plans — `PHASE2-PLAN-LOCAL-001` (Fabric knowledge /\n22:    `fabric-iq-ontology`), `PHASE2-PLAN-LOCAL-002` (Copilot Studio surface /\n23:    `copilot-studio-surface`), `PHASE2-PLAN-LOCAL-003` (analytics /\n24:    `analytics-warehouse`) — each with `phase: 2` (strict integer),\n25:    `deferredUntil: \"mvp-contracts-stable\"`, a non-empty\n26:    `triggeringStabilityCriteria` list naming the MVP contracts that must hold,\n27:    and `ownsWorkflowState: false`.\n28: 2. Guard scenario: `prematureActivationAttempts[PHASE2-PREACT-LOCAL-001]`\n29:    targets `PHASE2-PLAN-LOCAL-002` and is denied by receipt\n30:    `CR-LOCAL-PHASE2-PREACT-DENIED-001` (verb `policy_denied`, result\n31:    `rejected`); `projectionRemainsDeferred: true`.\n32: 3. Cross-reference to the 4-5 semantic-contract projection slice: every plan\n33:    carries `referencedSemanticContractProjectionSlice:\n34:    \"semantic-contract-projection-slice.json\"` plus `referencedProjectionIds`\n35:    that resolve in that slice's `projectionManifest` (PROJ-LOCAL-SCP-001..006,\n36:    all confirmed present). Referenced, not duplicated.\n37: \n38: ## Validator hardening (matches \"Validator must assert\" + the review kill list)\n39: \n40: - All plans deferred with non-empty stability criteria; `ownsWorkflowState`\n41:   strictly false (boolean check, not truthy).\n42: - Denial receipt binds to a plan id via `prematureActivationAttempts[].deniedByReceipt`\n43:   and the receipt's `com_evidence_refs` names the targeted plan — general rules\n44:   over collections, no hardcoded-id binding.\n45: - 4-5 cross-reference resolves when that slice is present (loads from\n46:   `$PSScriptRoot`, asserts its `storyKey`, harvests `projectionId`s, and checks\n47:   `planesAreProjectionsOnly=true`).\n48: - LIVE cross-slice id harvest from `$PSScriptRoot` via `Invoke-CollectSiblingIds`,\n49:   distinguishing MINTED ids (plan/attempt/receipt/run — must be unique across\n50:   ALL slices) from REFERENCED ids (targetPlanId, deniedByReceipt,\n51:   referencedProjectionIds, link source records — must resolve).\n52: - No self-asserted booleans standing in for proof; no conditional/skippable\n53:   mandatory checks; coverage derived (every plan must have a deferred\n54:   live-write entry; every receipt must be link-bound; every cited evidence id\n55:   in `acceptanceMapping.localEvidence` must resolve).\n56: - Guards all strict-boolean-true; ISO 8601 timestamps with explicit UTC offset;\n57:   `TryParse` numeric checks for `com_confidence`; wrapped JSON loads;\n58:   `$PSScriptRoot`-relative paths; final `PHASE2_PROJECTIONS_SLICE_VALIDATE_OK`\n59:   token + `exit 1` on any issue.\n60: \n61: ## Verification commands\n62: \n63: ```\n64: export DOTNET_ROOT=$HOME/.dotnet\n65: export PATH=$HOME/.dotnet:$HOME/.dotnet/tools:$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH\n66: pwsh -File _bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/phase2-projections-slice-validate.ps1\n67: ```\n68: \n69: Result: prints `PHASE2_PROJECTIONS_SLICE_VALIDATE_OK`, `EXIT=0`.\n70: \n71: ## Corruption test (story requires: corrupted copy FAILS)\n72: \n73: Backed up the slice, corrupted it in place (flipped\n74: `PHASE2-PLAN-LOCAL-001.ownsWorkflowState` to `true`, dropped the denial\n75: receipt and all premature-activation attempts), and reran the validator:\n76: \n77: ```\n78: - Projection plan PHASE2-PLAN-LOCAL-001 ownsWorkflowState must be strict boolean false...\n79: - Phase 2 projection run must include at least one prematureActivationAttempt...\n80: - Phase 2 projection run must include at least two receipts...\n81: - Phase 2 projection run must include >=1 premature-activation denial receipt...\n82: - Receipt source link ... must bind a receipt from this slice...\n83: - Acceptance mapping for AC 2 cites an evidence id that does not resolve...: PHASE2-PREACT-LOCAL-001\n84: - Acceptance mapping for AC 2 cites an evidence id that does not resolve...: CR-LOCAL-PHASE2-PREACT-DENIED-001\n85: EXIT=1\n86: ```\n87: \n88: Restored from backup and reconfirmed `EXIT=0` with the OK token. Also\n89: verified an out-of-tree corrupted copy FAILS (`EXIT=1`).\n90: \n91: ## What I read for conventions\n92: \n93: - `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/source-drift-supersession-slice.json`\n94:   and `...-slice-validate.ps1` (story 1-5) — the gold-standard slice +\n95:   validator pair; mirrored structure, guards, wrapped JSON loads,\n96:   `Test-HasNonEmptyField` / `Test-ConfidenceInRange` / `Test-IsoTimestamp`\n97:   / `Get-ComparableInstant` helpers, `Invoke-CollectSiblingIds` live\n98:   harvest, MINTED-vs-REFERENCED id discipline, acceptance-mapping\n99:   evidence-id resolution.\n100: - `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/semantic-contract-projection-slice.json`\n101:   (story 4-5) — cross-reference target; confirmed `projectionId`\n102:   PROJ-LOCAL-SCP-001..006 all present and `planesAreProjectionsOnly` guard.\n103: - `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/dataverse-mvp-schema-manifest.json`\n104:   — vocabulary source (verbs `reviewed` + `policy_denied`, actor types,\n105:   receipt results, `com_councilreceiptsource.com_evidence_role`).\n106: \n107: ## Assumptions / follow-ups\n108: \n109: - Assumption: the two deliverables being already present and committed is the\n110:   expected state for this dispatch (the work was produced in a prior pass and\n111:   this run is a verification/confirm pass). I did not rewrite working,\n112:   spec-conforming, passing code.\n113: - Follow-up (integrator, NOT this slice): wire\n114:   `phase2-projections-slice-validate.ps1` into\n115:   `council-mvp-local-validate.ps1` — the story explicitly forbids the slice\n116:   author from editing that suite wiring.\n117: - Follow-up: tenant-verification of each plan's triggering stability criteria\n118:   and any live Phase-2 plane write remain VERIFY IN TENANT, receipt-gated\n119:   post `mvp-contracts-stable`; this slice is local contract evidence only.\n\n(End of file - total 119 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Notes — Story 5.6: Manage Phase 2 Knowledge and Analytics Projections\n\n## Outcome\n\nBoth ringer-owned deliverables already exist in the worktree, committed at\n`ac56eb8` (\"epic 5 stories 5-1..5-6: slices + validators via Reflex v2\n(pre-review)\"), and are **complete and correct per the story spec**. No edits\nwere required; I verified them in place and left them unmodified.\n\n## Files owned / verified\n\n- `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/phase2-projections-slice.json`\n  (storyKey `5-6-manage-phase-2-knowledge-and-analytics-projections`)\n- `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/phase2-projections-slice-validate.ps1`\n  (prints `PHASE2_PROJECTIONS_SLICE_VALIDATE_OK`, exits 0 on success)\n\nNo `git commit` / `git add` / `git push` was run; `.git` was not touched.\n\n## What the slice proves (matches \"Slice must prove\")\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/doug/.ringer/work/bmad-hybrid/5-6-manage-phase-2-knowledge-and-analytics-projections/notes.md","text":"# Notes — Story 5.6: Manage Phase 2 Knowledge and Analytics Projections\n\n## Outcome\n\nBoth ringer-owned deliverables already exist in the worktree, committed at\n`ac56eb8` (\"epic 5 stories 5-1..5-6: slices + validators via Reflex v2\n(pre-review)\"), and are **complete and correct per the story spec**. No edits\nwere required; I verified them in place and left them unmodified.\n\n## Files owned / verified\n\n- `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/phase2-projections-slice.json`\n  (storyKey `5-6-manage-phase-2-knowledge-and-analytics-projections`)\n- `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/phase2-projections-slice-validate.ps1`\n  (prints `PHASE2_PROJECTIONS_SLICE_VALIDATE_OK`, exits 0 on success)\n\nNo `git commit` / `git add` / `git push` was run; `.git` was not touched.\n\n## What the slice proves (matches \"Slice must prove\")\n\n1. Three Phase-2 projection plans — `PHASE2-PLAN-LOCAL-001` (Fabric knowledge /\n   `fabric-iq-ontology`), `PHASE2-PLAN-LOCAL-002` (Copilot Studio surface /\n   `copilot-studio-surface`), `PHASE2-PLAN-LOCAL-003` (analytics /\n   `analytics-warehouse`) — each with `phase: 2` (strict integer),\n   `deferredUntil: \"mvp-contracts-stable\"`, a non-empty\n   `triggeringStabilityCriteria` list naming the MVP contracts that must hold,\n   and `ownsWorkflowState: false`.\n2. Guard scenario: `prematureActivationAttempts[PHASE2-PREACT-LOCAL-001]`\n   targets `PHASE2-PLAN-LOCAL-002` and is denied by receipt\n   `CR-LOCAL-PHASE2-PREACT-DENIED-001` (verb `policy_denied`, result\n   `rejected`); `projectionRemainsDeferred: true`.\n3. Cross-reference to the 4-5 semantic-contract projection slice: every plan\n   carries `referencedSemanticContractProjectionSlice:\n   \"semantic-contract-projection-slice.json\"` plus `referencedProjectionIds`\n   that resolve in that slice's `projectionManifest` (PROJ-LOCAL-SCP-001..006,\n   all confirmed present). Referenced, not duplicated.\n\n## Validator hardening (matches \"Validator must assert\" + the review kill list)\n\n- All plans deferred with non-empty stability criteria; `ownsWorkflowState`\n  strictly false (boolean check, not truthy).\n- Denial receipt binds to a plan id via `prematureActivationAttempts[].deniedByReceipt`\n  and the receipt's `com_evidence_refs` names the targeted plan — general rules\n  over collections, no hardcoded-id binding.\n- 4-5 cross-reference resolves when that slice is present (loads from\n  `$PSScriptRoot`, asserts its `storyKey`, harvests `projectionId`s, and checks\n  `planesAreProjectionsOnly=true`).\n- LIVE cross-slice id harvest from `$PSScriptRoot` via `Invoke-CollectSiblingIds`,\n  distinguishing MINTED ids (plan/attempt/receipt/run — must be unique across\n  ALL slices) from REFERENCED ids (targetPlanId, deniedByReceipt,\n  referencedProjectionIds, link source records — must resolve).\n- No self-asserted booleans standing in for proof; no conditional/skippable\n  mandatory checks; coverage derived (every plan must have a deferred\n  live-write entry; every receipt must be link-bound; every cited evidence id\n  in `acceptanceMapping.localEvidence` must resolve).\n- Guards all strict-boolean-true; ISO 8601 timestamps with explicit UTC offset;\n  `TryParse` numeric checks for `com_confidence`; wrapped JSON loads;\n  `$PSScriptRoot`-relative paths; final `PHASE2_PROJECTIONS_SLICE_VALIDATE_OK`\n  token + `exit 1` on any issue.\n\n## Verification commands\n\n```\nexport DOTNET_ROOT=$HOME/.dotnet\nexport PATH=$HOME/.dotnet:$HOME/.dotnet/tools:$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH\npwsh -File _bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/phase2-projections-slice-validate.ps1\n```\n\nResult: prints `PHASE2_PROJECTIONS_SLICE_VALIDATE_OK`, `EXIT=0`.\n\n## Corruption test (story requires: corrupted copy FAILS)\n\nBacked up the slice, corrupted it in place (flipped\n`PHASE2-PLAN-LOCAL-001.ownsWorkflowState` to `true`, dropped the denial\nreceipt and all premature-activation attempts), and reran the validator:\n\n```\n- Projection plan PHASE2-PLAN-LOCAL-001 ownsWorkflowState must be strict boolean false...\n- Phase 2 projection run must include at least one prematureActivationAttempt...\n- Phase 2 projection run must include at least two receipts...\n- Phase 2 projection run must include >=1 premature-activation denial receipt...\n- Receipt source link ... must bind a receipt from this slice...\n- Acceptance mapping for AC 2 cites an evidence id that does not resolve...: PHASE2-PREACT-LOCAL-001\n- Acceptance mapping for AC 2 cites an evidence id that does not resolve...: CR-LOCAL-PHASE2-PREACT-DENIED-001\nEXIT=1\n```\n\nRestored from backup and reconfirmed `EXIT=0` with the OK token. Also\nverified an out-of-tree corrupted copy FAILS (`EXIT=1`).\n\n## What I read for conventions\n\n- `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/source-drift-supersession-slice.json`\n  and `...-slice-validate.ps1` (story 1-5) — the gold-standard slice +\n  validator pair; mirrored structure, guards, wrapped JSON loads,\n  `Test-HasNonEmptyField` / `Test-ConfidenceInRange` / `Test-IsoTimestamp`\n  / `Get-ComparableInstant` helpers, `Invoke-CollectSiblingIds` live\n  harvest, MINTED-vs-REFERENCED id discipline, acceptance-mapping\n  evidence-id resolution.\n- `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/semantic-contract-projection-slice.json`\n  (story 4-5) — cross-reference target; confirmed `projectionId`\n  PROJ-LOCAL-SCP-001..006 all present and `planesAreProjectionsOnly` guard.\n- `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/dataverse-mvp-schema-manifest.json`\n  — vocabulary source (verbs `reviewed` + `policy_denied`, actor typ