LL=[]\nplatform-evaluation-slice.json: CSK=[] CR-LOCAL-SKILL=[]\nproposed-work-item-extraction-slice.json: CSK=[] CR-LOCAL-SKILL=[]\nreceipt-backed-state-changes-slice.json: CSK=[] CR-LOCAL-SKILL=[]\nsemantic-contract-projection-slice.json: CSK=[] CR-LOCAL-SKILL=[]\nskill-authority-expansion-slice.json: CSK=['CSK-LOCAL-FABRIC-PUBLISHER-001', 'CSK-LOCAL-MEETING-DIGEST-001'] CR-LOCAL-SKILL=['CR-LOCAL-SKILL-APPROVE-001', 'CR-LOCAL-SKILL-DENY-001']\nskill-registry-slice.json: CSK=['CSK-LOCAL-DRIFT-SCAN-001', 'CSK-LOCAL-LEGACY-SUMMARIZE-001', 'CSK-LOCAL-OUTBOUND-SEND-001'] CR-LOCAL-SKILL=['CR-LOCAL-SKILL-FLAG-001', 'CR-LOCAL-SKILL-PREVENT-001']\nsource-drift-supersession-slice.json: CSK=[] CR-LOCAL-SKILL=[]\nstate-transition-demo-evidence.json: BAD JSON Unexpected UTF-8 BOM (decode using utf-8-sig): line 1 column 1 (char 0)\ntenant-decision-packet.json: CSK=[] CR-LOCAL-SKILL=[]\ntenant-readiness-gates-slice.json: CSK=[] CR-LOCAL-SKILL=[]\nwork-item-execution-shell-slice.json: CSK=[] CR-LOCAL-SKILL=[]\nzero-multi-item-extraction-slice.json: CSK=[] CR-LOCAL-SKILL=[]\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cd _bmad-output/implementation-artifacts && ls *.json && echo \"---\" && python3 -c \"\nimport json,glob,os\nfor f in sorted(glob.glob('*.json')):\n    if f=='dataverse-mvp-schema-manifest.json': continue\n    try:\n        d=json.load(open(f))\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f'{f}: BAD JSON {e}'); continue\n    # harvest CSK, CR, REC, CSR ids\n    text=json.dumps(d)\n    import re\n    csk=sorted(set(re.findall(r'CSK-LOCAL-[A-Z0-9-]+',text)))\n    cr=sorted(set(re.findall(r'CR-LOCAL-SKILL-[A-Z0-9-]+',text)))\n    csr=sorted(set(re.findall(r'CSR-[A-Z0-9-]+',text)))\n    print(f'{f}: CSK={csk} CR-LOCAL-SKILL={cr}')\n\"","time":{"start":1784297788529,"end":1784297788535}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The manifest marks com_required_inputs as NOT required, but the story says each skill MUST declare \"required inputs\". The validator pins `com_required_inputs` as story-required (line 376: `$storyRequiredSkillFields = @($skillRequiredFields + @(\"com_required_inputs\") | Sort-Object -Unique)`). Good — so that's already covered.\n\nSo the manifest's required skill fields are exactly: com_name, com_council_skill_id, com_trigger, com_allowed_context, com_authority_class, com_approval_requirements, com_proof_owed, com_update_policy, com_status. Plus the story pins com_required_inputs. So all 10 fields the story lists are verified. Good.\n\nSo the slice and validator look complete and correct. The real problem is purely that I need to produce a non-empty patch against the ringer-owned files.\n\nLet me look more carefully for a legitimate hardening improvement. The hardening bar mentions: \"Verify a corrupted slice copy FAILS before finishing.\" The previous worker claimed to have verified this. But the validator itself doesn't have a self-test. That's not a code requirement though.\n\nLet me reconsider — maybe there IS a subtle real defect. Let me examine the receipt's `com_evidence_refs` resolution. The flag receipt's com_evidence_refs = \"CSK-LOCAL-LEGACY-SUMMARIZE-001; REC-LOCAL-FLAG-001\". The prevent's = \"CSK-LOCAL-OUTBOUND-SEND-001; REC-LOCAL-PREVENT-001\". \n\nNow, the acceptanceMapping AC2 evidence cites REC-LOCAL-FLAG-001 and REC-LOCAL-PREVENT-001 — but wait, those are scenario ids, and the regex in acceptance mapping check matches `REC-LOCAL-[A-Z0-9-]+`. The slice's acceptanceMapping evidence item 2 mentions \"REC-LOCAL-FLAG-001 recommends...\" — wait, but REC-LOCAL-FLAG-001 is the scenario id, and the scenario recommends the skill. Let me re-read AC2 evidence: \"skillRegistryRun.recommendationScenarios REC-LOCAL-FLAG-001 recommends CSK-LOCAL-LEGACY-SUMMARIZE-001...\" Yes that's the scenario. OK it resolves via sliceScenarioIds. Fine.\n\nOK. Let me look at a different angle. Let me check whether the sibling slice `proposed-work-item-extraction-slice.json` exists and whether its ids collide with anything here. And check the source-drift-supersession slice (story 1-5) which the story names as the gold standard.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_f706f82e6001L3vHWyQyIPNs47","sessionID":"ses_08f91df9fffe5mB6W2L75K6q9K","messageID":"msg_f706f4a74001iOhCUUwmy1mAkg"}}
