{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1784297797641,"sessionID":"ses_08f914172ffeudlWP9EWlAXTjJ","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-8136ed8caffcefc2","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/doug/.ringer/work/bmad-hybrid/5-3-record-microsoft-platform-evaluation-evidence/_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/platform-evaluation-slice.json"},"output":"<path>/home/doug/.ringer/work/bmad-hybrid/5-3-record-microsoft-platform-evaluation-evidence/_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/platform-evaluation-slice.json</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: {\n2:   \"artifactVersion\": \"2026-07-14\",\n3:   \"storyKey\": \"5-3-record-microsoft-platform-evaluation-evidence\",\n4:   \"status\": \"local-contract-not-tenant-verified\",\n5:   \"purpose\": \"Prove that Microsoft-native planes are evaluated before any custom substrate is approved, and that every custom-service proposal cites the specific Microsoft-native gap or tenant constraint it fills. Two capability evaluations each weigh at least four named Microsoft candidates against tenant gates, permission/DLP impact, licensing/cost, ALM path, contract gaps, decision, and a review reference. One custom-service proposal cites a recorded gap in an evaluation row, and its decision is recorded as an append-only receipt BEFORE any implementation; no implementation artifacts are referenced and no live Dataverse write is performed. Every would-be live write appears only as a deferred, receipt-gated entry.\",\n6:   \"guards\": {\n7:     \"noTenantWrites\": true,\n8:     \"noOutboundAction\": true,\n9:     \"noApprovalExecution\": true,\n10:     \"requiresExplicitHumanApprovalForExecution\": true,\n11:     \"microsoftNativeEvaluatedBeforeCustomSubstrate\": true,\n12:     \"customServicesMustCiteMicrosoftGap\": true,\n13:     \"decisionsRecordedBeforeImplementation\": true,\n14:     \"receiptsAreLocalContractEvidenceOnly\": true,\n15:     \"noImplementationArtifactsReferenced\": true\n16:   },\n17:   \"assumptions\": [\n18:     \"Microsoft product capability statements reflect public documentation as of 2026-07-07 (microsoft-platform-fit-matrix-2026-07-07.md contract date); tenant-specific gates, license SKUs, and DLP classifications are recorded as pending tenant verification, not as verified tenant facts.\",\n19:     \"The named candidate universe (Work IQ, Dataverse intelligence/MCP, Power Apps MCP agent feed, Copilot Studio, Power Automate, Fabric IQ/Graph, Fabric data agents) is the set the story spec enumerates; no candidate outside that set is admitted.\",\n20:     \"Doug is the human approval owner per tenant-decision-packet.json decisions.humanApprovalOwner.\"\n21:   ],\n22:   \"platformEvaluationRun\": {\n23:     \"runId\": \"PE-LOCAL-2026-07-14-001\",\n24:     \"actorType\": \"human\",\n25:     \"actorId\": \"Doug\",\n26:     \"authorityBasis\": \"local non-tenant Story 5.3 platform-fit authority; Doug is the human approval owner per tenant-decision-packet.json\",\n27:     \"semanticContractVersion\": \"2026-07-07\",\n28:     \"inputDecisionsFrom\": [\n29:       \"tenant-decision-packet.json\"\n30:     ],\n31:     \"decisionPolicy\": {\n32:       \"microsoftNativePlanesEvaluatedBeforeCustomSubstrate\": true,\n33:       \"customServiceMustCiteSpecificMicrosoftGapOrTenantConstraint\": true,\n34:       \"decisionsRecordedAsReceiptsBeforeAnyImplementation\": true,\n35:       \"receiptsAreLocalContractEvidenceOnly\": true,\n36:       \"noLiveDataverseMutationInThisSlice\": true,\n37:       \"evaluationRowsMapToManifestComCouncilplatformevaluation\": true\n38:     },\n39:     \"candidateUniverse\": [\n40:       \"Work IQ\",\n41:       \"Dataverse intelligence/MCP\",\n42:       \"Power Apps MCP agent feed\",\n43:       \"Copilot Studio\",\n44:       \"Power Automate\",\n45:       \"Fabric IQ/Graph\",\n46:       \"Fabric data agents\"\n47:     ],\n48:     \"evaluations\": [\n49:       {\n50:         \"capabilityEvaluationId\": \"PE-LOCAL-EVAL-001\",\n51:         \"com_council_capability\": \"memory-and-graph-grounding\",\n52:         \"capabilityQuestion\": \"Can a Microsoft-native plane ground Council memory candidates and the lightweight meaning graph without a custom substrate, given the link_only/hash_only source-body policy and the tenant decision to defer Fabric IQ/Graph to phase 2?\",\n53:         \"candidateRows\": [\n54:           {\n55:             \"rowId\": \"PE-LOCAL-EVAL-001-ROW-01\",\n56:             \"com_name\": \"Platform evaluation - memory/graph grounding - Work IQ\",\n57:             \"com_council_capability\": \"memory-and-graph-grounding\",\n58:             \"com_microsoft_candidate\": \"Work IQ\",\n59:             \"com_official_source_date_checked\": \"2026-07-07\",\n60:             \"com_tenant_gate\": \"Work IQ is not provisioned in the sdhdev tenant as of 2026-07-07; onboarding requires a tenant admin to enable the Work IQ service plan and confirm data residency. Pending tenant verification.\",\n61:             \"com_permission_dlp_impact\": \"Work IQ would index source-derived content; under the link_only/hash_only source-body policy the tenant DLP classification for Council sources must be confirmed before Work IQ indexing is allowed. Not yet tenant-verified.\",\n62:             \"com_licensing_cost_gate\": \"Work IQ licensing SKU and per-user licensing cost are not confirmed for this tenant; assumed to require a premium SK series. Pending tenant verification.\",\n63:             \"com_lifecycle_alm_path\": \"Work IQ artifacts do not have a confirmed Dataverse-solution-aware ALM path aligned with the CouncilOfMinionsMVP solution; ALM story is assumed unverified.\",\n64:             \"com_contract_gaps\": \"Gap: Work IQ has no documented append-only receipt ledger projection with idempotency-key alternate key and before/after state lineage matching the com_councilreceipt contract; it is not solution-aware in the CouncilOfMinionsMVP solution today.\",\n65:             \"com_decision\": \"defer\",\n66:             \"com_review_reference\": \"Defer until Work IQ is provisioned in the tenant and its receipt-ledger alignment is tested; revisit after Epic 2 receipt semantics land.\"\n67:           },\n68:           {\n69:             \"rowId\": \"PE-LOCAL-EVAL-001-ROW-02\",\n70:             \"com_name\": \"Platform evaluation - memory/graph grounding - Dataverse intelligence/MCP\",\n71:             \"com_council_capability\": \"memory-and-graph-grounding\",\n72:             \"com_microsoft_candidate\": \"Dataverse intelligence/MCP\",\n73:             \"com_official_source_date_checked\": \"2026-07-07\",\n74:             \"com_tenant_gate\": \"Dataverse MCP exposes table-row semantics over the existing sdhdev environment; the tenant environment and organization IDs are confirmed read-only in tenant-decision-packet.json. No new tenant gating beyond the existing Dataverse write gate.\",\n75:             \"com_permission_dlp_impact\": \"Dataverse MCP reads inherit the existing Council table permissions and DLP policies; no new connector boundary is introduced. DLP classification stays with the Dataverse environment, already approved for sandbox writes after read-only preflight.\",\n76:             \"com_licensing_cost_gate\": \"Dataverse intelligence/MCP is assumed to be covered by the existing Dataverse licensing already approved for the MVP operational store; no incremental SKU is assumed. Pending tenant verification of MCP entitlement.\",\n77:             \"com_lifecycle_alm_path\": \"Dataverse MCP is solution-aware within the CouncilOfMinionsMVP solution and follows the existing Dataverse ALM path (pac solution export/import); no new ALM rail is required.\",\n78:             \"com_contract_gaps\": \"Gap: Dataverse MCP exposes generic table-row CRUD semantics but projects no append-only receipt ledger view keyed by com_idempotency_key with com_before_state/com_after_state lineage, and no meaning-graph entity/edge projection matching the com_councilgraphentity/com_councilgraphedge contracts. The Council receipt contract and semantic contract require these projections; Dataverse MCP does not surface them natively, so a custom projection is required to fill this gap.\",\n79:             \"com_decision\": \"custom_gap_build\",\n80:             \"com_review_reference\": \"Custom service proposal CSP-LOCAL-001 cites this row's contract gap as the Microsoft-native gap it fills; decision recorded in receipt CR-LOCAL-PE-001 before any implementation.\"\n81:           },\n82:           {\n83:             \"rowId\": \"PE-LOCAL-EVAL-001-ROW-03\",\n84:             \"com_name\": \"Platform evaluation - memory/graph grounding - Fabric IQ/Graph\",\n85:             \"com_council_capability\": \"memory-and-graph-grounding\",\n86:             \"com_microsoft_candidate\": \"Fabric IQ/Graph\",\n87:             \"com_official_source_date_checked\": \"2026-07-07\",\n88:             \"com_tenant_gate\": \"Fabric IQ/Graph is explicitly deferred to phase 2 by tenant-decision-packet.json decisions.fabricIqGraphPhase2 (value: defer_to_phase_2); no Fabric capacity is provisioned for the MVP tenant.\",\n89:             \"com_permission_dlp_impact\": \"Fabric IQ/Graph would require a separate Fabric capacity and DLP boundary distinct from the Dataverse environment; not assessed for the MVP per the tenant decision to defer.\",\n90:             \"com_licensing_cost_gate\": \"Fabric capacity licensing is out of scope for the MVP per the tenant deferral decision; no cost gate is evaluated in this slice.\",\n91:             \"com_lifecycle_alm_path\": \"Fabric artifacts are not Dataverse-solution-aware in the CouncilOfMinionsMVP solution; ALM path is unverified and deferred.\",\n92:             \"com_contract_gaps\": \"Gap: Fabric IQ/Graph could host the meaning graph projection but is tenant-deferred to phase 2, so it cannot ground Council memory/graph semantics in the MVP without violating the recorded tenant decision.\",\n93:             \"com_decision\": \"defer\",\n94:             \"com_review_reference\": \"Defer per tenant-decision-packet.json fabricIqGraphPhase2=defer_to_phase_2; revisit in phase 2 graph and analytics projection.\"\n95:           },\n96:           {\n97:             \"rowId\": \"PE-LOCAL-EVAL-001-ROW-04\",\n98:             \"com_name\": \"Platform evaluation - memory/graph grounding - Fabric data agents\",\n99:             \"com_council_capability\": \"memory-and-graph-grounding\",\n100:             \"com_microsoft_candidate\": \"Fabric data agents\",\n101:             \"com_official_source_date_checked\": \"2026-07-07\",\n102:             \"com_tenant_gate\": \"Fabric data agents depend on Fabric capacity, which is deferred to phase 2 by the tenant decision; not provisioned in the MVP tenant.\",\n103:             \"com_permission_dlp_impact\": \"Fabric data agents operate on Fabric-resident data and introduce a boundary outside the Dataverse environment; not assessed for the MVP.\",\n104:             \"com_licensing_cost_gate\": \"Fabric data agents licensing is bundled with Fabric capacity and is out of scope for the MVP per the tenant deferral.\",\n105:             \"com_lifecycle_alm_path\": \"Fabric data agents are not Dataverse-solution-aware; ALM path is unverified and deferred.\",\n106:             \"com_contract_gaps\": \"Gap: Fabric data agents do not project the append-only receipt ledger or the com_councilgraphentity/com_councilgraphedge semantic contract and are blocked by the tenant Fabric deferral, so they cannot ground Council memory/graph semantics in the MVP.\",\n107:             \"com_decision\": \"reject\",\n108:             \"com_review_reference\": \"Reject for MVP because it depends on the tenant-deferred Fabric capacity; reconsider in phase 2.\"\n109:           }\n110:         ]\n111:       },\n112:       {\n113:         \"capabilityEvaluationId\": \"PE-LOCAL-EVAL-002\",\n114:         \"com_council_capability\": \"workflow-automation\",\n115:         \"capabilityQuestion\": \"Can a Microsoft-native plane drive receipt-backed Council Queue state changes and outbound-action requests without a custom automation substrate, respecting the no-flow-publish / no-agent-publish tenant guards?\",\n116:         \"candidateRows\": [\n117:           {\n118:             \"rowId\": \"PE-LOCAL-EVAL-002-ROW-01\",\n119:             \"com_name\": \"Platform evaluation - workflow automation - Power Automate\",\n120:             \"com_council_capability\": \"workflow-automation\",\n121:             \"com_microsoft_candidate\": \"Power Automate\",\n122:             \"com_official_source_date_checked\": \"2026-07-07\",\n123:             \"com_tenant_gate\": \"Power Automate flows run in the existing sdhdev tenant; the tenant guard noFlowPublish=true in dataverse-mvp-schema-manifest.json blocks publishing flows until Doug approves. No new tenant gating beyond the existing publish guard.\",\n124:             \"com_permission_dlp_impact\": \"Power Automate flows inherit the tenant DLP policy for connectors; Council flows must use Dataverse-only connectors under the link_only/hash_only source-body policy. DLP classification is pending tenant verification.\",\n125:             \"com_licensing_cost_gate\": \"Power Automate per-flow or per-user licensing is assumed to be covered by existing tenant entitlements; no incremental SKU is assumed. Pending tenant verification.\",\n126:             \"com_lifecycle_alm_path\": \"Power Automate flows are solution-aware within the CouncilOfMinionsMVP solution and follow the existing Dataverse ALM path; no new ALM rail is required, but flow publish stays guarded by noFlowPublish.\",\n127:             \"com_contract_gaps\": \"Gap: Power Automate can execute receipt-backed queue state changes but cannot itself define the receipt append-only ledger or idempotency semantics; it consumes the com_councilreceipt contract rather than projecting it. This is a consumption fit, not a contract gap requiring a custom build.\",\n128:             \"com_decision\": \"adopt\",\n129:             \"com_review_reference\": \"Adopt as the execution surface for receipt-backed queue state changes gated by noFlowPublish; aligns with Epic 2 Story 2.3 receipt semantics.\"\n130:           },\n131:           {\n132:             \"rowId\": \"PE-LOCAL-EVAL-002-ROW-02\",\n133:             \"com_name\": \"Platform evaluation - workflow automation - Copilot Studio\",\n134:             \"com_council_capability\": \"workflow-automation\",\n135:             \"com_microsoft_candidate\": \"Copilot Studio\",\n136:             \"com_official_source_date_checked\": \"2026-07-07\",\n137:             \"com_tenant_gate\": \"Copilot Studio agents are not published in the MVP tenant per the noAgentPublish=true guard; onboarding a Copilot agent requires Doug approval and a tenant admin to publish.\",\n138:             \"com_permission_dlp_impact\": \"Copilot Studio agents introduce a generative AI boundary over Council sources; under the link_only/hash_only source-body policy the DLP classification for generative grounding must be confirmed. Not yet tenant-verified.\",\n139:             \"com_licensing_cost_gate\": \"Copilot Studio licensing SKU is not confirmed for this tenant; assumed to require a Copilot Studio entitlement. Pending tenant verification.\",\n140:             \"com_lifecycle_alm_path\": \"Copilot Studio agents are solution-aware but the noAgentPublish guard blocks publication in the MVP; ALM path is verified but publication is gated.\",\n141:             \"com_contract_gaps\": \"Gap: Copilot Studio does not project the append-only receipt ledger or enforce idempotency keys; it can surface Council context but cannot own receipt-backed state transitions without violating noAgentPublish for the MVP.\",\n142:             \"com_decision\": \"defer\",\n143:             \"com_review_reference\": \"Defer until noAgentPublish is lifted by Doug and the generative-grounding DLP classification is tenant-verified.\"\n144:           },\n145:           {\n146:             \"rowId\": \"PE-LOCAL-EVAL-002-ROW-03\",\n147:             \"com_name\": \"Platform evaluation - workflow automation - Power Apps MCP agent feed\",\n148:             \"com_council_capability\": \"workflow-automation\",\n149:             \"com_microsoft_candidate\": \"Power Apps MCP agent feed\",\n150:             \"com_official_source_date_checked\": \"2026-07-07\",\n151:             \"com_tenant_gate\": \"The Power Apps MCP agent feed is explicitly deferred by tenant-decision-packet.json decisions.powerAppsMcpAgentFeedEvaluation (value: defer); the agent feed is not enabled in the MVP tenant.\",\n152:             \"com_permission_dlp_impact\": \"The MCP agent feed would expose app metadata to model-driven agents; DLP classification is not assessed for the MVP per the tenant deferral.\",\n153:             \"com_licensing_cost_gate\": \"Power Apps MCP agent feed licensing is out of scope for the MVP per the tenant deferral; no cost gate is evaluated in this slice.\",\n154:             \"com_lifecycle_alm_path\": \"The MCP agent feed is not Dataverse-solution-aware in the CouncilOfMinionsMVP solution; ALM path is unverified and deferred.\",\n155:             \"com_contract_gaps\": \"Gap: The Power Apps MCP agent feed could surface Council Queue actions to agents but is tenant-deferred, so it cannot drive receipt-backed workflow automation in the MVP without violating the recorded tenant decision.\",\n156:             \"com_decision\": \"defer\",\n157:             \"com_review_reference\": \"Defer per tenant-decision-packet.json powerAppsMcpAgentFeedEvaluation=defer; revisit after the model-driven app surface is accepted.\"\n158:           },\n159:           {\n160:             \"rowId\": \"PE-LOCAL-EVAL-002-ROW-04\",\n161:             \"com_name\": \"Platform evaluation - workflow automation - Work IQ\",\n162:             \"com_council_capability\": \"workflow-automation\",\n163:             \"com_microsoft_candidate\": \"Work IQ\",\n164:             \"com_official_source_date_checked\": \"2026-07-07\",\n165:             \"com_tenant_gate\": \"Work IQ is not provisioned in the sdhdev tenant as of 2026-07-07; onboarding requires a tenant admin to enable the Work IQ service plan. Pending tenant verification.\",\n166:             \"com_permission_dlp_impact\": \"Work IQ workflow automation would act on source-derived content; under the link_only/hash_only source-body policy the DLP classification must be confirmed before Work IQ automation is allowed. Not yet tenant-verified.\",\n167:             \"com_licensing_cost_gate\": \"Work IQ licensing SKU is not confirmed for this tenant; assumed to require a premium SK series. Pending tenant verification.\",\n168:             \"com_lifecycle_alm_path\": \"Work IQ automation artifacts do not have a confirmed Dataverse-solution-aware ALM path aligned with the CouncilOfMinionsMVP solution; ALM story is assumed unverified.\",\n169:             \"com_contract_gaps\": \"Gap: Work IQ is not provisioned in the tenant and projects no append-only receipt ledger semantics, so it cannot drive receipt-backed Council workflow automation in the MVP.\",\n170:             \"com_decision\": \"defer\",\n171:             \"com_review_reference\": \"Defer until Work IQ is provisioned in the tenant and its receipt-ledger alignment is tested.\"\n172:           }\n173:         ]\n174:       }\n175:     ],\n176:     \"customServiceProposals\": [\n177:       {\n178:         \"proposalId\": \"CSP-LOCAL-001\",\n179:         \"com_name\": \"Custom service proposal - Council Receipt Ledger projection\",\n180:         \"com_council_capability\": \"memory-and-graph-grounding\",\n181:         \"addressesGapInRow\": \"PE-LOCAL-EVAL-001-ROW-02\",\n182:         \"gapCitation\": \"Cites the recorded contract gap in evaluation row PE-LOCAL-EVAL-001-ROW-02 (Dataverse intelligence/MCP, decision custom_gap_build): Dataverse MCP exposes generic table-row CRUD semantics but projects no append-only receipt ledger view keyed by com_idempotency_key with com_before_state/com_after_state lineage, and no meaning-graph entity/edge projection matching the com_councilgraphentity/com_councilgraphedge contracts. The custom Council Receipt Ledger projection fills exactly this Microsoft-native gap.\",\n183:         \"tenantConstraintCited\": \"Respects the tenant decision in tenant-decision-packet.json to defer Fabric IQ/Graph to phase 2 (fabricIqGraphPhase2=defer_to_phase_2), so the projection must be Dataverse-native rather than Fabric-resident for the MVP.\",\n184:         \"decisionReceipt\": \"CR-LOCAL-PE-001\",\n185:         \"implementationArtifactsReferenced\": [],\n186:         \"proposalRationale\": \"Because Dataverse intelligence/MCP does not natively project an append-only receipt ledger or the semantic graph, and Fabric is tenant-deferred, a Dataverse-native custom projection of the com_councilreceipt and com_councilgraphentity/com_councilgraphedge contracts is required. The decision to propose this custom service is recorded as receipt CR-LOCAL-PE-001 before any implementation; no implementation artifacts are referenced in this slice. Any implementation is receipt-gated and deferred to a later epic.\"\n187:       }\n188:     ],\n189:     \"receipts\": [\n190:       {\n191:         \"com_receipt_id\": \"CR-LOCAL-PE-001\",\n192:         \"com_verb\": \"proposed\",\n193:         \"com_actor_type\": \"human\",\n194:         \"com_actor_id\": \"Doug\",\n195:         \"com_authority_basis\": \"local non-tenant Story 5.3 platform-fit authority; Doug is the human approval owner per tenant-decision-packet.json\",\n196:         \"com_occurred_at\": \"2026-07-14T10:00:00-04:00\",\n197:         \"com_idempotency_key\": \"platform-eval:custom-proposal:CSP-LOCAL-001:2026-07-14\",\n198:         \"com_before_state\": \"no custom-service proposal recorded for the memory-and-graph-grounding capability gap\",\n199:         \"com_after_state\": \"custom-service proposal CSP-LOCAL-001 recorded citing Microsoft-native gap PE-LOCAL-EVAL-001-ROW-02 (Dataverse intelligence/MCP custom_gap_build); implementation deferred and receipt-gated\",\n200:         \"com_evidence_refs\": \"customServiceProposals[CSP-LOCAL-001]; evaluations[PE-LOCAL-EVAL-001].candidateRows[PE-LOCAL-EVAL-001-ROW-02]\",\n201:         \"com_decision_rationale\": \"Microsoft-native planes were evaluated first; Dataverse intelligence/MCP was the strongest native fit but projects no append-only receipt ledger or meaning-graph view, so a custom Dataverse-native projection is proposed to fill that gap. The decision is recorded before any implementation; no implementation artifacts are referenced.\",\n202:         \"com_confidence\": 0.8,\n203:         \"com_result\": \"accepted\",\n204:         \"com_policy_flags\": \"local_contract_evidence_only; no_tenant_write; no_outbound_action; decision_recorded_before_implementation\",\n205:         \"com_append_only_locked\": true\n206:       },\n207:       {\n208:         \"com_receipt_id\": \"CR-LOCAL-PE-002\",\n209:         \"com_verb\": \"reviewed\",\n210:         \"com_actor_type\": \"human\",\n211:         \"com_actor_id\": \"Doug\",\n212:         \"com_authority_basis\": \"local non-tenant Story 5.3 platform-fit authority; Doug is the human approval owner per tenant-decision-packet.json\",\n213:         \"com_occurred_at\": \"2026-07-14T09:00:00-04:00\",\n214:         \"com_idempotency_key\": \"platform-eval:capability:memory-and-graph-grounding:2026-07-14\",\n215:         \"com_before_state\": \"memory-and-graph-grounding capability not yet evaluated against the Microsoft candidate universe\",\n216:         \"com_after_state\": \"memory-and-graph-grounding evaluated against Work IQ (defer), Dataverse intelligence/MCP (custom_gap_build), Fabric IQ/Graph (defer), Fabric data agents (reject); custom proposal CSP-LOCAL-001 cites the Dataverse MCP gap\",\n217:         \"com_evidence_refs\": \"evaluations[PE-LOCAL-EVAL-001]; customServiceProposals[CSP-LOCAL-001]\",\n218:         \"com_decision_rationale\": \"Four Microsoft candidates were reviewed for memory-and-graph grounding; none fully projects the receipt ledger or semantic graph natively, so Dataverse intelligence/MCP is the strongest partial fit and a custom gap build is recorded for the missing projection.\",\n219:         \"com_confidence\": 0.8,\n220:         \"com_result\": \"accepted\",\n221:         \"com_policy_flags\": \"local_contract_evidence_only; no_tenant_write; no_outbound_action\",\n222:         \"com_append_only_locked\": true\n223:       },\n224:       {\n225:         \"com_receipt_id\": \"CR-LOCAL-PE-003\",\n226:         \"com_verb\": \"reviewed\",\n227:         \"com_actor_type\": \"human\",\n228:         \"com_actor_id\": \"Doug\",\n229:         \"com_authority_basis\": \"local non-tenant Story 5.3 platform-fit authority; Doug is the human approval owner per tenant-decision-packet.json\",\n230:         \"com_occurred_at\": \"2026-07-14T09:30:00-04:00\",\n231:         \"com_idempotency_key\": \"platform-eval:capability:workflow-automation:2026-07-14\",\n232:         \"com_before_state\": \"workflow-automation capability not yet evaluated against the Microsoft candidate universe\",\n233:         \"com_after_state\": \"workflow-automation evaluated against Power Automate (adopt), Copilot Studio (defer), Power Apps MCP agent feed (defer), Work IQ (defer); Power Automate adopted as the execution surface under noFlowPublish\",\n234:         \"com_evidence_refs\": \"evaluations[PE-LOCAL-EVAL-002]\",\n235:         \"com_decision_rationale\": \"Four Microsoft candidates were reviewed for workflow automation; Power Automate is adopted as the receipt-backed execution surface, while the generative-agent and Work IQ paths are deferred under the existing tenant guards.\",\n236:         \"com_confidence\": 0.8,\n237:         \"com_result\": \"accepted\",\n238:         \"com_policy_flags\": \"local_contract_evidence_only; no_tenant_write; no_outbound_action\",\n239:         \"com_append_only_locked\": true\n240:       }\n241:     ],\n242:     \"deferredWrites\": [\n243:       {\n244:         \"record\": \"com_councilplatformevaluation rows for PE-LOCAL-EVAL-001\",\n245:         \"deferredUpdate\": \"Persisting the four evaluation rows for the memory-and-graph-grounding capability to the live com_councilplatformevaluation table is a receipt-backed mutation gated to a later epic; no live tenant write was performed in this slice.\"\n246:       },\n247:       {\n248:         \"record\": \"com_councilplatformevaluation rows for PE-LOCAL-EVAL-002\",\n249:         \"deferredUpdate\": \"Persisting the four evaluation rows for the workflow-automation capability to the live com_councilplatformevaluation table is a receipt-backed mutation gated to a later epic; no live tenant write was performed in this slice.\"\n250:       },\n251:       {\n252:         \"record\": \"custom service proposal CSP-LOCAL-001 implementation\",\n253:         \"deferredUpdate\": \"Implementing the Council Receipt Ledger projection proposed by CSP-LOCAL-001 is gated to a later epic and requires a separate implementation receipt before any code or Dataverse artifact is created; no implementation artifacts are referenced in this slice and no live tenant write was performed.\"\n254:       }\n255:     ]\n256:   },\n257:   \"acceptanceMapping\": [\n258:     {\n259:       \"acceptanceCriterion\": 1,\n260:       \"localEvidence\": [\n261:         \"platformEvaluationRun.evaluations contains two capability evaluations (PE-LOCAL-EVAL-001 memory-and-graph-grounding, PE-LOCAL-EVAL-002 workflow-automation), each with four candidate rows drawn from the named candidateUniverse\",\n262:         \"Each candidate row carries the manifest com_councilplatformevaluation fields: com_name, com_council_capability, com_microsoft_candidate, com_official_source_date_checked, com_tenant_gate, com_permission_dlp_impact, com_licensing_cost_gate, com_lifecycle_alm_path, com_contract_gaps, com_decision, com_review_reference\",\n263:         \"Candidate coverage is >=4 per evaluation and every candidate is a member of candidateUniverse; no candidate outside the named set is admitted\"\n264:       ],\n265:       \"tenantEvidenceRequired\": \"Tenant gates, DLP classifications, and licensing SKUs recorded in each row are pending tenant verification; live confirmation of Work IQ / Copilot Studio / Power Apps MCP agent feed provisioning and entitlements remains VERIFY IN TENANT.\"\n266:     },\n267:     {\n268:       \"acceptanceCriterion\": 2,\n269:       \"localEvidence\": [\n270:         \"platformEvaluationRun.customServiceProposals contains exactly one proposal (CSP-LOCAL-001) whose addressesGapInRow points to a recorded gap in evaluation row PE-LOCAL-EVAL-001-ROW-02 (Dataverse intelligence/MCP, com_decision custom_gap_build)\",\n271:         \"The proposal cites both a specific Microsoft-native contract gap (gapCitation quoting the row's com_contract_gaps) and a tenant constraint (tenantConstraintCited quoting tenant-decision-packet.json fabricIqGraphPhase2=defer_to_phase_2)\",\n272:         \"The proposal's decision is recorded as append-only receipt CR-LOCAL-PE-001 (verb proposed) BEFORE any implementation; implementationArtifactsReferenced is empty and no implementation marker appears in the slice\",\n273:         \"guards.noImplementationArtifactsReferenced=true and guards.decisionsRecordedBeforeImplementation=true; all would-be live writes appear only in deferredWrites as receipt-gated entries\"\n274:       ],\n275:       \"tenantEvidenceRequired\": \"Building the custom Council Receipt Ledger projection and persisting evaluation rows to the live com_councilplatformevaluation table are receipt-gated to a later epic and remain VERIFY IN TENANT; this slice is local contract evidence only.\"\n276:     }\n277:   ]\n278: }\n\n(End of file - total 278 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\n  \"artifa