rovalOwner.\"","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/doug/.ringer/work/bmad-hybrid/5-3-record-microsoft-platform-evaluation-evidence/_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/platform-evaluation-slice.json","text":"{\n  \"artifactVersion\": \"2026-07-14\",\n  \"storyKey\": \"5-3-record-microsoft-platform-evaluation-evidence\",\n  \"status\": \"local-contract-not-tenant-verified\",\n  \"purpose\": \"Prove that Microsoft-native planes are evaluated before any custom substrate is approved, and that every custom-service proposal cites the specific Microsoft-native gap or tenant constraint it fills. Two capability evaluations each weigh at least four named Microsoft candidates against tenant gates, permission/DLP impact, licensing/cost, ALM path, contract gaps, decision, and a review reference. One custom-service proposal cites a recorded gap in an evaluation row, and its decision is recorded as an append-only receipt BEFORE any implementation; no implementation artifacts are referenced and no live Dataverse write is performed. Every would-be live write appears only as a deferred, receipt-gated entry.\",\n  \"guards\": {\n    \"noTenantWrites\": true,\n    \"noOutboundAction\": true,\n    \"noApprovalExecution\": true,\n    \"requiresExplicitHumanApprovalForExecution\": true,\n    \"microsoftNativeEvaluatedBeforeCustomSubstrate\": true,\n    \"customServicesMustCiteMicrosoftGap\": true,\n    \"decisionsRecordedBeforeImplementation\": true,\n    \"receiptsAreLocalContractEvidenceOnly\": true,\n    \"noImplementationArtifactsReferenced\": true\n  },\n  \"assumptions\": [\n    \"Microsoft product capability statements reflect public documentation as of 2026-07-07 (microsoft-platform-fit-matrix-2026-07-07.md contract date); tenant-specific gates, license SKUs, and DLP classifications are recorded as pending tenant verification, not as verified tenant facts.\",\n    \"The named candidate universe (Work IQ, Dataverse intelligence/MCP, Power Apps MCP 