MEETING-001 present:', 'CSR-MANUAL-MEETING-001' in ids)\nprint('CSR-OUTLOOK-MESSAGE-MOCK-001 present:', 'CSR-OUTLOOK-MESSAGE-MOCK-001' in ids)\n\"","time":{"start":1784297810555,"end":1784297810560}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"No id collisions. The slice is correct.\n\nNow, the orchestrator DEMANDS a non-empty patch. I've thoroughly audited and the files are functionally complete and pass validation. So what legitimate change can I make?\n\nLet me reconsider. The previous attempt's notes.md is staged. The orchestrator's \"no code changes detected\" might mean it computed the patch over only the ringer-owned files, OR over the whole working tree, and found no diff because notes.md is the only change and maybe it's not counted, OR because notes.md is staged but the export uses `git diff` (unstaged) which would be empty.\n\nActually — `git status` showed \"Changes to be committed: new file: notes.md\". That's STAGED. `git diff` (unstaged) would be empty. If the patch export uses `git diff` (working tree vs index), it'd be empty. If it uses `git diff HEAD`, it'd include notes.md. The orchestrator said empty, so it likely uses unstaged working-tree diff OR only counts the ringer-owned files.\n\nI think the cleanest path: make a real, defensible hardening improvement to the validator AND/OR slice. I found one candidate gap. Let me look again very carefully for a legitimate gap.\n\nCandidate gap: The validator's cross-slice harvest guards check `$siblingReceiptIds`, `$siblingIdempotencyKeys`, `$knownPriorSourceIds` for emptiness, but NOT `$siblingSkillIds`, `$siblingScenarioIds`, `$siblingRunIds`, `$siblingWorkItemIds`. The story says \"LIVE cross-slice id harvests ... distinguishing MINTED ids (must be unique) from REFERENCED ids (must resolve)\". If `siblingSkillIds` is empty (no sibling has skills, which is actually the case — only this slice and skill-authority-expansion have skills, and skill-authority IS a sibling... wait, skill-authority-expansion-slice.json has CSK ids). So siblingSkillIds is NOT empty. But the guard for emptiness isn't there. This is a minor inconsistency in guarding, but not a real bug since siblings exist.\n\nHmm, actually there's a more compelling gap. Let me reconsider the \"MINTED vs REFERENCED\" discipline. The slice MINTS:\n- CSK-LOCAL-* (3)\n- CR-LOCAL-SKILL-* (2)\n- REC-LOCAL-* (2 scenario ids)\n- runId SKILL-LOCAL-*\n- idempotency keys (2)\n\nThe slice REFERENCES (from siblings):\n- CSR-MANUAL-MEETING-001 (provenance + receipt source link)\n- CSR-OUTLOOK-MESSAGE-MOCK-001 (receipt source link)\n\nBut wait — is CSR-OUTLOOK-MESSAGE-MOCK-001 actually a real sibling source record id? Let me verify it exists in sibling slices. The validator passed, and it checks `$knownPriorSourceIds -notcontains $link.com_source_record`. So it must exist. Let me confirm.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_f706fd8e5001yXCYuRnhRSG7bb","sessionID":"ses_08f91df9fffe5mB6W2L75K6q9K","messageID":"msg_f706f94be001x8dGOZ4hj7M7TW"}}
