{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1784297884442,"sessionID":"ses_08f91df9fffe5mB6W2L75K6q9K","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_51a838d668bf49d0a40de8be","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/doug/.ringer/work/bmad-hybrid/5-1-maintain-the-minion-skill-registry/_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/skill-registry-slice-validate.ps1","newString":"if ($knownPriorSourceIds.Count -eq 0) {\n  Add-Issue $issues \"No Source Record IDs could be harvested from sibling slices; provenance / receipt-source-link checks would silently no-op.\"\n}\nif ($siblingReceiptIds.Count -eq 0) {\n  Add-Issue $issues \"No Receipt IDs could be harvested from sibling slices; receipt collision checks would silently no-op.\"\n}\nif ($siblingIdempotencyKeys.Count -eq 0) {\n  Add-Issue $issues \"No idempotency keys could be harvested from sibling slices; key collision checks would silently no-op.\"\n}\n# The remaining harvested collections back MINTED-id uniqueness checks\n# (skills / scenarios / runIds). Without these guards a removed sibling would\n# let those collision checks pass without flagging — a skippable mandatory\n# check, which the Story 5.1 hardening bar forbids. They mirror the three\n# guards above so every harvested collection used downstream is either\n# populated or explicitly fails the run.\nif ($siblingSkillIds.Count -eq 0) {\n  Add-Issue $issues \"No Council Skill IDs could be harvested from sibling slices; minted skill id collision checks would silently no-op.\"\n}\nif ($siblingScenarioIds.Count -eq 0) {\n  Add-Issue $issues \"No recommendation scenario IDs could be harvested from sibling slices; minted scenario id collision checks would silently no-op.\"\n}\nif ($siblingRunIds.Count -eq 0) {\n  Add-Issue $issues \"No run IDs could be harvested from sibling slices; minted runId collision checks would silently no-op.\"\n}","oldString":"if ($knownPriorSourceIds.Count -eq 0) {\n  Add-Issue $issues \"No Source Record IDs could be harvested from sibling slices; provenance / receipt-source-link checks would silently no-op.\"\n}\nif ($siblingReceiptIds.Count -eq 0) {\n  Add-Issue $issues \"No Receipt IDs could be harvested from sibling slices; receipt collision checks would silently no-op.\"\n}\nif ($siblingIdempotencyKeys.Count -eq 0) {\n  Add-Issue $issues \"No idempotency keys could be harvested from sibling slices; key collision checks would silently no-op.\"\n}"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /home/doug/.ringer/work/bmad-hybrid/5-1-maintain-the-minion-skill-registry/_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/skill-registry-slice-validate.ps1\n===================================================================\n--- /home/doug/.ringer/work/bmad-hybrid/5-1-maintain-the-minion-skill-registry/_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/skill-registry-slice-validate.ps1\n+++ /home/doug/.ringer/work/bmad-hybrid/5-1-maintain-the-minion-skill-registry/_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/skill-registry-slice-validate.ps1\n@@ -302,8 +302,23 @@\n }\n if ($siblingIdempotencyKeys.Count -eq 0) {\n   Add-Issue $issues \"No idempotency keys could be harvested from sibling slices; key collision checks would silently no-op.\"\n }\n+# The remaining harvested collections back MINTED-id uniqueness checks\n+# (skills / scenarios / runIds). Without these guards a removed sibling would\n+# let those collision checks pass without flagging — a skippable mandatory\n+# check, which the Story 5.1 hardening bar forbids. They mirror the three\n+# guards above so every harvested collection used downstream is either\n+# populated or explicitly fails the run.\n+if ($siblingSkillIds.Count -eq 0) {\n+  Add-Issue $issues \"No Council Skill IDs could be harvested from sibling slices; minted skill id collision checks would silently no-op.\"\n+}\n+if ($siblingScenarioIds.Count -eq 0) {\n+  Add-Issue $issues \"No recommendation scenario IDs could be harvested from sibling slices; minted scenario id collision checks would silently no-op.\"\n+}\n+if ($siblingRunIds.Count -eq 0) {\n+  Add-Issue $issues \"No run IDs could be harvested from sibling slices; minted runId collision checks would silently no-op.\"\n+}\n \n $run = $slice.skillRegistryRun\n if ($null -eq $run) {\n   Add-Issue $issues \"Slice must carry a skillRegistryRun block.\"\n","filediff":{"file":"/home/doug/.ringer/work/bmad-hybrid/5-1-maintain-the-minion-skill-registry/_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/skill-registry-slice-validate.ps1","patch":"Index: /home/doug/.ringer/work/bmad-hybrid/5-1-maintain-the-minion-skill-registry/_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/skill-registry-slice-validate.ps1\n===================================================================\n--- /home/doug/.ringer/work/bmad-hybrid/5-1-maintain-the-minion-skill-registry/_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/skill-registry-slice-validate.ps1\n+++ /home/doug/.ringer/work/bmad-hybrid/5-1-maintain-the-minion-skill-registry/_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/skill-registry-slice-validate.ps1\n@@ -302,8 +302,23 @@\n }\n if ($siblingIdempotencyKeys.Count -eq 0) {\n   Add-Issue $issues \"No idempotency keys could be harvested from sibling slices; key collision checks would silently no-op.\"\n }\n+# The remaining harvested collections back MINTED-id uniqueness checks\n+# (skills / scenarios / runIds). Without these guards a removed sibling would\n+# let those collision checks pass without flagging — a skippable mandatory\n+# check, which the Story 5.1 hardening bar forbids. They mirror the three\n+# guards above so every harvested collection used downstream is either\n+# populated or explicitly fails the run.\n+if ($siblingSkillIds.Count -eq 0) {\n+  Add-Issue $issues \"No Council Skill IDs could be harvested from sibling slices; minted skill id collision checks would silently no-op.\"\n+}\n+if ($siblingScenarioIds.Count -eq 0) {\n+  Add-Issue $issues \"No recommendation scenario IDs could be harvested from sibling slices; minted scenario id collision checks would silently no-op.\"\n+}\n+if ($siblingRunIds.Count -eq 0) {\n+  Add-Issue $issues \"No run IDs could be harvested from sibling slices; minted runId collision checks would silently no-op.\"\n+}\n \n $run = $slice.skillRegistryRun\n if ($null -eq $run) {\n   Add-Issue $issues \"Slice must carry a skillRegistryRun block.\"\n","additions":15,"deletions":0},"truncated":false},"title":"_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/skill-registry-slice-validate.ps1","time":{"start":1784297884430,"end":1784297884435}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"So:\n- `$siblingWorkItemIds` — harvested but NEVER used. Dead. This slice has no work items (com_work_item is null), so there's no minted CWI-LOCAL-* to check for collision and no referenced CWI to check for resolution. The harvest is wasted but harmless. A review swarm might flag it as \"harvested but unused → either use it or remove it.\" But removing it reduces coverage intent. Actually since this slice has no work items, there's nothing to check. Keeping it is harmless. But it's a minor smell.\n\n- `$siblingSkillIds` — used at line 406 (minted collision). Guarded? No emptiness guard. \n- `$siblingScenarioIds` — used at line 490 (minted collision). Guarded? No.\n- `$siblingRunIds` — used at line 319 (minted collision). Guarded? No.\n\nSo three collections are USED for minted-collision checks but have NO emptiness guard, while the three parallel collections (receipts, keys, sourceRecords) DO have emptiness guards. This is the inconsistency. Adding guards closes the \"skippable mandatory check\" gap for minted-id uniqueness.\n\nThis is a clean, defensible hardening fix. Let me make it.\n\nLet me also reconsider: should I touch the slice JSON at all? The slice is correct; I shouldn't introduce fabricated changes. I'll only touch the validator. But the story says deliverables are exactly the two files; modifying only one is fine.\n\nWait — but will a validator-only change produce a non-empty patch? Yes — modifying the .ps1 file creates a diff vs HEAD. That's the patch the orchestrator wants. And it's a legitimate hardening improvement consistent with the story's hardening bar.\n\nLet me also verify the corrupted-slice FAIL requirement by running a corruption test after my change. And ensure the happy path still passes.\n\nLet me implement the guard additions. I'll add after the existing guards (lines 297-305) three more guards for skill/scenario/runId harvests. I'll model them on the existing style.\n\nActually, let me reconsider the message wording. The existing guards say \"No X could be harvested from sibling slices; Y checks would silently no-op.\" I'll mirror that.\n\nLet me write the edit.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_f7070eeb90011ay9jyqiijBksk","sessionID":"ses_08f91df9fffe5mB6W2L75K6q9K","messageID":"msg_f7070b445001lMDXehcMJVFajn"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1784297884443,"sessionID":"ses_08f91df9fffe5mB6W2L75K6q9K","part":{"id":"prt_f7070e5b0001Awv8I0QBNI0M5r","messageID":"msg_f7070b445001lMDXehcMJVFajn","sessionID":"ses_08f91df9fffe5mB6W2L75K6q9K","type":"text","text":"I found a real hardening gap. The validator guards three of its six cross-slice harvested id collections against silent no-op (receipts, idempotency keys, source records — lines 297-305), but the three collections used for **minted-id uniqueness** checks (skills, scenarios, runIds) have no such guard. If a skill-bearing sibling slice were ever removed, those collision checks would silently pass without flagging — exactly the \"skippable mandatory check\" the story's hardening bar forbids. I'll add the missing guards, mirroring the existing pattern.","time":{"start":1784297874865,"end":1784297884439}}}
