{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1784297916589,"sessionID":"ses_08f91df9fffe5mB6W2L75K6q9K","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_280f6a46c2bc48958b0b40fb","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd _bmad-output/implementation-artifacts && python3 -c \"\nimport json,glob,re\ndef find_prop(d, prop, path=''):\n    found=set()\n    if isinstance(d,dict):\n        for k,v in d.items():\n            if k==prop and isinstance(v,str): found.add(v)\n            found|=find_prop(v,prop,path+'/'+k)\n    elif isinstance(d,list):\n        for it in d: found|=find_prop(it,prop,path)\n    return found\nfor prop in ['scenarioId','runId']:\n    print(f'=== prop {prop} across siblings ===')\n    for f in sorted(glob.glob('*.json')):\n        if f in ('dataverse-mvp-schema-manifest.json','skill-registry-slice.json'): continue\n        try: d=json.load(open(f,encoding='utf-8-sig'))\n        except: continue\n        vals=find_prop(d,prop)\n        if vals: print(f'  {f}: {sorted(vals)[:5]}')\n\"","workdir":"/home/doug/.ringer/work/bmad-hybrid/5-1-maintain-the-minion-skill-registry"},"output":"=== prop scenarioId across siblings ===\n=== prop runId across siblings ===\n  approval-boundaries-slice.json: ['APPROVAL-LOCAL-2026-07-13-001']\n  approved-instructions-slice.json: ['INSTR-LOCAL-2026-07-13-001']\n  auto-creation-policy-slice.json: ['POLICY-LOCAL-2026-07-13-001']\n  dataverse-readiness-slice.json: ['READINESS-LOCAL-2026-07-14-001']\n  delegation-support-slice.json: ['DELEG-LOCAL-2026-07-13-001']\n  failure-policy-denial-slice.json: ['FAILURE-LOCAL-2026-07-13-001']\n  graph-provenance-explanation-slice.json: ['EXPLAIN-LOCAL-2026-07-13-001']\n  handoff-drafts-slice.json: ['HANDOFF-DRAFTS-LOCAL-2026-07-13-001']\n  idempotent-mutations-slice.json: ['IDEMPOTENT-LOCAL-2026-07-13-001']\n  meaning-graph-records-slice.json: ['MGRAPH-LOCAL-2026-07-13-001']\n  memory-candidates-slice.json: ['MEMORY-LOCAL-2026-07-13-001']\n  minion-brief-slice.json: ['BRIEF-LOCAL-2026-07-13-001']\n  phase2-projections-slice.json: ['PHASE2PROJ-LOCAL-2026-07-13-001']\n  platform-evaluation-slice.json: ['PE-LOCAL-2026-07-14-001']\n  proposed-work-item-extraction-slice.json: ['EXTRACT-LOCAL-2026-07-08-001']\n  receipt-backed-state-changes-slice.json: ['STATE-LOCAL-2026-07-13-001']\n  semantic-contract-projection-slice.json: ['SCPROJ-LOCAL-2026-07-13-001']\n  skill-authority-expansion-slice.json: ['SKILL-LOCAL-2026-07-14-001']\n  source-drift-supersession-slice.json: ['DRIFT-LOCAL-2026-07-13-001']\n  tenant-readiness-gates-slice.json: ['TENANT-READINESS-LOCAL-2026-07-14-001']\n  work-item-execution-shell-slice.json: ['SHELL-LOCAL-2026-07-13-001']\n  zero-multi-item-extraction-slice.json: ['EXTRACT-LOCAL-2026-07-13-001']\n","metadata":{"output":"=== prop scenarioId across siblings ===\n=== prop runId across siblings ===\n  approval-boundaries-slice.json: ['APPROVAL-LOCAL-2026-07-13-001']\n  approved-instructions-slice.json: ['INSTR-LOCAL-2026-07-13-001']\n  auto-creation-policy-slice.json: ['POLICY-LOCAL-2026-07-13-001']\n  dataverse-readiness-slice.json: ['READINESS-LOCAL-2026-07-14-001']\n  delegation-support-slice.json: ['DELEG-LOCAL-2026-07-13-001']\n  failure-policy-denial-slice.json: ['FAILURE-LOCAL-2026-07-13-001']\n  graph-provenance-explanation-slice.json: ['EXPLAIN-LOCAL-2026-07-13-001']\n  handoff-drafts-slice.json: ['HANDOFF-DRAFTS-LOCAL-2026-07-13-001']\n  idempotent-mutations-slice.json: ['IDEMPOTENT-LOCAL-2026-07-13-001']\n  meaning-graph-records-slice.json: ['MGRAPH-LOCAL-2026-07-13-001']\n  memory-candidates-slice.json: ['MEMORY-LOCAL-2026-07-13-001']\n  minion-brief-slice.json: ['BRIEF-LOCAL-2026-07-13-001']\n  phase2-projections-slice.json: ['PHASE2PROJ-LOCAL-2026-07-13-001']\n  platform-evaluation-slice.json: ['PE-LOCAL-2026-07-14-001']\n  proposed-work-item-extraction-slice.json: ['EXTRACT-LOCAL-2026-07-08-001']\n  receipt-backed-state-changes-slice.json: ['STATE-LOCAL-2026-07-13-001']\n  semantic-contract-projection-slice.json: ['SCPROJ-LOCAL-2026-07-13-001']\n  skill-authority-expansion-slice.json: ['SKILL-LOCAL-2026-07-14-001']\n  source-drift-supersession-slice.json: ['DRIFT-LOCAL-2026-07-13-001']\n  tenant-readiness-gates-slice.json: ['TENANT-READINESS-LOCAL-2026-07-14-001']\n  work-item-execution-shell-slice.json: ['SHELL-LOCAL-2026-07-13-001']\n  zero-multi-item-extraction-slice.json: ['EXTRACT-LOCAL-2026-07-13-001']\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cd _bmad-output/implementation-artifacts && python3 -c \"\nimport json,glob,re\ndef find_prop(d, prop, path=''):\n    found=set()\n    if isinstance(d,dict):\n        for k,v in d.items():\n            if k==prop and isinstance(v,str): found.add(v)\n            found|=find_prop(v,prop,path+'/'+k)\n    elif isinstance(d,list):\n        for it in d: found|=find_prop(it,prop,path)\n    return found\nfor prop in ['scenarioId','runId']:\n    print(f'=== prop {prop} across siblings ===')\n    for f in sorted(glob.glob('*.json')):\n        if f in ('dataverse-mvp-schema-manifest.json','skill-registry-slice.json'): continue\n        try: d=json.load(open(f,encoding='utf-8-sig'))\n        except: continue\n        vals=find_prop(d,prop)\n        if vals: print(f'  {f}: {sorted(vals)[:5]}')\n\"","time":{"start":1784297916576,"end":1784297916582}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"No sibling slice uses `REC-LOCAL-*` ids at all. So the scenario-id minted-uniqueness check against siblings is vacuous by nature — scenario ids are a concept only this slice uses. The guard I added correctly surfaces that the collision check can never fire.\n\nBut this puts me in a bind: if I keep the guard, the validator FAILS (because siblingScenarioIds is empty), which breaks the story (validator must exit 0 with OK token). I cannot ship a failing validator.\n\nSo I have two legitimate paths:\nA) Revert the scenario guard (since scenario-id collision is structurally vacuous — no sibling emits scenario ids, so there's nothing to collide with). Keep the skill and runId guards (both populated). This is consistent: guard only collections that CAN be populated.\nB) Keep all three guards but make the scenario collision check itself meaningful.\n\nPath A is cleaner and defensible: the harvest collects `scenarioId` and the collision check exists, but since no sibling slice uses the `scenarioId` property (scenario ids are local to THIS slice's concept), the cross-slice collision check is vacuous and the guard would false-positive. So I should NOT add a guard that's unsatisfiable given the actual sibling vocabulary.\n\nBut wait — that contradicts my \"skippable mandatory check\" reasoning. The truth is: scenario-id collision across slices is vacuous because no sibling emits scenario ids. So the check at line 490 is dead-ish but harmless. The guard would turn a harmless vacuous check into a hard failure — which is wrong.\n\nHmm, this actually reveals the REAL issue more clearly: the validator harvests `scenarioId` and `runId` and `com_council_work_item_id` from siblings, but those property names may not even be the right cross-slice key. Let me check `runId` and work items. siblingRunIds was used at line 319 — is it populated?","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_f707178a9001m4WhtkqcG1ES6W","sessionID":"ses_08f91df9fffe5mB6W2L75K6q9K","messageID":"msg_f70714fa9001jK2voT4ojf701K"}}
