{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1784297926764,"sessionID":"ses_08f910da3ffeUrS3w1SULaDIN4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_7d394656d2ec4a0aa9938b39","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/doug/.ringer/work/bmad-hybrid/5-2-approve-skill-authority-expansion/_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/skill-authority-expansion-slice-validate.ps1","newString":"  [string]$DemoEvidencePath = \"$PSScriptRoot\\state-transition-demo-evidence.json\",\n  [switch]$SkipCorruptionSelfTest\n)","oldString":"  [string]$DemoEvidencePath = \"$PSScriptRoot\\state-transition-demo-evidence.json\"\n)"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /home/doug/.ringer/work/bmad-hybrid/5-2-approve-skill-authority-expansion/_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/skill-authority-expansion-slice-validate.ps1\n===================================================================\n--- /home/doug/.ringer/work/bmad-hybrid/5-2-approve-skill-authority-expansion/_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/skill-authority-expansion-slice-validate.ps1\n+++ /home/doug/.ringer/work/bmad-hybrid/5-2-approve-skill-authority-expansion/_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/skill-authority-expansion-slice-validate.ps1\n@@ -4,9 +4,10 @@\n   [string]$ManualSlicePath = \"$PSScriptRoot\\manual-source-record-slice.json\",\n   [string]$OutlookSlicePath = \"$PSScriptRoot\\outlook-source-reference-slice.json\",\n   [string]$Story13ExtractionPath = \"$PSScriptRoot\\proposed-work-item-extraction-slice.json\",\n   [string]$Story14ExtractionPath = \"$PSScriptRoot\\zero-multi-item-extraction-slice.json\",\n-  [string]$DemoEvidencePath = \"$PSScriptRoot\\state-transition-demo-evidence.json\"\n+  [string]$DemoEvidencePath = \"$PSScriptRoot\\state-transition-demo-evidence.json\",\n+  [switch]$SkipCorruptionSelfTest\n )\n \n $ErrorActionPreference = \"Stop\"\n \n","filediff":{"file":"/home/doug/.ringer/work/bmad-hybrid/5-2-approve-skill-authority-expansion/_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/skill-authority-expansion-slice-validate.ps1","patch":"Index: /home/doug/.ringer/work/bmad-hybrid/5-2-approve-skill-authority-expansion/_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/skill-authority-expansion-slice-validate.ps1\n===================================================================\n--- /home/doug/.ringer/work/bmad-hybrid/5-2-approve-skill-authority-expansion/_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/skill-authority-expansion-slice-validate.ps1\n+++ /home/doug/.ringer/work/bmad-hybrid/5-2-approve-skill-authority-expansion/_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/skill-authority-expansion-slice-validate.ps1\n@@ -4,9 +4,10 @@\n   [string]$ManualSlicePath = \"$PSScriptRoot\\manual-source-record-slice.json\",\n   [string]$OutlookSlicePath = \"$PSScriptRoot\\outlook-source-reference-slice.json\",\n   [string]$Story13ExtractionPath = \"$PSScriptRoot\\proposed-work-item-extraction-slice.json\",\n   [string]$Story14ExtractionPath = \"$PSScriptRoot\\zero-multi-item-extraction-slice.json\",\n-  [string]$DemoEvidencePath = \"$PSScriptRoot\\state-transition-demo-evidence.json\"\n+  [string]$DemoEvidencePath = \"$PSScriptRoot\\state-transition-demo-evidence.json\",\n+  [switch]$SkipCorruptionSelfTest\n )\n \n $ErrorActionPreference = \"Stop\"\n \n","additions":2,"deletions":1},"truncated":false},"title":"_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/skill-authority-expansion-slice-validate.ps1","time":{"start":1784297926755,"end":1784297926761}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"No sibling validator has a corruption self-test either. So this is a genuine, spec-required gap across the epic, but I'm scoped only to 5-2's owned files. Adding the corruption self-test to 5-2's validator is in-scope and spec-required.\n\nLet me design the corruption self-test carefully so it:\n1. Makes a temp copy of the slice JSON.\n2. Mutates it in a way that should FAIL validation (e.g. flip the approval receipt's com_result to \"rejected\", or break the storyKey).\n3. Re-runs the validator logic against the temp copy and confirms it produces issues / non-zero exit.\n4. Cleans up the temp file.\n5. If the corrupted copy does NOT fail, add an issue (the self-test failed).\n\nBut re-running the whole validator recursively is tricky in PowerShell. A cleaner approach: the validator already has all its logic inline (not wrapped in a function), so I can't easily re-invoke it on a different slice path without refactoring.\n\nSimplest robust approach: invoke a child pwsh process running the same script with an env/param pointing at the corrupted copy, and assert the child exits non-zero. But the script doesn't take a \"corrupt mode\" param.\n\nAlternative: Use `Start-Process` or `& pwsh -File $PSCommandPath -SkillSlicePath <temp>` to re-run with the corrupted slice via the existing `-SkillSlicePath` parameter. The script already has `[string]$SkillSlicePath` as a param defaulting to `$PSScriptRoot\\skill-authority-expansion-slice.json`. So I can re-invoke the script with `-SkillSlicePath` pointing at a temp corrupted copy and check the exit code.\n\nBut there's a recursion concern: the child run would ALSO run the corruption self-test, creating infinite recursion. I need a guard param to skip the self-test in child invocations.\n\nLet me add a `-SkipCorruptionSelfTest` switch param. The self-test block, when run, invokes the script with `-SkipCorruptionSelfTest` and `-SkillSlicePath <temp>`, checks exit code, cleans up.\n\nThe self-test must run BEFORE the final OK token but AFTER all real checks. Actually, it should run as a final hardening step: if all real checks passed (issues empty), then verify a corrupted copy fails. If the corrupted copy does NOT fail, that's a critical hole — add an issue and fail.\n\nLet me place it right before the `if ($issues.Count -gt 0)` block, guarded by `-not $SkipCorruptionSelfTest`.\n\nDesign:\n- Create temp file in `$PSScriptRoot` (so sibling-slice harvest still works; actually the child uses $PSScriptRoot for siblings, which is fine — only the SkillSlicePath differs). Use a uniquely-named temp file that won't be harvested as a sibling (it's .json in $PSScriptRoot... wait, the sibling harvest globs ALL *.json in $PSScriptRoot except manifest and the skill slice. A temp .json would be picked up as a sibling! That would pollute the child's cross-slice harvest. But for the corruption test we only care that the child EXITS NON-ZERO, not about its specific issues. Still, pollution could cause false issues that aren't about the corruption. That's fine — we just need non-zero exit. But it could ALSO accidentally cause the child to pass if... no, the corruption itself (broken storyKey or flipped result) will cause issues regardless of sibling pollution.\n\nActually cleaner: put the temp file OUTSIDE $PSScriptRoot (e.g. in the system temp dir) so it's not harvested as a sibling. But then the child's `$PSScriptRoot`-relative sibling paths still resolve to the real folder. The child's `-SkillSlicePath` points to the temp file elsewhere. That works and avoids pollution. But `Read-JsonInput` and the path-existence check use the param, so fine. The sibling glob uses `$PSScriptRoot` which is the script's location (real folder) — unaffected by SkillSlicePath. Good.\n\nUse `$env:TEMP` / `[System.IO.Path]::GetTempPath()` for the temp file.\n\nMutation: flip the approval receipt's `com_result` from \"accepted\" to \"rejected\". That violates the approval-receipt result check (line 881) → issue → exit 1. Clean, targeted.\n\nLet me write it:\n\n```powershell\n# Corruption self-test (Story 5.2 hardening bar: \"Verify a corrupted slice copy\n# FAILS before finishing.\"). A corrupted copy of the slice must cause this\n# validator to exit non-zero; otherwise the validator is vacuously passing and\n# the review swarm's kill list fires. Runs only in the top-level invocation\n# (suppressed in the child re-run via -SkipCorruptionSelfTest) so there is no\n# recursion. Performed only when all real checks have already passed, so a\n# self-test failure is the only new failure mode.\nif (-not $SkipCorruptionSelfTest -and $issues.Count -eq 0) {\n  $tempDir = [System.IO.Path]::GetTempPath()\n  $tempSlice = [System.IO.Path]::Combine($tempDir, \"skill-authority-expansion-slice-corrupt-$([System.Guid]::NewGuid().ToString('N')).json\")\n  try {\n    $corrupt = $slice | ConvertTo-Json -Depth 20\n    $corruptObj = $corrupt | ConvertFrom-Json\n    $approvalToCorrupt = @($corruptObj.expansionRun.receipts | Where-Object { [string]$_.com_verb -eq \"approved\" }) | Select-Object -First 1\n    if ($null -ne $approvalToCorrupt) {\n      $approvalToCorrupt.com_result = \"rejected\"\n    }\n    else {\n      $corruptObj.storyKey = \"corrupted\"\n    }\n    $corruptObj | ConvertTo-Json -Depth 20 | Set-Content -LiteralPath $tempSlice -Encoding UTF8\n    $child = Start-Process -FilePath \"pwsh\" -ArgumentList @(\"-NoProfile\", \"-NonInteractive\", \"-File\", $PSCommandPath, \"-SkillSlicePath\", $tempSlice, \"-SkipCorruptionSelfTest\") -Wait -PassThru -WindowStyle Hidden -RedirectStandardOutput ([System.IO.Path]::Combine($tempDir, \"skill-corrupt-stdout-$([System.Guid]::NewGuid().ToString('N')).tmp\")) -RedirectStandardError ([System.IO.Path]::Combine($tempDir, \"skill-corrupt-stderr-$([System.Guid]::NewGuid().ToString('N')).tmp\"))\n    if ($child.ExitCode -eq 0) {\n      Add-Issue $issues \"Corruption self-test failed: a corrupted slice copy (approval receipt com_result flipped to rejected) exited 0 under this validator; the validator is vacuously passing and does not reject invalid input.\"\n    }\n  }\n  finally {\n    if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $tempSlice) { Remove-Item -LiteralPath $tempSlice -Force }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nWait, `Start-Process` with `-File` and `$PSCommandPath` — `$PSCommandPath` is the script path. Good. But I need to make sure `pwsh` is on PATH in the child. The validator is invoked via `pwsh -File ...` so pwsh is available. In the child, `pwsh` should resolve. To be safe, use the same pwsh that's running: `$PSCommandPath` and invoke via `& (Get-Process -Id $PID).Path`? Simpler: use `[System.Diagnostics.Process]`... actually `Start-Process pwsh` should work since the parent was launched with pwsh on PATH.\n\nHmm, but there's a subtlety: the child re-runs ALL checks including loading siblings from $PSScriptRoot. That's fine and fast. The child will fail on the corrupted approval result. Exit non-zero. Good.\n\nBut Start-Process redirect files need unique names; I generate them. Need to clean those up too. Let me also remove the redirect temp files in finally.\n\nAlso, `$PSCommandPath` in a script invoked with `-File` is the script path. Good.\n\nOne concern: the `param` block — adding `-SkipCorruptionSelfTest` as a switch. Let me add it.\n\nAlso need to be careful: when the child runs with the corrupted slice, the corruption is `com_result = \"rejected\"` on the approval receipt. The check at line 881 (`if ([string]$approval.com_result -ne \"accepted\")`) fires → issue → exit 1. Good. Also the approval-receipt count check still passes (1 approval receipt by verb). The result check fires. \n\nLet me also verify the child's sibling harvest isn't affected by the temp file being in temp dir (not $PSScriptRoot). Good — temp dir != $PSScriptRoot.\n\nNow, will this keep the validator passing on the REAL slice? Yes: real slice has no corruption, self-test runs, child with corrupted copy exits non-zero, no issue added, OK token prints. \n\nLet me implement. Add the switch param and the self-test block before the final issues check.\n\nActually, I realize I should double check: does `Start-Process` exist in pwsh / PowerShell Core? Yes, it's a built-in cmdlet. `-WindowStyle Hidden` is supported on Windows; on Linux it may not be. Let me avoid `-WindowStyle` for cross-platform safety (the validator runs on Linux per the ringer-check env). Use `-NoNewWindow`? That redirects to parent console. Better to just redirect stdout/stderr to files and not set window style.\n\nActually on Linux `Start-Process` supports `-RedirectStandardOutput` and `-RedirectStandardError` but requires both if either is set, and `-WindowStyle` is ignored/no-op. To be safe, omit `-WindowStyle`.\n\nLet me write the edit.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_f7071a516001jLfzwHhJAIbOGQ","sessionID":"ses_08f910da3ffeUrS3w1SULaDIN4","messageID":"msg_f7070926b001CesZxDosOd6DXP"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1784297926808,"sessionID":"ses_08f910da3ffeUrS3w1SULaDIN4","part":{"id":"prt_f70719912001i4MG4CUn3z5Vcz","messageID":"msg_f7070926b001CesZxDosOd6DXP","sessionID":"ses_08f910da3ffeUrS3w1SULaDIN4","type":"text","text":"The owned files are complete and pass at HEAD, but Ringer requires a non-empty code diff. There's a genuine spec-required gap: the hardening bar demands \"Verify a corrupted slice copy FAILS before finishing,\" and this validator has no corruption self-test. Adding it is in-scope, spec-required, keeps the validator passing, and produces a real diff. Let me also confirm the gold-standard sibling lacks it (it does), so this is a legitimate 5-2 strengthening, not a regression.","time":{"start":1784297920786,"end":1784297926804}}}
