{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1784298011740,"sessionID":"ses_08f91df9fffe5mB6W2L75K6q9K","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_1d9fb4c3d6734cbb8554c494","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/doug/.ringer/work/bmad-hybrid/5-1-maintain-the-minion-skill-registry/notes.md"},"output":"<path>/home/doug/.ringer/work/bmad-hybrid/5-1-maintain-the-minion-skill-registry/notes.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Story 5.1 — Maintain the Minion Skill Registry: worker notes\n2: \n3: ## Outcome\n4: The two ringer-owned deliverables were already present in the worktree,\n5: tracked in git and matching HEAD:\n6: \n7: - `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/skill-registry-slice.json`\n8: - `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/skill-registry-slice-validate.ps1`\n9: \n10: I verified they satisfy the story spec end-to-end (see verification below) and\n11: made **no edits** — the existing implementation is complete and correct. No\n12: git commit / branch / push was run, per the Ringer contract.\n13: \n14: ## What the slice proves\n15: - **3 Council Skill records** (`CSK-LOCAL-*`), minted in-slice:\n16:   - `CSK-LOCAL-DRIFT-SCAN-001` — `com_status=active`, authority `approved_automatic`\n17:   - `CSK-LOCAL-LEGACY-SUMMARIZE-001` — `com_status=deprecated`, authority `manual_only`\n18:   - `CSK-LOCAL-OUTBOUND-SEND-001` — `com_status=suspended`, authority `ask_before_use`\n19:   Each declares `com_trigger`, `com_allowed_context`, `com_required_inputs`,\n20:   `com_authority_class`, `com_approval_requirements`, `com_proof_owed`,\n21:   `com_update_policy`, `com_status`, plus provenance evidence/links.\n22: - **2 recommendation scenarios**, outcomes DERIVED from the skill record\n23:   (status + authority class), not self-asserted booleans:\n24:   - `REC-LOCAL-FLAG-001` → deprecated skill → `flagged`, backed by\n25:     `CR-LOCAL-SKILL-FLAG-001` (verb `held`, result `accepted`).\n26:   - `REC-LOCAL-PREVENT-001` → suspended skill → `prevented`, backed by\n27:     `CR-LOCAL-SKILL-PREVENT-001` (verb `policy_denied`, result `rejected`).\n28: \n29: ## Validator hardening (story \"Hardening bar\")\n30: All kill-list items are covered:\n31: \n32: - **No self-asserted booleans standing in for proof.** `decisionPolicyProof`\n33:   accumulates structural evidence (status coverage, outcome derivation,\n34:   receipt shape-matching, append-only, deferred-gate proof) and is checked\n35:   against every `decisionPolicy` boolean at the end: an asserted-but-unbacked\n36:   boolean fails (`skill-registry-slice-validate.ps1:906-918`).\n37: - **No hardcoded-id binding rules** — outcomes are discovered BY SHAPE over\n38:   collections (`flagReceipts` / `preventReceipts` via `Where-Object`,\n39:   `:720-747`), and each scenario's `outcomeReceipt` is bound by shape, not id\n40:   (`:749-791`). Coverage (exactly one active/deprecated/suspended; one\n41:   flag/prevent scenario) is derived, not counted (`:460-465`, `:571-594`).\n42: - **LIVE cross-slice id harvest from `$PSScriptRoot`** distinguishing MINTED\n43:   vs REFERENCED ids:\n44:   - `Invoke-CollectSiblingIds` walks EVERY co-located `*.json` (excluding the\n45:     manifest and this slice) and harvests work-item/receipt/idempotency/\n46:     source-record/skill/scenario/run ids into hashtables (`:108-182`,\n47:     `:284-293`).\n48:   - MINTED ids (`CSK-LOCAL-*`, `CR-LOCAL-SKILL-*`, `REC-LOCAL-*`, runId) must\n49:     be unique across all slices (`:406-408`, `:644-647`, `:490-492`, `:319-321`).\n50:   - REFERENCED ids (`CSR-*` in provenance / receipt-source-links / evidence\n51:     refs) must resolve to a known sibling Source Record (`:444-447`,\n52:     `:806-807`, `:700-710`).\n53: - **No conditional/skippable mandatory checks** — every guard, field, vocab\n54:   membership, and id-resolution check runs unconditionally over its\n55:   collection; `decisionPolicyProof` entries start `$true` and are AND-ed down\n56:   (so a silently-true default still requires the derived evidence to hold).\n57: - **Coverage derived, not counted** — `skillsByStatus`, `flagScenarios`,\n58:   `preventScenarios`, receipt-by-shape counts are all computed from records.\n59: - **Wrapped JSON loads** via `Read-JsonInput` (`:184-197`) with exit 1 on\n60:   malformed input. **TryParse** numeric checks for `com_confidence`\n61:   (`Test-ConfidenceInRange`, `:54-74`). **Strict booleans** for guards and\n62:   `com_append_only_locked` (`:267-271`, `:675-678`). **ISO 8601 with explicit\n63:   UTC offset** via `Test-IsoTimestamp` (`:76-106`). **`$PSScriptRoot`-relative\n64:   paths** in the `param` block (`:2-3`). Final token\n65:   `SKILL_REGISTRY_SLICE_VALIDATE_OK` + issue list + `exit 1` on any failure\n66:   (`:920-933`).\n67: - **Vocabulary discipline** — `com_status`, `com_authority_class`,\n68:   `com_verb`, `com_actor_type`, `com_result`, `com_evidence_role` all checked\n69:   against the manifest choice sets; required verbs/results/statuses/authorities\n70:   asserted present (`:229-253`).\n71: \n72: ## Verification commands\n73: ```bash\n74: export DOTNET_ROOT=$HOME/.dotnet\n75: export PATH=$HOME/.dotnet:$HOME/.dotnet/tools:$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH\n76: pwsh -File _bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/skill-registry-slice-validate.ps1\n77: # => prints SKILL_REGISTRY_SLICE_VALIDATE_OK, exit 0\n78: ```\n79: This is exactly the `ringer-check` line in the story spec.\n80: \n81: ## Corruption tests run (story: \"Verify a corrupted slice copy FAILS\")\n82: 1. **Status tamper** (deprecated→active): validator exits 1 with 9 issues\n83:    (duplicate active count, missing deprecated, derived-outcome mismatch,\n84:    authority-class inconsistency, three unbacked `decisionPolicy` booleans).\n85: 2. **Cross-slice receipt-id collision** (flag receipt → `CR-LOCAL-DRIFT-001`,\n86:    a sibling source-drift receipt): validator exits 1 flagging both the\n87:    `CR-LOCAL-SKILL-*` identity violation and the sibling collision, plus the\n88:    dangling acceptance-mapping id.\n89: \n90: Both confirm the hardening bar is met.\n91: \n92: ## Files read for conventions\n93: - `dataverse-mvp-schema-manifest.json` — authoritative vocabulary\n94:   (table `com_councilskill` columns, `com_recordstatus`, `com_authorityclass`,\n95:   `com_receiptverb`, `com_receiptresult`, `com_actortype`,\n96:   `com_councilreceiptsource.com_evidence_role`).\n97: - `source-drift-supersession-slice.json` / `-validate.ps1` (story 1-5) —\n98:   gold-standard slice + validator pair mirrored for structure, helpers\n99:   (`Add-Issue`, `Get-ChoiceValues`, `Test-HasNonEmptyField`,\n100:   `Test-ConfidenceInRange`, `Test-IsoTimestamp`, `Read-JsonInput`), guards,\n101:   receipt field sets, and the success-token/exit-1 convention.\n102: - `skill-authority-expansion-slice.json` (story 5-2) — sibling skill slice;\n103:   confirmed its `CSK-LOCAL-*` ids and `CR-LOCAL-SKILL-*` receipt ids do NOT\n104:   collide with the ids minted here (DRIFT-SCAN / LEGACY-SUMMARIZE /\n105:   OUTBOUND-SEND vs MEETING-DIGEST / FABRIC-PUBLISHER; FLAG/PREVENT vs\n106:   APPROVE/DENY).\n107: \n108: ## Assumptions / follow-ups\n109: - **Assumption:** the two deliverable files as already committed in HEAD are\n110:   the intended final state for this story; the Ringer check exports them as a\n111:   patch (no diff vs HEAD because they are already in-tree and correct). If\n112:   the orchestrator expected a fresh diff, the work is nonetheless complete\n113:   and verified — there was nothing to change.\n114: - **Assumption (carried from the slice's `receiptVerbPolicy` local\n115:   extension):** the manifest `com_receiptverb` has no skill-scoped flag/prevent\n116:   verb, so the slice reuses `held` (flag) and `policy_denied` (prevent), with\n117:   `com_result` + `com_before_state`/`com_after_state` disambiguating the\n118:   recommendation outcome from a Work Item state move. This is a documented\n119:   local extension; `guards.noWorkItemStateChangeInThisSlice` stays `true`.\n120: - **Follow-up (integrator, NOT this story):** wiring\n121:   `skill-registry-slice-validate.ps1` into `council-mvp-local-validate.ps1` is\n122:   the integrator's job after review (hard rule: do not edit\n123:   `council-mvp-local-validate.ps1`).\n124: - **Follow-up (Epic 2):** every live Council Skill row write and any\n125:   flag/prevent enforcement on the live recommendation path is recorded only in\n126:   `skillUpdatesDeferred` as receipt-gated to Epic 2 Story 2.3 — no live tenant\n127:   write exists in this slice.\n\n(End of file - total 127 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Story 5.1 — Maintain the Minion Skill Registry: worker notes\n\n## Outcome\nThe two ringer-owned deliverables were already present in the worktree,\ntracked in git and matching HEAD:\n\n- `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/skill-registry-slice.json`\n- `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/skill-registry-slice-validate.ps1`\n\nI verified they satisfy the story spec end-to-end (see verification below) and\nmade **no edits** — the existing implementation is complete and correct. No\ngit commit / branch / push was run, per the Ringer contract.\n\n## What the slice proves\n- **3 Council Skill records** (`CSK-LOCAL-*`), minted in-slice:\n  - `CSK-LOCAL-DRIFT-SCAN-001` — `com_status=active`, authority `approved_automatic`\n  - `CSK-LOCAL-LEGACY-SUMMARIZE-001` — `com_status=deprecated`, authority `manual_only`\n  - `CSK-LOCAL-OUTBOUND-SEND-001` — `com_status=suspended`, authority `ask_before_use`\n  Each declares `com_trigger`, `com_allowed_context`, `com_required_inputs`,\n  `com_authority_class`, `com_approval_requirements`, `com_proof_owed`,","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/doug/.ringer/work/bmad-hybrid/5-1-maintain-the-minion-skill-registry/notes.md","text":"# Story 5.1 — Maintain the Minion Skill Registry: worker notes\n\n## Outcome\nThe two ringer-owned deliverables were already present in the worktree,\ntracked in git and matching HEAD:\n\n- `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/skill-registry-slice.json`\n- `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/skill-registry-slice-validate.ps1`\n\nI verified they satisfy the story spec end-to-end (see verification below) and\nmade **no edits** — the existing implementation is complete and correct. No\ngit commit / branch / push was run, per the Ringer contract.\n\n## What the slice proves\n- **3 Council Skill records** (`CSK-LOCAL-*`), minted in-slice:\n  - `CSK-LOCAL-DRIFT-SCAN-001` — `com_status=active`, authority `approved_automatic`\n  - `CSK-LOCAL-LEGACY-SUMMARIZE-001` — `com_status=deprecated`, authority `manual_only`\n  - `CSK-LOCAL-OUTBOUND-SEND-001` — `com_status=suspended`, authority `ask_before_use`\n  Each declares `com_trigger`, `com_allowed_context`, `com_required_inputs`,\n  `com_authority_class`, `com_approval_requirements`, `com_proof_owed`,\n  `com_update_policy`, `com_status`, plus provenance evidence/links.\n- **2 recommendation scenarios**, outcomes DERIVED from the skill record\n  (status + authority class), not self-asserted booleans:\n  - `REC-LOCAL-FLAG-001` → deprecated skill → `flagged`, backed by\n    `CR-LOCAL-SKILL-FLAG-001` (verb `held`, result `accepted`).\n  - `REC-LOCAL-PREVENT-001` → suspended skill → `prevented`, backed by\n    `CR-LOCAL-SKILL-PREVENT-001` (verb `policy_denied`, result `rejected`).\n\n## Validator hardening (story \"Hardening bar\")\nAll kill-list items are covered:\n\n- **No self-asserted booleans standing in for proof.** `decisionPolicyProof`\n  accumulates structural evidence (status coverage, outcome derivation,\n  receipt shape-matching, append-only, deferred-gate proof) and is checked\n  against every `decisionPolicy` boolean at the end: an asserted-but-unbacked\n  boolean fails (`skill-registry-slice-validate.ps1:906-918`).\n- **No hardcoded-id binding rules** — outcomes are discovered BY SHAPE over\n  collections (`flagReceipts` / `preventReceipts` via `Where-Object`,\n  `:720-747`), and each scenario's `outcomeReceipt` is bound by shape, not id\n  (`:749-791`). Coverage (exactly one active/deprecated/suspended; one\n  flag/prevent scenario) is derived, not counted (`:460-465`, `:571-594`).\n- **LIVE cross-slice id harvest from `$PSScriptRoot`** distinguishing MINTED\n  vs REFERENCED ids:\n  - `Invoke-CollectSiblingIds` walks EVERY co-located `*.json` (excluding the\n    manifest and this slice) and harvests work-item/receipt/idempotency/\n    source-record/skill/scenario/run ids into hashtables (`:108-182`,\n    `:284-293`).\n  - MINTED ids (`CSK-LOCAL-*`, `CR-LOCAL-SKILL-*`, `REC-LOCAL-*`, runId) must\n    be unique across all slices (`:406-408`, `:644-647`, `:490-492`, `:319-321`).\n  - REFERENCED ids (`CSR-*` in provenance / receipt-source-links / evidence\n    refs) must resolve to a known sibling Source Record (`:444-447`,\n    `:806-807`, `:700-710`).\n- **No conditional/skippable mandatory checks** — every guard, field, vocab\n  membership, and id-resolution check runs unconditionally over its\n  collection; `decisionPolicyProof` entries start `$true` and are AND-ed down\n  (so a silently-true default still requires the derived evidence to hold).\n- **Coverage derived, not counted** — `skillsByStatus`, `flagScenarios`,\n  `preventScenarios`, receipt-by-shape counts are all computed from records.\n- **Wrapped JSON loads** via `Read-JsonInput` (`:184-197`) with exit 1 on\n  malformed input. **TryParse** numeric checks for `com_confidence`\n  (`Test-ConfidenceInRange`, `:54-74`). **Strict booleans** for guards and\n  `com_append_only_locked` (`:267-271`, `:675-678`). **ISO 8601 with explicit\n  UTC offset** via `Test-IsoTimestamp` (`:76-106`). **`$PSScriptRoot`-relative\n  paths** in the `param` block (`:2-3`). Final token\n  `SKILL_REGISTRY_SLICE_VALIDATE_OK` + issue list + `exit 1` on any failure\n  (`:920-933`).\n- **Vocabulary discipline** — `com_status`, `com_authority_class`,\n  `com_verb`, `com_actor_type`, `com_result`, `com_evidence_role` all checked\n  against the manifest choice sets; required verbs/results/statuses/authorities\n  asserted present (`:229-253`).\n\n## Verification commands\n```bash\nexport DOTNET_ROOT=$HOME/.dotnet\nexport PATH=$HOME/.dotnet:$HOME/.dotnet/tools:$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH\npwsh -File _bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/skill-registry-slice-validate.ps1\n# => prints SKILL_REGISTRY_SLICE_VALIDATE_OK, exit 0\n```\nThis is exactly the `ringer-check` line in the story spec.\n\n## Corruption tests run (story: \"Verify a corrupted slice copy FAILS\")\n1. **Status tamper** (deprecated→active): validator exits 1 with 9 issues\n   (duplicate active count, missing deprecated, derived-outcome mismatch,\n   authority-class inconsistency, three unbacked `decisionPolicy` booleans).\n2. **Cross-slice receipt-id collision** (flag receipt → `CR-LOCAL-DRIFT-001`,\n   a sibling source-drift receipt): validator exits 1 flagging both the\n   `CR-LOCAL-SKILL-*` identity violation and the sibling collision, plus the\n   dangling acceptance-mapping id.\n\nBoth confirm the hardening bar is met.\n\n## Files read for conventions\n- `dataverse-mvp-schema-manifest.json` — authoritative vocabulary\n  (table `com_councilskill` columns, `com_recordstatus`, `com_authorityclass`,\n  `com_receiptverb`, `com_receiptresult`, `com_actortype`,\n  `com_councilreceiptsource.com_evidence_role`).\n- `source-drift-supersession-slice.json` / `-validate.ps1` (story 1-5) —\n  gold-standard slice + validator pair mirrored for structure, helpers\n  (`Add-Issue`, `Get-ChoiceValues`, `Test-HasNonEmptyField`,\n  `Test-ConfidenceInRange`, `Test-IsoTimestamp`, `Read-JsonInput`), guards,\n  receipt field sets, and the success-token/exit-1 convention.\n- `skill-authority-expansion-slice.json` (story 5-2) — sibling skill slice;\n  confirmed its `CSK-LOCAL-*` ids and `CR-LOCAL-SKILL-*` receipt ids do NOT\n  collide with the ids minted here (DRIFT-SCAN / LEGACY-SUMMARIZE /\n  OUTBOUND-SEND vs MEETING-DIGEST / FABRIC-PUBLISHER; FLAG/PREVENT vs\n  APPROVE/DENY).\n\n## Assumptions / follow-ups\n- **Assumption:** the two deliverable files as already committed in HEAD are\n  the intended final state for this story; the Ringer check exports them as a\n  patch (no diff vs HEAD because they are already in-tree and correct). If\n  the orchestrator expected a fresh diff, the work is nonetheless complete\n  and verified — there was nothing to change.\n- **Assumption (carried from the slice's `receiptVerbPolicy` local\n  extension):** the manifest `com_receiptverb` has no skill-scoped flag/prevent\n  verb, so the slice reuses `held` (flag) and `policy_denied` (prevent), with\n  `com_result` + `com_before_state`/`com_after_state` disambiguating the\n  recommendation outcome from a Work Item state move. This is a documented\n  local extension; `guards.noWorkItemStateChangeInThisSlice` stays `true`.\n- **Follow-up (integrator, NOT this story):** wiring\n  `skill-registry-slice-validate.ps1` into `council-mvp-local-validate.ps1` is\n  the integrator's job after review (hard rule: do not edit\n  `council-mvp-local-validate.ps1`).\n- **Follow-up (Epic 2):** every live Council Skill row write and any\n  flag/prevent enforcement on the live recommendation path is recorded only in\n  `skillUpdatesDeferred` as receipt-gated to Epic 2 Story 2.3 — no live tenant\n  write exists in this slice.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":127,"totalLines":127,"truncated":false}},"title":"notes.md","time":{"start":1784298011729,"end":1784298011737}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Good — non-empty diff (17 insertions) on the ringer-owned validator file. notes.md is staged (A) from the previous worker; I'll overwrite it with accurate content. Let me read the existing notes.md first since I must read before writing... actually it's staged from the previous worker. Let me just read it then overwrite.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_f7072fa73001SU3odSXjKe52tp","sessionID":"ses_08f91df9fffe5mB6W2L75K6