act insertion points.\n\nFor (A) and (B): insert into the `if ($semanticSlicePresent) { ... }` block, after the existing `planesAreProjectionsOnly` guard check (around line 408-410).\n\nFor (C), (D), (E): insert into the role-based receipt requirements section. (C) goes in the `foreach ($denialReceipt in $denialRoleReceipts)` loop. (D) goes in the `foreach ($deferReceipt in $deferRoleReceipts)` loop. (E) goes after the attempts/receipts binding section — actually (E) is about deferred plane writes, so it could go in the deferred-plane-writes section (around line 864-897) OR in the denial binding section. Let me put (E) in the deferred-plane-writes section since that's where `$deferredPlaneWrites` is iterated, but I need `$denialRoleReceipts` and the attempt→plan mapping. Those are defined earlier. So I can add (E) right after the deferred-plane-writes loop, using a derived map of denied plan ids → denial receipt ids.\n\nLet me build a `$deniedPlanToReceipt` map in the denial binding section:\n```\n$deniedPlanToReceipt = @{}\nforeach ($attempt in $attempts) {\n  $tp = [string]$attempt.targetPlanId\n  $dr = [string]$attempt.deniedByReceipt\n  if (-not [string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace($tp) -and -not [string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace($dr)) {\n    $deniedPlanToReceipt[$tp] = $dr\n  }\n}\n```\nThen in the deferred-plane-writes loop, for each deferred entry whose planId is in `$deniedPlanToReceipt`, check that `deferredUpdate` references that receipt id.\n\nActually, (E) fits more naturally as a derived-coverage check right after the deferred-plane-writes loop. Let me add the map building + the check there.\n\nHmm, but `$deniedPlanToReceipt` needs `$attempts` which is defined at line 594. And `$deferredPlaneWrites` at line 864. So I can build the map just before the deferred-plane-writes loop, or inside the denial binding section. Let me build it in the denial binding section (after the \"every denial-role receipt must be bound to a plan via some attempt\" block, around line 822).\