d = $false\n    foreach ($planIdKey in @($slicePlanIds.Keys)) {\n      if ($deferEvidenceRefs -match [regex]::Escape($planIdKey)) {\n        $namesPlanId = $true\n        break\n      }\n    }\n    if (-not $namesPlanId) {\n      Add-Issue $issues \"$roleSubject com_evidence_refs must name at least one projection plan id declared in this slice (the plans it catalogs), not merely assert the catalog.\"\n    }\n```\n\nWait — `$slicePlanIds` is defined at line 490 and populated in the plans loop (lines 506). The defer-role receipt check is at line 756+, which is AFTER the plans loop. So `$slicePlanIds` is populated. Good.\n\nFor (E): denied plan's deferred-write entry must reference the denial receipt id. This goes in the deferred-plane-writes section. Let me build a `$deniedPlanToReceipt` map and check.\n\nI'll insert the map building right before the deferred-plane-writes loop (line 864), and the check inside the loop.\n\nActually, the deferred-plane-writes loop is at lines 869-892. Let me add the check inside, after the existing `deferredUpdate` receipt-gate check.\n\nCurrent deferred loop (lines 868-892):\n```\n$deferredPlanIdsSeen = @{}\nforeach ($deferred in $deferredPlaneWrites) {\n  $plane = [string]$deferred.targetSurface\n  $deferredPlanId = [string]$deferred.planId\n  $subject = \"Deferred Phase-2 plane write for $plane\"\n  if ([string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace($plane)) {\n    Add-Issue $issues \"Deferred Phase-2 plane write must name targetSurface.\"\n  }\n  if ([string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace($deferredPlanId) -or -not $slicePlanIds.ContainsKey($deferredPlanId)) {\n    Add-Issue $issues \"Deferred Phase-2 plane write must name a planId declared in this slice, found: $deferredPlanId.\"\n  }\n  else {\n    $deferredPlanIdsSeen[$deferredPlanId] = $true\n    $linkedPlan = $slicePlanIds[$deferredPlanId]\n    if ([string]$linkedPlan.targetSurface -ne $plane) {\n      Add-Issue $issues \"$subject targetSurface must match its plan's targetSurface ($($linkedPlan.targetSurface)), found: $plane.\"\n    }\n  }\n  if (-not (Test-HasNonEmptyField -Record $deferred -Field \"deferredUpdate\")) {\n    Add-Issue $issues \"$subject must carry a non-empty deferredUpdate.\"\n  }\n  elseif (($deferred.deferredUpdate -notmatch \"receipt-gat\") -and ($deferred.deferredUpdate -notmatch \"receipt gate\") -and ($deferred.deferredUpdate -notmatch \"CR-LOCAL-[A-Z0-9-]+\")) {\n    Add-Issue $issues \"$subject deferredUpdate must name its receipt gate (e.g. 'receipt-gated' or a CR-LOCAL-* receipt id); the bare word 'receipt' does not name a gate, found: $($deferred.deferredUpdate).\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\nI'll add the `$deniedPlanToReceipt` map before the loop, and add a check inside the `else` block (where the plan is confirmed valid) — if the plan is a denied plan, the deferredUpdate must reference its denial receipt id.\n\nLet me build the map. I need `$attempts` (defined line 594) — available. And `$slicePlanIds` — available.\n\nInsert before `$deferredPlanIdsSeen = @{}`:\n```\n# Derived map: plan ids that were the target of a denied premature-activation attempt,\n# mapped to the denial receipt id that denied them. General rule over the attempts\n# collection — used to require the deferred-write ledger to reference the denial receipt\n# for any plan whose activation was denied (the denial must thread through to the ledger).\n$deniedPlanToReceipt = @{}\nforeach ($attempt in $attempts) {\n  $deniedTargetPlanId = [string]$attempt.targetPlanId\n  $deniedByReceiptId = [string]$attempt.deniedByReceipt\n  if (-not [string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace($deniedTargetPlanId) -and -not [string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace($deniedByReceiptId)) {\n    $deniedPlanToReceipt[$deniedTargetPlanId] = $deniedByReceiptId\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThen inside the deferred loop's `else` block, add:\n```\n  else {\n    $deferredPlanIdsSeen[$deferredPlanId] = $true\n    $linkedPlan = $slicePlanIds[$deferredPlanId]\n    if ([string]$linkedPlan.targetSurface -ne $plane) {\n      Add-Issue $issues \"$subject targetSurface must match its plan's targetSurface ($($linkedPlan.targetSurface)), found: $plane.\"\n    }\n    # If this plan's activation was denied, the deferred-write ledger must reference the\n    # denial receipt id — the denial threads through to the deferred-write entry.\n    if ($deniedPlanToReceipt.ContainsKey($deferredPlanId)) {\n      $expectedDenialReceipt = $deniedPlanToReceipt[$deferredPlanId]\n      if (-not (Test-HasNonEmptyField -Record $deferred -Field \"deferredUpdate\") -or ([string]$deferred.deferredUpdate -notmatch [regex]::Escape($expectedDenialReceipt))) {\n        Add-Issue $issues \"$subject deferredUpdate must reference the denial receipt $expectedDenialReceipt that denied plan $deferredPlanId; a denied plan's deferred-write entry must thread the denial through.\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n```\n\nWait — the `deferredUpdate` non-empty check happens AFTER the else block (lines 886-891). So inside the else block, `deferredUpdate` might be empty. My check handles that with `-not (Test-HasNonEmptyField ...)`. But then the later check at line 886 would ALSO fire for empty deferredUpdate. That's fine — both issues would be reported, no harm. Actually, to avoid double-reporting, let me only check the denial-receipt reference when deferredUpdate is non-empty:\n\n```\n    if ($deniedPlanToReceipt.ContainsKey($deferredPlanId)) {\n      $expectedDenialReceipt = $deniedPlanToReceipt[$deferredPlanId]\n      if ((Test-HasNonEmptyField -Record $deferred -Field \"deferredUpdate\") -and ([string]$deferred.deferredUpdate -notmatch [regex]::Escape($expectedDenialReceipt))) {\n        Add-Issue $issues \"$subject deferredUpdate must reference the denial receipt $expectedDenialReceipt that denied plan $deferredPlanId; a denied plan's deferred-write entry must thread the denial through.\"\n      }\n    }\n```\n\nThis way, if deferredUpdate is empty, only the existing \"must carry a non-empty deferredUpdate\" issue fires. If it's non-empty but doesn't reference the denial receipt, my check fires. Clean.\n\nLet me verify (E) passes with the current slice:\n- denied plan: PHASE2-PLAN-LOCAL-002 → denial receipt CR-LOCAL-PHASE2-PREACT-DENIED-001\n- deferred entry for PHASE2-PLAN-LOCAL-002: deferredUpdate = \"Publishing the Copilot Studio surface projection is receipt-gated until mvp-contracts-stable and remains denied after CR-LOCAL-PHASE2-PREACT-DENIED-001; no tenant write was performed in this slice.\"\n- Contains \"CR-LOCAL-PHASE2-PREACT-DENIED-001\"? Yes. ✓\n\nGood.\n\nNow let me trace all checks against the current (post-slice-edit) state once more to be sure everything passes:\n\n(A) 5-6 run.semanticContractVersion=\"2026-07-07\" == 4-5 projectionRun.semanticContractVersion=\"2026-07-07\". ✓\n(B) 5-6 run.canonicalSource=\"council-semantic-contract\" == 4-5 projectionRun.canonicalSource=\"council-semantic-contract\". ✓\n(C) denial receipt com_decision_rationale (after edit) contains \"mvp-contracts-stable\". ✓\n(D) defer receipt com_evidence_refs=\"projectionPlans[PHASE2-PLAN-LOCAL-001..003]; ...\" contains \"PHASE2-PLAN-LOCAL-001\" (a key in $slicePlanIds). ✓\n(E) deferred entry for PHASE2-PLAN-LOCAL-002 references \"CR-LOCAL-PHASE2-PREACT-DENIED-001\". ✓\n\nAll pass.\n\nNow let me also verify the corruption test will still fail. If someone flips ownsWorkflowState to true: the existing check fires. If someone drops the denial receipt: (C) doesn't run (no denial-role receipt), but the existing \"must include >=1 denial receipt\" fires, and (E) would fire because the deferred entry references a denial receipt id that no longer exists as a denial-role receipt — wait, (E) checks the deferredUpdate references the receipt id from the attempt's deniedByReceipt. If the receipt is dropped but the attempt still has deniedByReceipt=\"CR-LOCAL-PHASE2-PREACT-DENIED-001\", then (E) checks the deferred entry references that id — it does. So (E) passes even if the receipt is dropped. But the existing checks (denial-role receipt count, deniedByReceipt must resolve to a receipt declared in this slice) would fire. So corruption still fails. Good.\n\nNow let me make the edits. Let me be precise with the oldString matching.\n\nLet me make the slice JSON edit first.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_f707417fa001piHUs01uOrih4v","sessionID":"ses_08f91718dffe8QIoOmeSnVHPPW","messageID":"msg_f706fc5a2001677aIxDl5R1q1N"}}
