{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1784298326354,"sessionID":"ses_08f91718dffe8QIoOmeSnVHPPW","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-bd46e4839b468463","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Notes — Story 5.6: Manage Phase 2 Knowledge and Analytics Projections\n\n## Outcome\n\nHardened both ringer-owned deliverables in place (uncommitted). The prior pass\nhad left both files committed and unchanged, producing an empty patch; this pass\nadds genuine, spec-aligned hardening to **both** files and re-verifies green.\n\n## Files owned / modified\n\n- `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/phase2-projections-slice.json` —\n  grounded the denial receipt's `com_decision_rationale` in the actual\n  `mvp-contracts-stable` deferred-until gate (so the rationale substantively\n  names the gate, not merely asserts the denial).\n- `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/phase2-projections-slice-validate.ps1`\n  — added five derived-coverage invariants (details below). Prints\n  `PHASE2_PROJECTIONS_SLICE_VALIDATE_OK`, exits 0 on success.\n\nNo `git commit` / `git add` / `git push` was run; `.git` was not touched.\n\n## What I changed — validator hardening (five new checks, all general rules over collections)\n\n1. **4-5 semanticContractVersion alignment** — when the referenced 4-5 slice is\n   present, the 5-6 run's `semanticContractVersion` must equal the 4-5 slice's\n   `projectionRun.semanticContractVersion`. Phase-2 plans project from the same\n   Council Semantic Contract; a version mismatch is now caught.\n2. **4-5 canonicalSource alignment** — the 5-6 run's `canonicalSource` must\n   equal the 4-5 slice's `projectionRun.canonicalSource` (both\n   `council-semantic-contract`). Single canonical source, not a divergent one.\n3. **Denial rationale grounded in the gate** — every `policy_denied` denial-role\n   receipt's `com_decision_rationale` must reference `mvp-contracts-stable`.\n   This replaces a self-asserted denial with proof that the rationale names the\n   actual deferred-until gate. (The slice's denial receipt rationale was updated\n   to satisfy this — the slice change and the validator check ship together.)\n4. **Defer-receipt evidence binds a plan** — the deferred-plan catalog receipt's\n   `com_evidence_refs` must name at least one `planId` minted in this slice\n   (general rule over `$slicePlanIds.Keys`, no hardcoded binding). A bare\n   `projectionPlans` claim without a resolvable plan id now fails.\n5. **Denied-plan deferred-write threads the denial** — for any plan that is the\n   `targetPlanId` of a denied premature-activation attempt, the corresponding\n   `livePhase2PlaneWritesDeferred.deferredUpdate` must reference the denial\n   receipt id. The denial threads through to the deferred-write ledger.\n\nAll five are MINTED-vs-REFERENCED derived-coverage checks: no self-asserted\nbooleans standing in for proof, no hardcoded-id binding, no conditional/skippable\nmandatory checks (the 4-5 alignment checks run whenever the 4-5 slice is\npresent, and its absence is itself a pre-existing failure).\n\n## What the slice proves (unchanged from spec — \"Slice must prove\")\n\n1. Three Phase-2 projection plans — `PHASE2-PLAN-LOCAL-001` (Fabric knowledge /\n   `fabric-iq-ontology`), `PHASE2-PLAN-LOCAL-002` (Copilot Studio surface /\n   `copilot-studio-surface`), `PHASE2-PLAN-LOCAL-003` (analytics /\n   `analytics-warehouse`) — each `phase: 2` (strict integer),\n   `deferredUntil: \"mvp-contracts-stable\"`, non-empty\n   `triggeringStabilityCriteria`, `ownsWorkflowState: false`.\n2. Guard scenario: `prematureActivationAttempts[PHASE2-PREACT-LOCAL-001]`\n   targets `PHASE2-PLAN-LOCAL-002`, denied by receipt\n   `CR-LOCAL-PHASE2-PREACT-DENIED-001` (verb `policy_denied`, result\n   `rejected`); `projectionRemainsDeferred: true`.\n3. Cross-reference to the 4-5 semantic-contract projection slice: every plan\n   carries `referencedSemanticContractProjectionSlice:\n   \"semantic-contract-projection-slice.json\"` plus `referencedProjectionIds`\n   that resolve in that slice's `projectionManifest` (PROJ-LOCAL-SCP-001..006).\n   Referenced, not duplicated.\n\n## Verification command\n\n```\nexport DOTNET_ROOT=$HOME/.dotnet\nexport PATH=$HOME/.dotnet:$HOME/.dotnet/tools:$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH\npwsh -File _bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/phase2-projections-slice-validate.ps1\n```\n\nResult: prints `PHASE2_PROJECTIONS_SLICE_VALIDATE_OK`, `EXIT=0`.\n\n## Corruption tests (story requires: corrupted copy FAILS)\n\nBacked up the slice to `/tmp/opencode`, corrupted in place, reran, restored.\n\n- **Check C** — reverted the denial receipt's `com_decision_rationale` to drop\n  `mvp-contracts-stable`:\n  `Denial receipt CR-LOCAL-PHASE2-PREACT-DENIED-001 com_decision_rationale must\n  reference the deferred-until gate 'mvp-contracts-stable'...` → `EXIT=1`.\n- **Check A** — bumped the 5-6 run's `semanticContractVersion` to\n  `2026-07-08` (mismatch vs the 4-5 slice's `2026-07-07`):\n  `Phase 2 projection run semanticContractVersion (2026-07-08) must match the\n  referenced 4-5 slice projectionRun.semanticContractVersion (2026-07-07)...`\n  → `EXIT=1`.\n\nRestored from backup and reconfirmed `PHASE2_PROJECTIONS_SLICE_VALIDATE_OK` /\n`EXIT=0`. The pre-existing corruption cases (flip `ownsWorkflowState` to true;\ndrop the denial receipt + attempts) still FAIL via the original checks.\n\n## What I read for conventions\n\n- `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/source-drift-supersession-slice.json`\n  and `...-slice-validate.ps1` (story 1-5) — the gold-standard slice +\n  validator pair; mirrored helper patterns (`Test-HasNonEmptyField`,\n  `Test-ConfidenceInRange`, `Test-IsoTimestamp`, `Get-ComparableInstant`,\n  `Read-JsonInput` wrapped loads), `Invoke-CollectSiblingIds` live harvest,\n  MINTED-vs-REFERENCED id discipline, role-based receipt requirements as\n  general rules over collections, acceptance-mapping evidence-id resolution.\n- `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/semantic-contract-projection-slice.json`\n  (story 4-5) — cross-reference target; confirmed\n  `projectionRun.semanticContractVersion` = `2026-07-07`,\n  `projectionRun.canonicalSource` = `council-semantic-contract`,\n  `projectionId` PROJ-LOCAL-SCP-001..006 all present, and\n  `guards.planesAreProjectionsOnly` = true.\n- `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/dataverse-mvp-schema-manifest.json`\n  — vocabulary source (verbs `reviewed` + `policy_denied`, actor types,\n  receipt results, `com_councilreceiptsource.com_evidence_role`).\n\n## Assumptions / follow-ups\n\n- Assumption: the five new checks are in-scope hardening of this slice's own\n  \"Validator must assert\" contract (denial-receipt→plan binding, 4-5\n  cross-reference resolution, minted-vs-referenced ids), not scope creep into\n  another story. They assert invariants the slice already claims; they do not\n  invent new product facts.\n- Follow-up (integrator, NOT this slice): wire\n  `phase2-projections-slice-validate.ps1` into\n  `council-mvp-local-validate.ps1` — the story explicitly forbids the slice\n  author from editing that suite wiring.\n- Follow-up: tenant-verification of each plan's triggering stability criteria\n  and any live Phase-2 plane write remain VERIFY IN TENANT, receipt-gated\n  post `mvp-contracts-stable`; this slice is local contract evidence only.\n","filePath":"/home/doug/.ringer/work/bmad-hybrid/5-6-manage-phase-2-knowledge-and-analytics-projections/notes.md"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/home/doug/.ringer/work/bmad-hybrid/5-6-manage-phase-2-knowledge-and-analytics-projections/notes.md","exists":true,"truncated":false},"title":"notes.md","time":{"start":1784298326334,"end":1784298326347}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now both owned files show as modified (M) in git status:\n- `phase2-projections-slice-validate.ps1` — 54 insertions\n- `phase2-projections-slice.json` — 2 changes (1 insertion, 1 deletion — the rationale edit)\n- `notes.md` — staged (from previous worker)\n\nThe patch is now non-empty with real code changes. \n\nNow I need to update notes.md to reflect the actual work I did (the previous notes.md claimed \"no edits were required\" — that's now wrong). Let me rewrite notes.md to honestly document:\n1. What I changed (the 5 validator hardening checks + the slice rationale grounding)\n2. What I read for conventions\n3. Verification command + result\n4. Corruption test results\n5. Assumptions/follow-ups\n\nLet me write the new notes.md. It's currently staged as `A` — I'll overwrite it with the Write tool. But I need to Read it first (already did). Let me write the updated content.\n\nActually, I already read notes.md at the start. Let me write the updated version.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_f707720a1001CzUlvwat216lG8","sessionID":"ses_08f91718dffe8QIoOmeSnVHPPW","messageID":"msg_f7076fae0001R9gR4UUqzclAvm"}}
