{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Confirmed: T5 is a real hole. The validator passes (RC=0) when the proposal cites the wrong row's gap content — as long as 2 generic shared terms (\"contract\", \"semantics\") appear. This violates the story requirement: \"the custom proposal's gap citation references a recorded gap in an evaluation row.\" The citation must reference the SPECIFIC recorded gap, not isolated generic vocabulary.\n\nNow let me apply the fix: replace the isolated-term-count fallback with a verbatim contiguous phrase-run check. Let me make the two edits.\n\nLet me record a todo list to track this properly since it's a multi-step task. Actually, the task is focused enough. But let me track it since there are distinct steps: fix validator, re-test baseline, re-test T5 (now should fail), re-test all other corruptions, write notes.md. Let me use a todo list.\n\nActually, let me just proceed efficiently. Let me make the edits.\n\nFirst, let me re-read the exact lines to edit to ensure exact match.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_f70784a22001wn5Amx77eACLt2","sessionID":"ses_08f914172ffeudlWP9EWlAXTjJ","messageID":"msg_f707812030013LRxBXTaCK4c6c"}}
