\n\nThis PASSED. But it shouldn't have — it has no verbatim contiguous run from the cited row's gap text. Let me check why it passed.\n\nThe cited row's gap text (PE-LOCAL-EVAL-001-ROW-02, Dataverse MCP):\n\"Gap: Dataverse MCP exposes generic table-row CRUD semantics but projects no append-only receipt ledger view keyed by com_idempotency_key with com_before_state/com_after_state lineage, and no meaning-graph entity/edge projection matching the com_councilgraphentity/com_councilgraphedge contracts. The Council receipt contract and semantic contract require these projections; Dataverse MCP does not surface them natively, so a custom projection is required to fill this gap.\"\n\nT5b citation normalized: \"references row pe-local-eval-001-row-02 because the contract and semantics require a projection this is the recorded gap\"\n\nNow, does any 3-token contiguous run from the gap appear in this citation?\n\nGap normalized tokens include: \"...the council receipt contract and semantic contract require these projections...\"\n\nWait — \"contract and semantic contract require these projections\" — let me find 3-runs in the gap that appear in T5b's \"the contract and semantics require a projection\".\n\nHmm. T5b has \"the contract and semantics require a projection\". The gap has \"contract and semantic contract require these projections\". Note: \"semantic\" (singular) vs \"semantics\" (plural in T5b). These differ. So \"semantic contract\" (gap) ≠ \"semantics require\" (T5b).\n\nLet me look for a 3-run. Gap tokens around there: \"...receipt contract and semantic contract require these projections...\". T5b: \"...the contract and semantics require a projection...\".\n\nIs there a 3-token run shared? Let me list gap 3-runs near \"contract\":\n- \"receipt contract and\"\n- \"contract and semantic\"\n- \"and semantic contract\"\n- \"semantic contract require\"\n- \"contract require these\"\n- \"require these projections\"\n\nT5b 3-runs:\n- \"the contract and\"\n- \"contract and semantics\"  ← \"semantics\" not \"semantic\"\n- \"and semantics require\"\n- \"semantics require a\"\n- \"require a projection\"\n\nComparing: \"contract and semantic\" (gap) vs \"contract and semantics\" (T5b) — differ at 3rd token (semantic vs semantics). No match.\n\nHmm, so no 3-run should match. But it PASSED. Let me reconsider — maybe my normalization produces different tokens. Wait, \"semantics\" → normalized \"semantics\"; \"semantic\" → \"semantic\". Different. So no match there.\n\nLet me look more carefully. Why did T5b pass? Let me check whether there's some OTHER 3-run that matches. The citation \"references row pe-local-eval-001-row-02 because the contract and semantics require a projection this is the recorded gap\".\n\nGap has the token sequence \"...this gap\" at the end (\"...required to fill this gap\"). T5b has \"this is the recorded gap\". Gap 3-run: \"fill this gap\". T5b has \"this is the\" and \"is the recorded\" and \"the recorded gap\" and \"recorded gap\" (end). Does \"fill this gap\" appear in T5b? No. Does \"this gap\" appear? T5b has \"this is the recorded gap\" — \"this gap\" is not contiguous (there's \"is the recorded\" between). So no.\n\nHmm wait. Let me reconsider. Maybe the issue is that \"row pe-local-eval-001-row-02\" — the token \"pe-local-eval-001-row-02\" is in BOTH the citation (from \"references row PE-LOCAL-EVAL-001-ROW-02\") and... no, the gap text doesn't contain the row id.\n\nWait, let me reconsider. Actually — does the gap text contain \"a projection\"? Gap: \"...so a custom projection is required to fill this gap.\" → tokens \"a custom projection is required to fill this gap\". T5b: \"require a projection\". \n\nGap 3-run: \"custom projection is\", \"projection is required\", \"a custom projection\". T5b: \"require a projection\", \"a projection this\". Does \"a projection\" appear as a 3-run? No, \"a projection\" is 2 tokens. The check requires 3 contiguous tokens.\n\nHmm. So why did T5b pass? Let me actually debug this. Let me check what phrase matched.\n\nActually — wait. Maybe the issue is my normalization of the citation includes the row id \"pe-local-eval-001-row-02\" and the gap... no.\n\nLet me actually run a debug to find which phrase matched in T5b. Let me also reconsider: maybe \"the contract and\" — gap has \"the council receipt contract and...\" → \"the council receipt\" no. Hmm. Does gap have \"the contract\"? Gap: \"The Council receipt contract and semantic contract require these projections\". Tokens: \"the council receipt contract and semantic contract require these projections\". So \"the contract\" is NOT contiguous in gap (it's \"the council receipt contract\"). So \"the contract and\" is not a gap 3-run.\n\nLet me debug T5b to see the matched phrase. Actually, let me reconsider — maybe there's a bug in my loop. Let me check: `$lastStart = $gapTokens.Count - $requiredRunLength`. If gapTokens.Count = 50, lastStart = 47. Loop i from 0 to 47 inclusive (48 iterations). At i=47: tokens[47..49] (3 tokens). Good.\n\nBut wait — what if `$normCitation.IndexOf($phrase, ...)` matches a SUBSTRING that spans across what should be token boundaries? Since both are normalized to single spaces and I join tokens with single space, a phrase \"a b c\" would match in normCitation if \"a b c\" appears as a substring. But normCitation is also single-spaced normalized. So a phrase match means 3 contiguous tokens match. That's correct.\n\nUnless... the phrase contains a token that's a substring of a longer token. E.g., gap phrase \"and a custom\" — wait. Hmm. Let me think about token boundary issues. If gap has tokens [..., \"a\", \"custom\", \"projection\", ...] and I form phrase \"a custom projection\", and normCitation has \"...require a projection this is...\" — does \"a custom projection\" appear in normCitation? No, because normCitation doesn't have \"custom\" between \"a\" and \"projection\". So no match. Good.\n\nBut what about a SHORTER token being a substring? Like gap phrase \"is the recorded\" — if normCitation has \"this is the recorded gap\", then \"is the recorded\" IS a substring of \"this is the recorded gap\"! Because \"this is the recorded gap\" contains \"is the recorded\" as a substring (starting at index 5: \"this [is the recorded] gap\"). \n\nSo the substring match can match ACROSS token boundaries if the phrase happens to be a substring of a longer run. In this case, \"is the recorded\" — is this a gap 3-run? Gap tokens include \"is required to\" (from \"projection is required to fill\"). Does gap have \"is the recorded\"? Gap: \"...projection is required to fill this gap.\" → \"projection is required\" no \"is the\". Hmm. Does gap have \"the recorded\"? No.\n\nOK so that's not it. Let me actually just debug. Let me write a quick PowerShell or Python to find the matching phrase for T5b.\n\nActually, let me reconsider — maybe T5b legitimately contains a 3-run from the gap that I'm not seeing. Let me list ALL 3-runs in the gap and check each against T5b's citation. Let me do this with Python.\n\nActually, let me reconsider the gap text more fully. Let me get the exact gap text for row 02 and the T5b citation, normalize both, and find common 3-runs. Let me run Python.\n\nHmm wait — actually, I bet the issue is the token \"recorded\". Let me check: gap has \"no append-only receipt ledger view keyed by com_idempotency_key\". T5b has \"this is the recorded gap\". No common 3-run there.\n\nLet me just run the debug.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_f707aadf5001Xxc6hv1NJ2JBYq","sessionID":"ses_08f914172ffeudlWP9EWlAXTjJ","messageID":"msg_f7079dbc3001A4c5ZvLao0s3Ss"}}
