equiredRunLength - 1)] -join ' ')\n          if ($normCitation.IndexOf($phrase, [System.StringComparison]::Ordinal) -ge 0) {\n            $phraseHit = $true\n            break\n          }\n        }\n```\n\nwith the delimiter-blob approach:\n```\n        $normCitation = [string]((([string]$citation).ToLower() -replace '[^a-z0-9_/-]+', ' ') -replace '\\s+', ' ')\n        $citationTokens = @($normCitation.Trim() -split ' ' | Where-Object { -not [string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace($_) })\n        $normGap = [string]((([string]$gapText).ToLower() -replace '[^a-z0-9_/-]+', ' ') -replace '\\s+', ' ')\n        $gapTokens = @($normGap.Trim() -split ' ' | Where-Object { -not [string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace($_) })\n        # Token-boundary-aware containment: the delimiter never appears inside a\n        # normalized token (tokens are [a-z0-9_/-] only), so a delimited phrase can\n        # only match whole tokens, never a prefix of one (e.g. \"semantic\" inside\n        # \"semantics\"). This is what makes the tie a true phrase match, not a bare\n        # substring scan.\n        $phraseDelim = '|'\n        $citationBlob = $phraseDelim + ($citationTokens -join $phraseDelim) + $phraseDelim\n        $phraseHit = $false\n        $requiredRunLength = 3\n        $lastStart = $gapTokens.Count - $requiredRunLength\n        for ($i = 0; $i -le $lastStart; $i++) {\n          $phrase = $phraseDelim + ($gapTokens[$i..($i + $requiredRunLength - 1)] -join $phraseDelim) + $phraseDelim\n          if ($citationBlob.IndexOf($phrase, [System.StringComparison]::Ordinal) -ge 0) {\n            $phraseHit = $true\n            break\n          }\n        }\n```\n\nThis fixes the partial-token bug. Let me apply this edit.\n\nWait — one concern: the delimiter '|'. The normalized tokens are [a-z0-9_/-] only (no '|'). So '|' never appears in a token. Good. And the blob is \"|tok1|tok2|...|tokN|\". A phrase \"|a|b|c|\" matches only if \"a\",\"b\",\"c\" are consecutive whole tokens. The leading and trailing '|' ensure boundary alignment. For a phrase at the START of the citation, citationBlob starts with \"|tok1|...\", and phrase \"|tok1|tok2|tok3|\" — the leading '|' matches the blob's leading '|'. Good. For a phrase at the END, the trailing '|' matches. Good. Mid-phrase: \"|a|b|c|\" matches \"|x|a|b|c|y|\". Good.\n\nEdge: if requiredRunLength tokens at the very start: phrase \"|gapTok0|gapTok1|gapTok2|\" and citationBlob \"|gapTok0|gapTok1|gapTok2|...\". The leading '|' of phrase matches blob's leading '|'. Good.\n\nThis is correct. Let me apply.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_f707bdd06001VGGGSP68farANC","sessionID":"ses_08f914172ffeudlWP9EWlAXTjJ","messageID":"msg_f707ac5ee001L0PrtVy3NWhdKf"}}
