{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1784298704588,"sessionID":"ses_08f914172ffeudlWP9EWlAXTjJ","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-bcd1ec23f94eefaf","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/doug/.ringer/work/bmad-hybrid/5-3-record-microsoft-platform-evaluation-evidence/notes.md"},"output":"<path>/home/doug/.ringer/work/bmad-hybrid/5-3-record-microsoft-platform-evaluation-evidence/notes.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Story 5.3 — Record Microsoft Platform Evaluation Evidence — Worker Notes\n2: \n3: ## Outcome\n4: \n5: The two ringer-owned deliverables were already present in the worktree HEAD\n6: (commit `068ce1b` \"epic 5: review-hardened validators for 5-1/5-2/5-3/5-5/5-6\")\n7: and are correct and hardened. No code edits were required; this worker verified\n8: the state, exercised the corrupted-copy tripwire, and wrote this notes file.\n9: \n10: ## Files I own (ringer-owned)\n11: \n12: - `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/platform-evaluation-slice.json`\n13: - `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/platform-evaluation-slice-validate.ps1`\n14: \n15: Both files are committed in HEAD and pass validation with exit 0 +\n16: `PLATFORM_EVALUATION_SLICE_VALIDATE_OK`. There is no uncommitted diff to the\n17: owned files; `git diff --stat HEAD` is empty. The only new file is this\n18: `notes.md` (the output contract).\n19: \n20: ## What I changed\n21: \n22: - Nothing in the two owned files — they were already complete and committed by\n23:   the prior review-hardening wave (commits `ac56eb8`, `068ce1b`).\n24: - Verified the slice + validator satisfy every clause of the story spec (see\n25:   \"Verification\" below).\n26: - Verified a corrupted slice copy FAILS (removed one candidate row from\n27:   PE-LOCAL-EVAL-001; validator emitted\n28:   \"Evaluation PE-LOCAL-EVAL-001 must consider at least four Microsoft\n29:   candidates, found 3.\" plus downstream minted-id collision notes, and exited\n30:   1).\n31: - Wrote `notes.md` (this file).\n32: \n33: ## What I read for conventions\n34: \n35: - `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/dataverse-mvp-schema-manifest.json` —\n36:   authoritative vocabulary. The slice's `com_decision` values (adopt/defer/\n37:   reject/custom_gap_build) come from `com_platformdecision`; receipt verbs\n38:   (proposed/reviewed) from `com_receiptverb`; actor types (human/system) from\n39:   `com_actortype`; results (accepted) from `com_receiptresult`. The\n40:   `com_councilplatformevaluation` table column set drives the row-completeness\n41:   union used by the validator.\n42: - `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/source-drift-supersession-slice.json`\n43:   and `...-slice-validate.ps1` (story 1-5) — the gold-standard slice + validator\n44:   pair. Mirrored patterns: story-keyed slice, declared `guards` with\n45:   `receiptsAreLocalContractEvidenceOnly: true`, no-live-write guards, wrapped\n46:   JSON loads (`Read-JsonInput`), `TryParse` numeric checks, strict booleans,\n47:   ISO 8601 timestamp checks, `$PSScriptRoot`-relative paths, issue list + exit\n48:   1, final `<NAME>_SLICE_VALIDATE_OK` token.\n49: - Sibling slices for cross-slice id checks: `manual-source-record-slice.json`,\n50:   `outlook-source-reference-slice.json`, `proposed-work-item-extraction-slice.json`,\n51:   `zero-multi-item-extraction-slice.json`, plus\n52:   `state-transition-demo-evidence.json`. The validator LIVE-harvests every\n53:   `*-slice.json` in `$PSScriptRoot` plus the demo evidence for minted-vs-referenced\n54:   id resolution.\n55: \n56: ## Command that verifies it\n57: \n58: ```\n59: export DOTNET_ROOT=$HOME/.dotnet; export PATH=$HOME/.dotnet:$HOME/.dotnet/tools:$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH; pwsh -File _bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/platform-evaluation-slice-validate.ps1\n60: ```\n61: \n62: Expected: prints `PLATFORM_EVALUATION_SLICE_VALIDATE_OK` and exits 0. Confirmed\n63: locally. Corrupted-copy test (point `-PlatformSlicePath` at a temp copy with one\n64: candidate row removed) correctly exits 1 with issues listed.\n65: \n66: ## How the slice proves each story requirement\n67: \n68: ### Slice must prove\n69: \n70: 1. **Two capability evaluations, each with >=4 candidates from the named set,\n71:     each row capturing tenant gates, permission/DLP, licensing/cost, ALM path,\n72:     contract gaps, decision, review reference.**\n73:    - `platformEvaluationRun.evaluations` carries `PE-LOCAL-EVAL-001`\n74:      (memory-and-graph-grounding) with 4 rows (Work IQ, Dataverse\n75:      intelligence/MCP, Fabric IQ/Graph, Fabric data agents) and\n76:      `PE-LOCAL-EVAL-002` (workflow-automation) with 4 rows (Power Automate,\n77:      Copilot Studio, Power Apps MCP agent feed, Work IQ). All candidates are\n78:      members of the spec `candidateUniverse`. Each row carries all seven\n79:      story-mandated capture fields plus the manifest-required `com_name`,\n80:      `com_council_capability`, `com_microsoft_candidate`,\n81:      `com_official_source_date_checked`, `com_decision`.\n82: 2. **One custom-service proposal citing a specific Microsoft-native gap / tenant\n83:     constraint, decision recorded as a receipt BEFORE implementation, no\n84:     implementation artifacts referenced.**\n85:    - `customServiceProposals[0]` = `CSP-LOCAL-001`, `addressesGapInRow` =\n86:      `PE-LOCAL-EVAL-001-ROW-02` (Dataverse intelligence/MCP, decision\n87:      `custom_gap_build`). `gapCitation` quotes the row's recorded\n88:      `com_contract_gaps`; `tenantConstraintCited` quotes\n89:      `tenant-decision-packet.json fabricIqGraphPhase2=defer_to_phase_2`.\n90:      `decisionReceipt` = `CR-LOCAL-PE-001` (verb `proposed`, append-only\n91:      locked). `implementationArtifactsReferenced` is empty; no\n92:      implementation-marker field appears anywhere in the slice (the validator\n93:      walks every property name).\n94: \n95: ### Validator must assert (hardening bar)\n96: \n97: - **Candidate coverage (>=4 per evaluation, from the named set):** derived,\n98:   not counted — each row's `com_microsoft_candidate` must be a member of the\n99:   closed `specCandidateUniverse`, no candidate duplicated within an eval, and\n100:   `rows.Count -lt 4` trips.\n101: - **Row field completeness:** checked over the UNION of manifest-required PE\n102:   columns and the story-mandated capture set (so the manifest-optional fields\n103:   cannot be silently dropped).\n104: - **Custom proposal gap citation references a recorded gap in an evaluation\n105:   row:** `addressesGapInRow` must resolve to a minted row whose decision is\n106:   `custom_gap_build` AND whose `com_contract_gaps` is non-empty AND whose gap\n107:   text substantively overlaps the `gapCitation` (verbatim run or >=2\n108:   significant terms derived from the cited row, never hardcoded).\n109: - **Decision receipts complete and precede any implementation marker:**\n110:   manifest-required receipt fields + `com_before_state/com_after_state/\n111:   com_evidence_refs/com_decision_rationale/com_policy_flags` enforced; the\n112:   Microsoft-native-before-custom-substrate ordering is DERIVED from receipt\n113:   timestamps (every evaluation-review receipt timestamp <= every proposal\n114:   decision receipt timestamp), not from a self-asserted guard. No\n115:   implementation-marker field name may appear anywhere in the slice.\n116: - **Minted-vs-referenced ids:** `Collect-Ids` walks the parsed object graph\n117:   (not raw text) for CWI/CR/CSR; minted CR ids (this slice's receipts) must be\n118:   unique across ALL sibling slices + demo evidence; referenced CWI/CR/CSR ids\n119:   not minted here must resolve to a sibling or demo id. Within-slice uniqueness\n120:   enforced for `PE-LOCAL-*` and `CSP-LOCAL-*` namespaces at their minting\n121:   fields only.\n122: - **Cross-slice uniqueness:** LIVE `Get-ChildItem -Filter \"*-slice.json\"` in\n123:   `$PSScriptRoot` (excluding this slice) — no hardcoded sibling list, no\n124:   hardcoded-id binding rules. A missing-sibling-files tripwire prevents the\n125:   check silently no-op'ing.\n126: - **No conditional/skippable mandatory checks:** each collection-driven check\n127:   has a \"would silently no-op\" tripwire if the underlying collection is empty.\n128: - **Coverage derived not counted:** confirmed above.\n129: - **Corrupted slice copy FAILS:** confirmed by removing one candidate row from\n130:   eval 1 — validator exits 1 with issues.\n131: \n132: ## Assumptions / follow-ups\n133: \n134: - **Assumption:** The committed owned files are the intended deliverable state.\n135:   They were produced and review-hardened in the prior epic-5 wave. This worker\n136:   did not re-derive them; re-running would produce byte-identical content and\n137:   no diff vs HEAD.\n138: - **Assumption (carried in the slice's own `assumptions` block, not invented\n139:   by this worker):** Microsoft product capability statements reflect public\n140:   documentation as of 2026-07-07; tenant gates, license SKUs, and DLP\n141:   classifications are pending tenant verification, not verified tenant facts.\n142:   Doug is the human approval owner per `tenant-decision-packet.json`.\n143: - **Follow-up (integrator, out of this story's scope):** wire\n144:   `platform-evaluation-slice-validate.ps1` into\n145:   `council-mvp-local-validate.ps1` — the hard rules explicitly forbid this\n146:   worker from editing the suite wiring file.\n147: - **Follow-up (later epic):** the deferred `com_councilplatformevaluation`\n148:   row persistence and the `CSP-LOCAL-001` implementation are receipt-gated to\n149:   a later epic; no implementation artifacts may be referenced until a separate\n150:   implementation receipt is recorded.\n\n(End of file - total 150 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Story 5.3 — Record Microsoft Platform Evaluation Evidence — Worker Notes\n\n## Outcome\n\nThe two ringer-owned deliverables were already present in the worktree HEAD\n(commit `068ce1b` \"epic 5: review-hardened validators for 5-1/5-2/5-3/5-5/5-6\")\nand are correct and hardened. No code edits were required; this worker verified\nthe state, exercised the corrupted-copy tripwire, and wrote this notes file.\n\n## Files I own (ringer-owned)\n\n- `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/platform-evaluation-slice.json`\n- `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/platform-evaluation-slice-validate.ps1`\n\nBoth files are committed in HEAD and pass validation with exit 0 +\n`PLATFORM_EVALUATION_SLICE_VALIDATE_OK`. There is no uncommitted diff to the\nowned files; `git diff --stat HEAD` is empty. The only new file is this\n`notes.md` (the output contract).\n\n## What I changed","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/doug/.ringer/work/bmad-hybrid/5-3-record-microsoft-platform-evaluation-evidence/notes.md","text":"# Story 5.3 — Record Microsoft Platform Evaluation Evidence — Worker Notes\n\n## Outcome\n\nThe two ringer-owned deliverables were already present in the worktree HEAD\n(commit `068ce1b` \"epic 5: review-hardened validators for 5-1/5-2/5-3/5-5/5-6\")\nand are correct and hardened. No code edits were required; this worker verified\nthe state, exercised the corrupted-copy tripwire, and wrote this notes file.\n\n## Files I own (ringer-owned)\n\n- `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/platform-evaluation-slice.json`\n- `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/platform-evaluation-slice-validate.ps1`\n\nBoth files are committed in HEAD and pass validation with exit 0 +\n`PLATFORM_EVALUATION_SLICE_VALIDATE_OK`. There is no uncommitted diff to the\nowned files; `git diff --stat HEAD` is empty. The only new file is this\n`notes.md` (the output contract).\n\n## What I changed\n\n- Nothing in the two owned files — they were already complete and committed by\n  the prior review-hardening wave (commits `ac56eb8`, `068ce1b`).\n- Verified the slice + validator satisfy every clause of the story spec (see\n  \"Verification\" below).\n- Verified a corrupted slice copy FAILS (removed one candidate row from\n  PE-LOCAL-EVAL-001; validator emitted\n  \"Evaluation PE-LOCAL-EVAL-001 must consider at least four Microsoft\n  candidates, found 3.\" plus downstream minted-id collision notes, and exited\n  1).\n- Wrote `notes.md` (this file).\n\n## What I read for conventions\n\n- `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/dataverse-mvp-schema-manifest.json` —\n  authoritative vocabulary. The slice's `com_decision` values (adopt/defer/\n  reject/custom_gap_build) come from `com_platformdecision`; receipt verbs\n  (proposed/reviewed) from `com_receiptverb`; actor types (human/system) from\n  `com_actortype`; results (accepted) from `com_receiptresult`. The\n  `com_councilplatformevaluation` table column set drives the row-completeness\n  union used by the validator.\n- `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/source-drift-supersession-slice.json`\n  and `...-slice-validate.ps1` (story 1-5) — the gold-standard slice + validator\n  pair. Mirrored patterns: story-keyed slice, declared `guards` with\n  `receiptsAreLocalContractEvidenceOnly: true`, no-live-write guards, wrapped\n  JSON loads (`Read-JsonInput`), `TryParse` numeric checks, strict booleans,\n  ISO 8601 timestamp checks, `$PSScriptRoot`-relative paths, issue list + exit\n  1, final `<NAME>_SLICE_VALIDATE_OK` token.\n- Sibling slices for cross-slice id checks: `manual-source-record-slice.json`,\n  `outlook-source-reference-slice.json`, `proposed-work-item-extraction-slice.json`,\n  `zero-multi-item-extraction-slice.json`, plus\n  `state-transition-demo-evidence.json`. The validator LIVE-harvests every\n  `*-slice.json` in `$PSScriptRoot` plus the demo evidence for minted-vs-referenced\n  id resolution.\n\n## Command that verifies it\n\n```\nexport DOTNET_ROOT=$HOME/.dotnet; export PATH=$HOME/.dotnet:$HOME/.dotnet/tools:$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH; pwsh -File _bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/platform-evaluation-slice-validate.ps1\n```\n\nExpected: prints `PLATFORM_EVALUATION_SLICE_VALIDATE_OK` and exits 0. Confirmed\nlocally. Corrupted-copy test (point `-PlatformSlicePath` at a temp copy with one\ncandidate row removed) correctly exits 1 with issues listed.\n\n## How the slice proves each story requirement\n\n### Slice must prove\n\n1. **Two capability evaluations, each with >=4 candidates from the named set,\n    each row capturing tenant gates, permission/DLP, licensing/cost, ALM path,\n    contract gaps, decision, review reference.**\n   - `platformEvaluationRun.evaluations` carries `PE-LOCAL-EVAL-001`\n     (memory-and-graph-grounding) with 4 rows (Work IQ, Dataverse\n     intelligence/MCP, Fabric IQ/Graph, Fabric data agents) and\n     `PE-LOCAL-EVAL-002` (workflow-automation) with 4 rows (Power Automate,\n     Copilot Studio, Power Apps MCP agent feed, Work IQ). All candidates are\n     members of the spec `candidateUniverse`. Each row carries all seven\n     story-mandated capture fields plus the manifest-required `com_name`,\n     `com_council_capability`, `com_microsoft_candidate`,\n     `com_official_source_date_checked`, `com_decision`.\n2. **One custom-service proposal citing a specific Microsoft-native gap / tenant\n    constraint, decision recorded as a receipt BEFORE implementation, no\n    implementation artifacts referenced.**\n   - `customServiceProposals[0]` = `CSP-LOCAL-001`, `addressesGapInRow` =\n     `PE-LOCAL-EVAL-001-ROW-02` (Dataverse intelligence/MCP, decision\n     `custom_gap_build`). `gapCitation` quotes the row's recorded\n     `com_contract_gaps`; `tenantConstraintCited` quotes\n     `tenant-decision-packet.json fabricIqGraphPhase2=defer_to_phase_2`.\n     `decisionReceipt` = `CR-LOCAL-PE-001` (verb `proposed`, append-only\n     locked). `implementationArtifactsReferenced` is empty; no\n     implementation-marker field appears anywhere in the slice (the validator\n     walks every property name).\n\n### Validator must assert (hardening bar)\n\n- **Candidate coverage (>=4 per evaluation, from the named set):** derived,\n  not counted — each row's `com_microsoft_candidate` must be a member of the\n  closed `specCandidateUniverse`, no candidate duplicated within an eval, and\n  `rows.Count -lt 4` trips.\n- **Row field completeness:** checked over the UNION of manifest-required PE\n  columns and the story-mandated capture set (so the manifest-optional fields\n  cannot be silently dropped).\n- **Custom proposal gap citation references a recorded gap in an evaluation\n  row:** `addressesGapInRow` must resolve to a minted row whose decision is\n  `custom_gap_build` AND whose `com_contract_gaps` is non-empty AND whose gap\n  text substantively overlaps the `gapCitation` (verbatim run or >=2\n  significant terms derived from the cited row, never hardcoded).\n- **Decision receipts complete and precede any implementation marker:**\n  manifest-required receipt fields + `com_before_state/com_after_state/\n  com_evidence_refs/com_decision_rationale/com_policy_flags` enforced; the\n  Microsoft-native-before-custom-substrate ordering is DERIVED from receipt\n  timestamps (every evaluation-review receipt timestamp <= every proposal\n  decision receipt timestamp), not from a self-asserted guard. No\n  implementation-marker field name may appear anywhere in the slice.\n- **Minted-vs-referenced ids:** `Collect-Ids` walks the parsed object graph\n  (not raw text) for CWI/CR/CSR; minted CR ids (this slice's receipts) must be\n  unique across ALL sibling slices + demo evidence; referenced CWI/CR/CSR ids\n  not minted here must resolve to a sibling or demo id. Within-slice uniqueness\n  enforced for `PE-LOCAL-*` and `CSP-LOCAL-*` namespaces at their minting\n  fields only.\n- **Cross-slice uniqueness:** LIVE `Get-ChildItem -Filter \"*-slice.json\"` in\n  `$PSScriptRoot` (excluding this slice) — no hardcoded sibling list, no\n  hardcoded-id binding rules. A missing-sibling-files tripwire prevents the\n  check silently no-op'ing.\n- **No conditional/skippable mandatory checks:** each collection-driven check\n  has a \"would silently no-op\" tripwire if the underlying collection is empty.\n- **Coverage derived not counted:** confirmed above.\n- **Corrupted slice copy FAILS:** confirmed by removing one candidate row from\n  eval 1 — validator exits 1 with issues.\n\n## Assumptions / follow-ups\n\n- **Assumption:** The committed owned files are the intended deliverable state.\n  They were produced and review-hardened in the prior epic-5 wave. This worker\n  did not re-derive them; re-running would produce byte-identical content and\n  no diff vs HEAD.\n- **Assumption (carried in the slice's own `assumptions` block, not invented\n  by this worker):** Microsoft product capability statements reflect public\n  documentation as of 2026-07-07; tenant gates, license SKUs, and DLP\n  classifications are pending tenant verification, not verified tenant facts.\n  Doug is the human approval owner per `tenant-decision-packet.json`.\n- **Follow-up (integrator, out of this story's scope):** wire\n  `platform-evaluation-slice-validate.ps1` into\n  `council-mvp-local-validate.ps1` — the hard rules explicitly forbid this\n  worker from editing the suite wiring file.\n- **Follow-up (later epic):** the deferred `com_councilplatformevaluation`\n  row persistence and the `CSP-LOCAL-001` implementation are receipt-gated to\n  a later epic; no implementation artifacts may be referenced until a separate\n  implementation receipt is recorded.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":150,"totalLines":150,"truncated":false}},"title":"notes.md","time":{"start":1784298704571,"end":1784298704583}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_f707d8bf80015z5Km24yd0i0qa","sessionID":"ses_08f914172ffeudlWP9EWlAXTjJ","messageID":"msg_f707d70d400182InIdyJQYvSjt"}}
