{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1784298753883,"sessionID":"ses_08f914172ffeudlWP9EWlAXTjJ","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-940d61753117bf49","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Story 5.3 — Record Microsoft Platform Evaluation Evidence — Worker Notes\n\n## Outcome\n\nFound and fixed a real validator proof-gap in the gap-citation substantive-\noverlap check. The committed slice JSON is correct and unchanged (byte-identical\nto HEAD); only `platform-evaluation-slice-validate.ps1` is edited (uncommitted).\nValidator still passes on the legitimate slice; a corrupted slice now FAILS where\nit previously passed.\n\n## Files I own (ringer-owned)\n\n- `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/platform-evaluation-slice.json` —\n  unchanged (byte-identical to HEAD; no diff).\n- `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/platform-evaluation-slice-validate.ps1`\n  — edited: 38 insertions / 14 deletions in the custom-proposal gap-citation\n  check (lines ~458-512).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe gap-citation \"substantive overlap\" check (validator, custom-proposal loop)\npreviously fell back to **counting >= 2 isolated \"significant terms\"** shared\nbetween `gapCitation` and the cited row's `com_contract_gaps`. That fallback is\nsatisfied by generic vocabulary that recurs across many rows (`contract`,\n`semantics`, `receipt`, `projection`), so a citation that cites row\n`PE-LOCAL-EVAL-001-ROW-02` (Dataverse MCP) by id but **describes a different\nrow's gap** (Power Automate content) still passed. This violates the story\nrequirement that the citation reference *a recorded gap in an evaluation row*,\nand matches the review kill-list anti-pattern \"self-asserted/counted proof\nstanding in for a real tie.\"\n\nReplacement (derived, not counted):\n\n1. Both the cited row's `com_contract_gaps` and the proposal `gapCitation` are\n   normalized identically — lowercased, runs of non-`[a-z0-9_/-]` collapsed to a\n   single space — so the comparison is content-driven and survives punctuation /\n   casing reflows.\n2. The check derives whether any **verbatim contiguous run of >= 3 word-tokens**\n   drawn from the cited row's own gap text appears in the citation.\n3. Containment is **token-boundary-aware**: a delimited blob (`|tok|tok|tok|`)\n   is used, where the `|` delimiter never appears inside a normalized token, so a\n   delimited phrase can only match whole tokens — never a prefix of one (e.g.\n   `semantic` must NOT match inside `semantics`). This closed a second bug found\n   while fixing the first: a naive substring `.IndexOf` matched\n   `contract and semantic` inside `contract and semantics`.\n4. Removed the hardcoded English stopword list and the isolated-term count; the\n   cited row's gap text supplies the candidate phrases, never this slice's own\n   vocabulary.\n\nThe existing legitimate `gapCitation` (CSP-LOCAL-001) contains a long verbatim\nrun from the cited row's gap text, so it still passes under the stricter rule.\n\n## What I read for conventions\n\n- `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/dataverse-mvp-schema-manifest.json` —\n  authoritative vocabulary. `com_platformdecision` = adopt/defer/reject/\n  custom_gap_build/not_tested; `com_receiptverb` includes proposed/reviewed;\n  `com_actortype` includes human; `com_receiptresult` includes accepted. The\n  `com_councilplatformevaluation` table's required columns\n  (`com_name`, `com_council_capability`, `com_microsoft_candidate`,\n  `com_official_source_date_checked`, `com_decision`) plus the story-mandated\n  capture set drive the row-completeness union.\n- `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/source-drift-supersession-slice-validate.ps1`\n  (story 1-5) — the gold-standard validator. Mirrored patterns: story-keyed\n  slice, declared `guards` incl. `receiptsAreLocalContractEvidenceOnly: true`,\n  no-live-write guards, wrapped JSON loads (`Read-JsonInput`), `TryParse`\n  numeric checks, strict booleans, ISO 8601 timestamp checks with explicit UTC\n  offset, `$PSScriptRoot`-relative paths, issue list + `exit 1`, final\n  `<NAME>_SLICE_VALIDATE_OK` token. The gap-citation check style was matched to\n  this validator's \"derive a real tie, never count coincidental tokens\" bar.\n- Sibling slices for cross-slice id checks: `manual-source-record-slice.json`,\n  `outlook-source-reference-slice.json`, `proposed-work-item-extraction-slice.json`,\n  `zero-multi-item-extraction-slice.json`, plus\n  `state-transition-demo-evidence.json`. The validator LIVE-harvests every\n  `*-slice.json` in `$PSScriptRoot` plus the demo evidence for minted-vs-\n  referenced id resolution.\n\n## Command that verifies it\n\n```\nexport DOTNET_ROOT=$HOME/.dotnet; export PATH=$HOME/.dotnet:$HOME/.dotnet/tools:$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH; pwsh -File _bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/platform-evaluation-slice-validate.ps1\n```\n\nExpected: prints `PLATFORM_EVALUATION_SLICE_VALIDATE_OK` and exits 0. Confirmed\nlocally (Evaluations: 2, Candidate rows: 8, Custom proposals: 1, Receipts: 3).\n\n## How the fix was verified (corrupted-copy tripwires)\n\nEach corruption was applied to a temp copy of the slice, the validator run, then\nthe slice restored from backup. Expected vs. actual:\n\n- baseline (unmodified): PASS (legitimate citation contains a long verbatim run\n  from the cited row).\n- T5 — cite the cited row id but describe a DIFFERENT row's gap (Power\n  Automate content): now FAIL (previously PASSED — the hole).\n- T5b — citation uses only generic isolated terms (`contract`, `semantics`) with\n  the `semantic`/`semantics` prefix trap: now FAIL (token-boundary-aware match\n  prevents the prefix false-hit).\n- T5c — citation contains a genuine verbatim 3-token run from the cited row:\n  PASS (sanity — real citations still pass).\n- T8 — paraphrase-only citation with no contiguous run: FAIL.\n- T1 — proposal decision receipt timestamp before evaluation-review receipts:\n  FAIL (Microsoft-native-before-custom ordering derived from timestamps).\n- T2 — strip evaluation-review receipt evidence_refs: FAIL (no-op tripwire).\n- T3 — add `deployedService` implementation-marker field: FAIL.\n- T4 — bogus `com_decision` value: FAIL (manifest vocabulary).\n- T6 — duplicate minted `PE-LOCAL-EVAL-001`: FAIL (within-slice uniqueness).\n- T7 — candidate outside the named universe: FAIL.\n\nNo regressions: every previously-failing corruption still fails.\n\n## Assumptions / follow-ups\n\n- **Assumption:** The committed slice JSON (`platform-evaluation-slice.json`) is\n  correct as committed in HEAD (commits `ac56eb8`, `068ce1b`); this worker made\n  no edits to it. Only the validator needed hardening.\n- **Assumption (carried in the slice's own `assumptions` block, not invented by\n  this worker):** Microsoft product capability statements reflect public\n  documentation as of 2026-07-07; tenant gates, license SKUs, and DLP\n  classifications are pending tenant verification, not verified tenant facts.\n  Doug is the human approval owner per `tenant-decision-packet.json`.\n- **Follow-up (integrator, out of this story's scope):** wire\n  `platform-evaluation-slice-validate.ps1` into\n  `council-mvp-local-validate.ps1` — the hard rules explicitly forbid this\n  worker from editing the suite wiring file.\n- **Follow-up (later epic):** the deferred `com_councilplatformevaluation`\n  row persistence and the `CSP-LOCAL-001` implementation are receipt-gated to\n  a later epic; no implementation artifacts may be referenced until a separate\n  implementation receipt is recorded.\n","filePath":"/home/doug/.ringer/work/bmad-hybrid/5-3-record-microsoft-platform-evaluation-evidence/notes.md"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/home/doug/.ringer/work/bmad-hybrid/5-3-record-microsoft-platform-evaluation-evidence/notes.md","exists":true,"truncated":false},"title":"notes.md","time":{"start":1784298753861,"end":1784298753879}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoni